window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v5-index"]=[{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p11-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"inner","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 1  the soliloquy volume cold open  sudou s first person soliloquy alone with his backstory  no other character appears  and p 12 carries no prose   to be completely honest  i ain t really a capable person  his mother abandoned the family to go into the nightclub business  his father toiled as a janitor with a permanently hunched back  and the sight of it sickened him   being the idiot i am  i decided to give up on studyin  and go into sports    he chose getting stronger over studying and frames it as his own idea  not a defeat  solo sports first   tennis and pingpong  good but never top tier   then basketball  despite not being a team player he got seriously into it  kept improving  and was recommended to a high school with one of the best basketball teams in the entire country  the pulled recommendation defines his self read   that was when i really understood the painful truth  i was trash  born from trash  chose this school for what it promised   that was why i chose this school    free  and able to guarantee even his future  blank short scan page  running footer only  no prose to cite","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p11-1\">Ch.1: the soliloquy<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.11–12<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volume cold open: Sudou’s first-person soliloquy alone with his backstory; no other character appears, and p.12 carries no prose.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “To be completely honest, I ain’t really a capable person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> His mother abandoned the family to go into the nightclub business; his father toiled as a janitor with a permanently hunched back, and the sight of it sickened him.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Being the idiot I am, I decided to give up on studyin’ and go into sports.” — he chose getting stronger over studying and frames it as his own idea, not a defeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Solo sports first — tennis and pingpong, good but never top-tier — then basketball: despite not being a team player he got seriously into it, kept improving, and was recommended to a high school with one of the best basketball teams in the entire country.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The pulled recommendation defines his self-read: “That was when I really understood the painful truth: I was trash, born from trash.”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Chose this school for what it promised: “That was why I chose this school.” — free, and able to guarantee even his future.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank/short scan page: running footer only; no prose to cite.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p16-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  the zodiac debrief at pallet back table of the crowded cafe pallet after summer vacation  ayanokoji sits with hirata  karuizawa and horikita  reviewing the cruise ship zodiac exam and its hidden vips  the rabbit group read alphabetically   ayanokouji kun  ichinose san  ibuki san  karuizawa san   made him the rabbit vip  the dragon group s fifth name was kushida san   i honestly don t have a clue    lied to the group when horikita asked what he thought  notices karuizawa has started calling hirata yousuke kun  he meets her gaze and she diverts her eyes  plays along as the cooperative nobody while hirata works to cement the four person group  exchanges the no presence   long shadows banter with her  she is not joking when she takes the bait  names sudou among the athletic students the festival is built to give their first real opening","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1\">Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–15<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back table of the crowded café Pallet after summer vacation: Ayanokōji sits with Hirata, Karuizawa and Horikita, reviewing the cruise-ship zodiac exam and its hidden VIPs.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I honestly don’t have a clue” — lied to the group when Horikita asked what he thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The rabbit group read alphabetically — Ayanokouji-kun, Ichinose-san, Ibuki-san, Karuizawa-san — made him the rabbit VIP; the dragon group’s fifth name was Kushida-san.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Notices Karuizawa has started calling Hirata Yousuke-kun; he meets her gaze and she diverts her eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Plays along as the cooperative nobody while Hirata works to cement the four-person group.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Exchanges the no-presence / long-shadows banter with her; she is not joking when she takes the bait.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Names Sudou among the athletic students the festival is built to give their first real opening.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the rules and the huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  the zodiac debrief at pallet at pallet he keeps the two girls  friction down   his presence makes the discomfort between karuizawa and horikita mysteriously disappear   i think ryuuen kun figured it all out in the middle of the test   if he understood the rules  he should have discovered all the vips   i m glad we re discussing this  horikita san and ayanokouji kun   i actually have a proposal   first  to bring our class together  i d like to rope in kushida san as an ally  proposes her as the fourth ally to unite the boys   starting with ike kun and yamauchi kun   over horikita s refusal  his proposal is rejected  she side eyes ayanokoji instead of softening","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p13-1\">Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–15<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Pallet he keeps the two girls’ friction down — his presence makes the discomfort between Karuizawa and Horikita mysteriously disappear.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I think Ryuuen-kun figured it all out in the middle of the test,”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “If he understood the rules, he should have discovered all the VIPs,”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I’m glad we’re discussing this, Horikita-san and Ayanokouji-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I actually have a proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First, to bring our class together, I’d like to rope in Kushida-san as an ally.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Proposes her as the fourth ally to unite the boys — starting with Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun — over Horikita’s refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> His proposal is rejected; she side-eyes Ayanokōji instead of softening.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p16-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  the zodiac debrief at pallet at pallet with hirata  karuizawa and ayanokoji  she walks the rabbit group through the alphabetical vip rule and the cruise ship exam s logic   if you put the names of the students in the rabbit group in alphabetical order  it would be ayanokouji kun  ichinose san  ibuki san  and then karuizawa san  confirms karuizawa s dragon group deduction   kushida fifth   and explains why the pattern was hard to see mid exam   though it appears that ryuuen kun rules class c alone  perhaps that isn t actually true   a rebellious student must ve tossed out the wrong answer in direct defiance of ryuuen kun   that said  you evaded ryuuen kun s clutches quite well    aims it at karuizawa   unnecessary    refuses hirata s proposal to rope kushida in   i won t deny the fact that she has certain skills  but we can do anything she can on our own   those who claim that they have no presence usually cast long shadows   do you take me for a fool    stung by ayanokoji s no presence bait  not joking","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1\">Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–15<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Pallet with Hirata, Karuizawa and Ayanokōji, she walks the rabbit group through the alphabetical VIP rule and the cruise-ship exam’s logic.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “If you put the names of the students in the rabbit group in alphabetical order, it would be Ayanokouji-kun, Ichinose-san, Ibuki-san, and then Karuizawa-san,”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Though it appears that Ryuuen-kun rules Class C alone, perhaps that isn’t actually true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “A rebellious student must’ve tossed out the wrong answer in direct defiance of Ryuuen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Confirms Karuizawa’s dragon-group deduction — Kushida fifth — and explains why the pattern was hard to see mid-exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That said, you evaded Ryuuen-kun’s clutches quite well.” — aims it at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unnecessary,” — refuses Hirata’s proposal to rope Kushida in.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t deny the fact that she has certain skills, but we can do anything she can on our own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those who claim that they have no presence usually cast long shadows,”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you take me for a fool?” — stung by Ayanokōji’s no-presence bait; not joking.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing and the huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 2  passing mention named in the alphabetical rabbit group roster karuizawa recites   third  between ichinose san and karuizawa san  her place in the roster is the exhibit for the zodiac vip rule","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the alphabetical rabbit-group roster Karuizawa recites — third, between Ichinose-san and Karuizawa-san.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her place in the roster is the exhibit for the zodiac VIP rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the rivalry heat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 2  the zodiac debrief at pallet at pallet she works through the rabbit group s alphabetical vip order and lands on her own role in the cruise ship exam   that s why i was chosen as vip   but isn t that really  really simple    on the dragon group s fifth name giveaway for kushida  sits with her at pallet   the two girls are completely incompatible at first glance  but hirata s presence erases the discomfort  has started calling him yousuke kun  hugs his arm  and asks him to confirm her poker face   ayanokoji notices the shift   i do have a surprisingly good poker face  keeps her eyes on him after the others lose interest  he meets her gaze and she diverts hers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p13-1\">Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–15<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Pallet she works through the rabbit group’s alphabetical VIP order and lands on her own role in the cruise-ship exam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “That’s why I was chosen as VIP”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “But isn’t that really, really simple?” — on the dragon group’s fifth-name giveaway for Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I do have a surprisingly good poker face.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sits with her at Pallet — the two girls are completely incompatible at first glance, but Hirata’s presence erases the discomfort.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Has started calling him Yousuke-kun, hugs his arm, and asks him to confirm her poker face — Ayanokōji notices the shift.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Keeps her eyes on him after the others lose interest; he meets her gaze and she diverts hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p28-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the Class C exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke sakayanagi-arisu kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  passing mentions named in the zodiac recap as the dragon group s fifth name and therefore its vip  again at p 15 as hirata s proposed ally and at p 30 as a beauty benchmark  her name is the exhibit for the alphabetical vip rule horikita walks through  hirata wants her roped in to unite the boys  horikita refuses  sakayanagi is called  as cute as kushida and sakura  in narration","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p13-1\">Ch.2: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13, 15, 30<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the zodiac recap as the dragon group’s fifth name and therefore its VIP; again at p.15 as Hirata’s proposed ally and at p.30 as a beauty benchmark.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her name is the exhibit for the alphabetical VIP rule Horikita walks through.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata wants her roped in to unite the boys; Horikita refuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Sakayanagi is called “as cute as Kushida and Sakura” in narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Asked for the middle ground<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"sports festival ch 2  2 1  the rules briefing chabashira s two hour homeroom hands out the printed sports festival rules  september to early october becomes heavy physical education  classes a and d form the red team  classes b and c the white team  across all grade levels  class d competes alongside class a  individual events score 15 12 10 8  fifth place loses one point and each place below loses one more  a team competition win is worth 500  recommended participant events score 50 30 15 10  fifth loses two points and each place below loses two more  the 1200 metre relay pays three times those values  after combined class scores are reviewed  100 class points are deducted from the first  second  and third year batches of the two classes on the losing team  chabashira adds that points move class by class  not just by team  even a red team win can still hit class d with the 100 point penalty if it holds the lowest combined overall score  grade ranking is separate  50 class points to each grade s first place class  no change for second  50 deducted for third  100 for fourth  an individual winner chooses 5000 private points or three written test points  second chooses 3000 or two  third chooses 1000 or one  test points taken this way cannot be given to another student  the lowest scorer in an individual competition loses 1000 private points  or one written test point if they hold fewer than 1000  overall mvp takes 100 000 private points  each grade s top three scorers take 10 000 private points apiece  the ten lowest scoring students in each year lose ten points on their next written exam  thirteen events in order  100 metre dash  hurdle race  capture the flag  boys  ball toss  girls  tug of war by sex  obstacle course race  three legged race  cavalry battle  200 metre dash  then scavenger hunt  four way tug of war  mixed three legged race  and the mixed grade 1200 metre relay  the participation table must be a class consensus  the window opens one week before the festival and closes at 5 00 pm the day before  a missed window means random assignment  falling below the minimum for an all participant event means disqualification  a recommended event substitute can be bought for 100 000 private points per competition  her absence and health questions draw out the substitute price and the student decides health policy  delivers the whole briefing in a detached  matter of fact manner and lets out one slight laugh at ike s question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html#sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the rules briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html\">Sports Festival<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira’s two-hour homeroom hands out the printed sports festival rules; September to early October becomes heavy physical education.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Classes A and D form the Red Team, Classes B and C the White Team, across all grade levels; Class D competes alongside Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Individual events score 15/12/10/8; fifth place loses one point and each place below loses one more; a team-competition win is worth 500.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Recommended-participant events score 50/30/15/10; fifth loses two points and each place below loses two more; the 1200-metre relay pays three times those values.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> After combined class scores are reviewed, 100 class points are deducted from the first-, second- and third-year batches of the two classes on the losing team.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira adds that points move class-by-class, not just by team: even a Red Team win can still hit Class D with the 100-point penalty if it holds the lowest combined overall score.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Grade ranking is separate: 50 class points to each grade’s first-place class, no change for second, 50 deducted for third, 100 for fourth.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> An individual winner chooses 5000 private points or three written-test points, second chooses 3000 or two, third chooses 1000 or one; test points taken this way cannot be given to another student.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The lowest scorer in an individual competition loses 1000 private points, or one written-test point if they hold fewer than 1000.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Overall MVP takes 100,000 private points; each grade’s top three scorers take 10,000 private points apiece.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The ten lowest-scoring students in each year lose ten points on their next written exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Thirteen events in order: 100-metre dash, hurdle race, capture the flag (boys), ball toss (girls), tug-of-war by sex, obstacle course race, three-legged race, cavalry battle, 200-metre dash; then scavenger hunt, four-way tug-of-war, mixed three-legged race, and the mixed-grade 1200-metre relay.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The participation table must be a class consensus; the window opens one week before the festival and closes at 5:00 pm the day before; a missed window means random assignment.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Falling below the minimum for an all-participant event means disqualification; a recommended-event substitute can be bought for 100,000 private points per competition.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her absence and health questions draw out the substitute price and the student-decides health policy.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Delivers the whole briefing in a detached, matter-of-fact manner and lets out one slight laugh at Ike’s question.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  2 1  the rules and the huddle afternoon homeroom becomes a two hour session  chabashira announces the september sports festival and its handout  the class erupts  teases her about finally having an opportunity to get in touch with her brother on the red team  she glares and tells him to drop it   at least you have an opportunity to get in touch now  huh  watches the huddle from the side   ike and yamauchi push for personal chances against the class s interest  yamauchi is present at the huddle  no line of his is tagged in the translation   it s a sad fact of reality    answering horikita s complaint that only guys like these come to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the rules and the huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Afternoon homeroom becomes a two-hour session: Chabashira announces the September sports festival and its handout; the class erupts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “At least you have an opportunity to get in touch now, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s a sad fact of reality,” — answering Horikita’s complaint that only guys like these come to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Teases her about finally having an opportunity to get in touch with her brother on the Red Team; she glares and tells him to drop it.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Watches the huddle from the side — Ike and Yamauchi push for personal chances against the class’s interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi is present at the huddle; no line of his is tagged in the translation.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the Red Team assembly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  2 1  the sports festival briefing afternoon homeroom runs two hours  she distributes the festival handout and weekly schedules in a detached  matter of fact manner   however  from september to the beginning of october  we will be holding more physical education classes to prepare for the school sports festival   in any case  this event will massively impact each and every class    answers hirata s special exam question vaguely  explains the red white split   class d and class a ride the red team together   you in class d are assigned to the red team   their reward will be not having any points deducted    the cruel  brief answer to the winning team question   in the sports festival  you can earn test points as a prize  which you can then apply to a written exam    lets out a slight laugh  an unusual sight  reads out the ten lowest penalty  for first years  ten points off the next written exam   should you fall short of the minimum required number of people for competitions for all participants  you will be deemed unable to continue and disqualified   a substitute requires 100 000 private points per competition   next period s location will move to gymnasium 1  where you ll meet with students from other classes and grade levels","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the sports festival briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Afternoon homeroom runs two hours: she distributes the festival handout and weekly schedules in a detached, matter-of-fact manner.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “However, from September to the beginning of October, we will be holding more physical education classes to prepare for the school sports festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “In any case, this event will massively impact each and every class.” — answers Hirata’s special-exam question vaguely.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “You in Class D are assigned to the Red Team.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Explains the Red/White split — Class D and Class A ride the Red Team together.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Their reward will be not having any points deducted.” — the cruel, brief answer to the winning-team question.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the sports festival, you can earn test points as a prize, which you can then apply to a written exam.” — lets out a slight laugh, an unusual sight.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Reads out the ten-lowest penalty: for first-years, ten points off the next written exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Should you fall short of the minimum required number of people for competitions for all participants, you will be deemed unable to continue and disqualified,”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A substitute requires 100,000 private points per competition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Next period’s location will move to Gymnasium 1, where you’ll meet with students from other classes and grade levels.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the gate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 1  the briefing in homeroom he is the first to ask whether the festival is another special exam  chabashira s answer stays vague   sensei  is this festival another of the special exams   um  sensei  how many points does the winning team get    chabashira answers  none   wait  so  we can decide the order in which we ll participate    on the participation table  the absence questions in the room are his and horikita s   both read the handout like exam material","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom he is the first to ask whether the festival is another special exam; Chabashira’s answer stays vague.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Sensei, is this festival another of the special exams?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Um, sensei, how many points does the winning team get?” — Chabashira answers: none.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Wait. So, we can decide the order in which we’ll participate?” — on the participation table.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The absence questions in the room are his and Horikita’s — both read the handout like exam material.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 1  the briefing and the huddle in homeroom she spots the testing method on the handout before most of the class and calls ayanokoji over  at the mention that class a   her brother s year   rides the same red team  she mutters at ayanokoji to drop it   don t talk about that here  after hirata s practical questions she raises her own  what happens on the day if someone is absent from a group competition   well  how many points are needed to assign a substitute  sudou  ike and yamauchi corner her in the free homeroom period to argue the festival strategy   why do only guys like these come to me   that s not a valid opinion    shuts down ike s fun and win line at once   within our class  you stand out as someone with superior athletic skill    concedes sudou s claim on the recommended events   stamina isn t an unlimited resource    her counter to entering sudou in everything   we re not coming to any decisions right now    ends the huddle without a decision","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing and the huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom she spots the testing method on the handout before most of the class and calls Ayanokōji over. Sudou, Ike and Yamauchi corner her in the free homeroom period to argue the festival strategy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Don’t talk about that here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Well, how many points are needed to assign a substitute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Why do only guys like these come to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> At the mention that Class A — her brother’s year — rides the same Red Team, she mutters at Ayanokōji to drop it.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Hirata’s practical questions she raises her own: what happens on the day if someone is absent from a group competition?<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not a valid opinion.” — shuts down Ike’s fun-and-win line at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Within our class, you stand out as someone with superior athletic skill.” — concedes Sudou’s claim on the recommended events.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stamina isn’t an unlimited resource.” — her counter to entering Sudou in everything.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re not coming to any decisions right now.” — ends the huddle without a decision.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly and the coin<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 2  2 1  the huddle named as one of the athletic students fired up by the sports festival   probably the first exam that lets him contribute meaningfully  his athletic ability is the class s read on him before the events are even set  pulls ike and yamauchi to her and opens the strategy huddle   let s figure this out  horikita   class d can win this   if i do that  we ll win    claims every recommended participant event  tells ike flatly that the recommended events belong to people who are good at sports   you re not  kanji  pushes back on her stamina caution   even tired  he moves better than the unathletic guys   and leaves without a decision   but it s better to leave it to me than put forward someone unathletic  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16, 23–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the athletic students fired up by the sports festival — probably the first exam that lets him contribute meaningfully.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Let’s figure this out, Horikita,”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Class D can win this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “If I do that, we’ll win,” — claims every recommended-participant event.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His athletic ability is the class’s read on him before the events are even set.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pulls Ike and Yamauchi to her and opens the strategy huddle.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Tells Ike flatly that the recommended events belong to people who are good at sports.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re not, Kanji,”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pushes back on her stamina caution — even tired, he moves better than the unathletic guys — and leaves without a decision.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But it’s better to leave it to me than put forward someone unathletic, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.1: the soliloquy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: The ability camp, then the grip-strength king<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p17-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki sakayanagi-arisu ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 2  the briefing and the huddle shouts at the red white announcement  then joins sudou and yamauchi in crowding horikita for strategy   whoa  seriously  we re really doing that   yeah  yeah  let s think of a way to win   i d like to have fun and win    smacked down by horikita at once   hey  you don t know that for sure    miracles happen  and it should be fair  takes sudou s  you re not  kanji  without an answer  frustrated but silent by the end of the huddle  the pair are dissatisfied together  the translation never tags which boy speaks the  we want a chance  lines  whispers  hey  check out that girl  pointing at the class a girl with the cane   he s smitten like the rest   hey  check out that girl","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p17-1\">Ch.2: the briefing and the huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.17, 23–27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shouts at the Red/White announcement, then joins Sudou and Yamauchi in crowding Horikita for strategy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Whoa! Seriously?! We’re really doing that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Yeah, yeah, let’s think of a way to win!”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “I’d like to have fun and win!” — smacked down by Horikita at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you don’t know that for sure!” — miracles happen, and it should be fair.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Takes Sudou’s “You’re not, Kanji,” without an answer; frustrated but silent by the end of the huddle.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The pair are dissatisfied together; the translation never tags which boy speaks the “we want a chance” lines.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Whispers “Hey, check out that girl,” pointing at the Class A girl with the cane — he’s smitten like the rest.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, check out that girl,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Grip strength and the scavenger hunt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v5-p17-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 2  the sports festival s point economy chabashira s handout prices the school sports festival in private points  test points and class points at once  individual competition placement pays 15 12 10 8 points on the class scoreboard  fifth place loses one point  and each place below loses one more  recommended participant events pay 50 30 15 10  fifth place loses two points  each place below loses two more  the relay pays three times those values  the winning team of a team competition takes 500 points  after combined class scores are reviewed  100 class points are deducted from the first  second  and third year batches of the two classes on the losing team  chabashira adds that points move class by class  not just by team  grade ranking is separate  50 class points to each grade s first place class  no change for second  50 deducted for third  100 for fourth  first place in an individual competition chooses 5000 private points or three written test points  second chooses 3000 or two  third chooses 1000 or one   test points accepted this way cannot be given to another student  the lowest scorer in an individual competition loses 1000 private points  or one written test point if they have fewer than 1000  overall mvp  100 000 private points  each grade s top three scorers  10 000 private points apiece  the ten lowest scoring students in each year lose ten points on their next written exam   for first years the penalty is a written exam deduction  a substitute for a recommended participant event costs 100 000 private points per competition","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v5-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v5-p17-1\">Ch.2: the sports festival’s point economy<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.17–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira’s handout prices the school sports festival in private points, test points and class points at once.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Individual competition placement pays 15/12/10/8 points on the class scoreboard; fifth place loses one point, and each place below loses one more.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Recommended-participant events pay 50/30/15/10; fifth place loses two points, each place below loses two more; the relay pays three times those values; the winning team of a team competition takes 500 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> After combined class scores are reviewed, 100 class points are deducted from the first-, second- and third-year batches of the two classes on the losing team; Chabashira adds that points move class-by-class, not just by team.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Grade ranking is separate: 50 class points to each grade’s first-place class, no change for second, 50 deducted for third, 100 for fourth.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> First place in an individual competition chooses 5000 private points or three written-test points; second chooses 3000 or two; third chooses 1000 or one — test points accepted this way cannot be given to another student.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The lowest scorer in an individual competition loses 1000 private points, or one written-test point if they have fewer than 1000.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Overall MVP: 100,000 private points; each grade’s top three scorers: 10,000 private points apiece.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The ten lowest-scoring students in each year lose ten points on their next written exam — for first-years the penalty is a written-exam deduction.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> A substitute for a recommended-participant event costs 100,000 private points per competition.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Class D’s festival point compromise<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p23-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2  2 1  the huddle gathers with sudou and ike around horikita the moment free homeroom starts  the pair voice the demand for a personal shot at points  only ike s lines are tagged by the translation  sudou s recommended events claim brushes them off  he and ike appear frustrated but say nothing  the  we want a chance  speeches sit untagged between horikita and sudou   the translation does not say whether ike or yamauchi speaks them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p23-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the huddle<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.23–25<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gathers with Sudou and Ike around Horikita the moment free homeroom starts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The pair voice the demand for a personal shot at points; only Ike’s lines are tagged by the translation.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou’s recommended-events claim brushes them off; he and Ike appear frustrated but say nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The “we want a chance” speeches sit untagged between Horikita and Sudou — the translation does not say whether Ike or Yamauchi speaks them.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: On the losing end of the demo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"fujimaki katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami","q":"sports festival ch 2  2 2  the assembly gymnasium 1  four hundred strong  fujimaki briefs the red team  first year class a assembles under katsuragi  class c walks out  sakayanagi is introduced  and the class a class d pact is struck  only the final event   the 1200 metre relay   brings all classes from all grade levels together  every other event is divided by grade level  third year class a takes red team command in place of the student council president  class a and class d agree to keep out of each other s way  no shared competition details  only a meeting to come for the group events  ryuuen refuses class b s cooperation talk and walks class c out   the white team s first year halves open the festival estranged  ichinose confronts the walkout to his face and gets gratitude for the trouble saved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html#sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html\">Sports Festival<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gymnasium 1, four hundred strong: Fujimaki briefs the Red Team, first-year Class A assembles under Katsuragi, Class C walks out, Sakayanagi is introduced, and the Class A–Class D pact is struck.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#fujimaki\">Fujimaki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Only the final event — the 1200-metre relay — brings all classes from all grade levels together; every other event is divided by grade level.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> Third-year Class A takes Red Team command in place of the student council president.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Class A and Class D agree to keep out of each other’s way: no shared competition details, only a meeting to come for the group events.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryuuen refuses Class B’s cooperation talk and walks Class C out — the White Team’s first-year halves open the festival estranged.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Ichinose confronts the walkout to his face and gets gratitude for the trouble saved.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the rules briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Four-way tug-of-war and the luck events<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  2 2  the red team assembly over four hundred people gather in gymnasium 1  fujimaki takes red team command  first year class a assembles under katsuragi  ryuuen walks class c out  sakayanagi arisu is introduced  and ayanokoji and horikita argue strategy in the corner  notes that the student council president does not take red team command and wonders when he will make a move  takes the class a class d pact at face value   no shared competition details  only a promise not to get in each other s way  reads the gym s layout  a clear line between katsuragi s followers and nearly all the students sitting with sakayanagi  reconsiders which faction is superior  cites her as the kind who might put feelings aside for victory if ryuuen and class b reconcile  warns horikita that ryuuen likely already has one or more tactics in mind for the festival   the school has never once called the festival a  special exam   i think the sports festival is supposed to do the same with our physical abilities   you re looking for loopholes   you re not thinking big enough    his read on horikita s tunnel vision   we need to make sure that we re prepared  that s all there is to it   there s a good chance that he has a plan in place   we have to think like that to rise to class a s level  has studied ryuuen s strategies and thought processes ever since the fight that nearly got sudou expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the Red Team assembly<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Over four hundred people gather in Gymnasium 1: Fujimaki takes Red Team command, first-year Class A assembles under Katsuragi, Ryuuen walks Class C out, Sakayanagi Arisu is introduced, and Ayanokōji and Horikita argue strategy in the corner.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “The school has never once called the festival a ‘special exam.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I think the sports festival is supposed to do the same with our physical abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You’re looking for loopholes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Notes that the student council president does not take Red Team command and wonders when he will make a move.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Takes the Class A–Class D pact at face value — no shared competition details, only a promise not to get in each other’s way.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reads the gym’s layout: a clear line between Katsuragi’s followers and nearly all the students sitting with Sakayanagi; reconsiders which faction is superior.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Cites her as the kind who might put feelings aside for victory if Ryuuen and Class B reconcile.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Warns Horikita that Ryuuen likely already has one or more tactics in mind for the festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re not thinking big enough,” — his read on Horikita’s tunnel vision.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need to make sure that we’re prepared. That’s all there is to it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a good chance that he has a plan in place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have to think like that to rise to Class A’s level,”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has studied Ryuuen’s strategies and thought processes ever since the fight that nearly got Sudou expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the rules and the huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the gate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-fujimaki-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu fujimaki","q":"fujimaki ch 2  2 2  red team command steps forward in the crowded gymnasium 1 among instructors and students and takes command of the red team for the sports festival   i m fujimaki  from the third year class a  announced as the student who will assume command of red team   the student council president does not take it   however  each and every one of them is a crucial battle in which you stake your survival at this school    his warning that future exams wear games  clothes   the only competition which all classes from all grade levels will participate in together is the final event the 1200 meter relay race  releases the first years to gather and discuss strategies by grade level  starting immediately  takes the command the student council president declined  ayanokoji notes the absence and wonders when he will move  no first name is printed anywhere in the chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-fujimaki-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: Red Team command<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#fujimaki\">Fujimaki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Steps forward in the crowded Gymnasium 1 among instructors and students and takes command of the Red Team for the sports festival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> “I’m Fujimaki, from the third-year Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> “However, each and every one of them is a crucial battle in which you stake your survival at this school,” — his warning that future exams wear games’ clothes.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> “The only competition which all classes from all grade levels will participate in together is the final event—the 1200-meter relay race.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Announced as the student who will assume command of Red Team — the student council president does not take it.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Releases the first-years to gather and discuss strategies by grade level, starting immediately.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Takes the command the student council president declined; Ayanokōji notes the absence and wonders when he will move.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No first name is printed anywhere in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-fujimaki-y1v5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the opening speech<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2  2 2  the assembly meets katsuragi at the red team assembly and becomes class d s negotiating face   i look forward to working with you  accepts the keep out of each other s way pact   no shared competition details   and thanks him with  i m counting on you   it s pretty hard to trust other people in this school  katsuragi kun   so  you won t share any details about the competitions you re participating in  reassures her when she apologizes for being consistently absent   you have nothing to apologize for  looks to the rest of the class for the pact s final decision  no one objects","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Katsuragi at the Red Team assembly and becomes Class D’s negotiating face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I look forward to working with you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It’s pretty hard to trust other people in this school, Katsuragi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “So, you won’t share any details about the competitions you’re participating in?”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Accepts the keep-out-of-each-other’s-way pact — no shared competition details — and thanks him with “I’m counting on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reassures her when she apologizes for being consistently absent.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have nothing to apologize for.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Looks to the rest of the class for the pact’s final decision; no one objects.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Runs the homeroom, the vote and the roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune fujimaki horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 2  passing mention named as the third year class a student and student council president suzune is scanning for  he does not take red team command  she has never sought him out first   he always initiates contact   and cannot find him in the four hundred strong crowd  fujimaki s command of the red team makes ayanokoji wonder when the president will make a move","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the third-year Class A student and student council president Suzune is scanning for; he does not take Red Team command.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#fujimaki\">Fujimaki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She has never sought him out first — he always initiates contact — and cannot find him in the four-hundred-strong crowd.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Fujimaki<\/b> Fujimaki’s command of the Red Team makes Ayanokōji wonder when the president will make a move.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: The brother, revealed to the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 2  the assembly and the coin in gymnasium 1 she scans restlessly for her brother  he never takes red team command  and fujimaki does instead  has never gone to meet him first   he always initiates contact   and cannot spot him in the crowd of four hundred  gets his warning about ryuuen and answers with a pointed question about personal experience  he leaves it at  i ve warned you  pulls him into the strategy question   what factor besides athleticism decides the festival   and gets  mere luck  for her trouble   i m not talking about random chance  though    wants a definite method  not luck  carries shame over her island mistakes  the narration reads her as even more obsessed with victory   different  i think it s the same kind of special exam    against ayanokoji s distinction   i definitely want class d to win    retort when he says she wants loopholes  not preparation   so  you re saying that we need to fight clean and fight hard to win   wait  are you saying that classes b and c are working together behind the scenes   but if that s true  it s crazy    can t believe ryuuen could have a plan already   fine  do enlighten me    swallows the rudeness and asks to be set straight  defends her b and c reading against his push  she thinks a behind the scenes deal is unlikely  suggests ichinose might set aside her feelings and cooperate with ryuuen for victory   ayanokoji calls the view too small","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly and the coin<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–34<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In Gymnasium 1 she scans restlessly for her brother; he never takes Red Team command, and Fujimaki does instead.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m not talking about random chance, though,” — wants a definite method, not luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Different? I think it’s the same kind of special exam.” — against Ayanokōji’s distinction.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I definitely want Class D to win,” — retort when he says she wants loopholes, not preparation.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Has never gone to meet him first — he always initiates contact — and cannot spot him in the crowd of four hundred.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Gets his warning about Ryuuen and answers with a pointed question about personal experience; he leaves it at “I’ve warned you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Pulls him into the strategy question — what factor besides athleticism decides the festival — and gets “Mere luck?” for her trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Carries shame over her island mistakes; the narration reads her as even more obsessed with victory.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’re saying that we need to fight clean and fight hard to win?”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Are you saying that Classes B and C are working together behind the scenes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if that’s true, it’s crazy.” — can’t believe Ryuuen could have a plan already.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine, do enlighten me.” — swallows the rudeness and asks to be set straight.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Defends her B-and-C reading against his push; she thinks a behind-the-scenes deal is unlikely.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Suggests Ichinose might set aside her feelings and cooperate with Ryuuen for victory — Ayanokōji calls the view too small.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing and the huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Her plan wins the vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 2  2 2  the class a face assembles the first year class a students in droves after fujimaki s speech and becomes the class s negotiating face at the red team meeting   i hope we can join forces without any problems  strikes the keep out of each other s way pact with hirata   no shared competition details  only a meeting to come for the group events   i was thinking that it d be best if we just keep out of each other s way   letting that information slip might lead to unnecessary conflict down the road   i ll consult with everyone else  warns horikita off him  he ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant   and leaves his own experience unspoken   don t underestimate ryuuen   i ve warned you  introduces sakayanagi by name and asks for sensitivity  watches her quietly while nearly all the class sits with her faction   that s sakayanagi arisu  yahiko is named among the few boys and girls sitting on his side of the line  the narration reads his faction as possibly no longer superior   sakayanagi may be demonstrating her power deliberately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the Class A face<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Assembles the first-year Class A students in droves after Fujimaki’s speech and becomes the class’s negotiating face at the Red Team meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I hope we can join forces without any problems,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I was thinking that it’d be best if we just keep out of each other’s way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Letting that information slip might lead to unnecessary conflict down the road.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Strikes the keep-out-of-each-other’s-way pact with Hirata — no shared competition details, only a meeting to come for the group events.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll consult with everyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Warns Horikita off him: he’ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant — and leaves his own experience unspoken.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t underestimate Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve warned you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Introduces Sakayanagi by name and asks for sensitivity; watches her quietly while nearly all the class sits with her faction.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s Sakayanagi Arisu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Yahiko is named among the few boys and girls sitting on his side of the line.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The narration reads his faction as possibly no longer superior — Sakayanagi may be demonstrating her power deliberately.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The standing Class A meetings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p27-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 2  2 2  confronting the walkout interrupts katsuragi s briefing as almost her entire class s counterpart walks out   she questions ryuuen to his face   so  you don t intend to hold a discussion   i see  so  you re just saving us the hassle  then   you really think you can win without cooperating  gets gratitude for the trouble saved and his sneer as an answer  class c leaves anyway  ayanokoji later names her as the kind who might set feelings aside and cooperate with ryuuen for victory","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: confronting the walkout<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.27<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Interrupts Katsuragi’s briefing as almost her entire class’s counterpart walks out — she questions Ryuuen to his face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “So, you don’t intend to hold a discussion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I see. So, you’re just saving us the hassle, then,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “You really think you can win without cooperating?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Gets gratitude for the trouble saved and his sneer as an answer; Class C leaves anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ayanokōji later names her as the kind who might set feelings aside and cooperate with Ryuuen for victory.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami manabe-shiho katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  2 2  the walkout when ichinose asks why class c won t discuss strategy  he turns with his hands in his pockets and leads the whole class out of the gym   it s a waste of time   you should be grateful   hmm  i wonder    to ichinose s challenge on winning without cooperating  refuses her cooperation talk to her face  the exit confirms class c s dictatorship  manabe follows him out after the glance back at karuizawa  katsuragi s warning to horikita is keyed to him  he ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant  ayanokoji s read  always looking to win  possibly already holding one or more festival tactics behind the b and c refusal  the walkout confirms his hold on class c inside the volume s first pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the walkout<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.27–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">When Ichinose asks why Class C won’t discuss strategy, he turns with his hands in his pockets and leads the whole class out of the gym.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “It’s a waste of time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You should be grateful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Hmm, I wonder.” — to Ichinose’s challenge on winning without cooperating.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Refuses her cooperation talk to her face; the exit confirms Class C’s dictatorship.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Manabe follows him out after the glance-back at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi’s warning to Horikita is keyed to him: he’ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ayanokōji’s read: always looking to win, possibly already holding one or more festival tactics behind the B-and-C refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The walkout confirms his hold on Class C inside the volume’s first pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The reconnaissance that isn’t<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p28-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 2  2 2  the class c exit as class c files out of the gym  her expression sours for an instant at manabe s glance  manabe looks back at her from ryuuen s wake   the cruise ship scrap and bullying history   then averts her eyes and follows the class out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p28-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the Class C exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As Class C files out of the gym, her expression sours for an instant at Manabe’s glance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Manabe looks back at her from Ryuuen’s wake — the cruise-ship scrap and bullying history — then averts her eyes and follows the class out.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: The other camp, then the entrance meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v5-p28-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho","q":"manabe shiho ch 2  passing mention as class c leaves the gym  manabe looks back at karuizawa for a moment  averts her eyes  and follows ryuuen out  the glance reopens the cruise ship scrap where karuizawa s bullying history surfaced","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-manabe-shiho-y1v5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html#sc-manabe-shiho-y1v5-p28-1\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As Class C leaves the gym, Manabe looks back at Karuizawa for a moment, averts her eyes, and follows Ryuuen out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The glance reopens the cruise-ship scrap where Karuizawa’s bullying history surfaced.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p28-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke sakayanagi-arisu","q":"sakayanagi arisu ch 2  2 2  the introduction first full appearance  the petite girl alone with a thin cane  introduced by katsuragi as disabled   class a s other rumored leader   unfortunately  i won t be very useful in this competition   your kindness overwhelms me    to the class d boys who rush to reassure her  the class s line is clear between his followers and hers  nearly all the students sit with her   perhaps a deliberate demonstration  hirata reassures her when she apologizes for being consistently absent  short silver hair  pale skin  a dreamlike quality that makes people instinctively want to protect her   and a strength of will behind the weakness  did not participate in the island or cruise ship tests  whether a penalty was incurred is left open by the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p28-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: the introduction<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.28–31<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First full appearance: the petite girl alone with a thin cane, introduced by Katsuragi as disabled — Class A’s other rumored leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “Unfortunately, I won’t be very useful in this competition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “Your kindness overwhelms me,” — to the Class D boys who rush to reassure her.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The class’s line is clear between his followers and hers; nearly all the students sit with her — perhaps a deliberate demonstration.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata reassures her when she apologizes for being consistently absent.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Short silver hair, pale skin, a dreamlike quality that makes people instinctively want to protect her — and a strength of will behind the weakness.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Did not participate in the island or cruise ship tests; whether a penalty was incurred is left open by the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Rumored from a distance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p30-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2  passing mention named in the narration comparing sakayanagi s looks to kushida and her  one of the two girls sakayanagi is measured against when class d s boys size her up","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p30-1\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.30<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the narration comparing Sakayanagi’s looks to Kushida and her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> One of the two girls Sakayanagi is measured against when Class D’s boys size her up.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Follows Sudou’s hand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p30-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko","q":"totsuka yahiko ch 2  passing mention named among the boys sitting with katsuragi s faction in the class a split  one of the few class a students counted on katsuragi s side of the line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p30-1\">Ch.2: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.30<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named among the boys sitting with Katsuragi’s faction in the Class A split.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> One of the few Class A students counted on Katsuragi’s side of the line.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p107-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: shouting for Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  2 3  the gate after class he stays behind alone with a file on his phone   whatever it showed  he decides no traps are necessary   then runs into chabashira spraying water at the main gate   are you on duty today   don t you think that s an exaggeration   no  nothing like that    to chabashira s guess that he already has an eccentric strategy in place   i m free to decide my own path  she warns that if he shows no results soon she ll stop covering for him  the confrontation was only a matter of time  blank short scan page inside the dialogue  footer and watermark only  p 38 is likewise a blank scan","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the gate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.35–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After class he stays behind alone with a file on his phone — whatever it showed, he decides no traps are necessary — then runs into Chabashira spraying water at the main gate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Are you on duty today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Don’t you think that’s an exaggeration?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “No, nothing like that,” — to Chabashira’s guess that he already has an eccentric strategy in place.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m free to decide my own path.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She warns that if he shows no results soon she’ll stop covering for him; the confrontation was only a matter of time.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank/short scan page inside the dialogue (footer and watermark only); p.38 is likewise a blank scan.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the Red Team assembly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: The blackboard vote, the betrayal warning, the roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2  2 3  the gate spraying water at the main gate after school  she s on duty and clocks that he stayed behind later than usual   you stayed behind longer than usual  ayanokouji   are you prepared for the sports festival   in your case  i would have thought that you d already have some eccentric idea or strategy in place   but if you don t show me some results soon  i ll stop covering for you  their talk stops when their eyes meet   public discussion helps no one  she accepts his right to choose his path but puts a deadline on her cover  blank short scan page sits inside the dialogue  footer and watermark only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the gate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.35–37<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spraying water at the main gate after school; she’s on duty and clocks that he stayed behind later than usual.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “You stayed behind longer than usual, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Are you prepared for the sports festival?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “In your case, I would have thought that you’d already have some eccentric idea or strategy in place,”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if you don’t show me some results soon, I’ll stop covering for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Their talk stops when their eyes meet — public discussion helps no one; she accepts his right to choose his path but puts a deadline on her cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank/short scan page sits inside the dialogue (footer and watermark only).<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the sports festival briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3: Watches the homeroom from the back<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"","q":"sports festival ch 3  3  four way tug of war and the luck events the four way tug of war takes four people from each of the four classes   sixteen in all   who pull simultaneously  so tactics matter beyond raw strength  luck based events such as the scavenger hunt are staffed by rock paper scissors among the volunteers  on hirata s call   simple is best  how about we go with rock paper scissors  class d s roster fills only about a third of the all participant spots at the first pass  the rest stay open for later practice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html#sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Four-way tug-of-war and the luck events<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html\">Sports Festival<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The four-way tug-of-war takes four people from each of the four classes — sixteen in all — who pull simultaneously, so tactics matter beyond raw strength.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Luck-based events such as the scavenger hunt are staffed by rock-paper-scissors among the volunteers, on Hirata’s call: “Simple is best. How about we go with rock-paper-scissors?”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Scope<\/span> Class D’s roster fills only about a third of the all-participant spots at the first pass; the rest stay open for later practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the festival runs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  3  the blackboard vote  the betrayal warning  the roster class 1 d homeroom  hirata chalks two systems for the sports festival while ayanokoji narrates the class s first real strategy meeting of the volume   we began making comprehensive preparations for the sports festival  which was only one month away  lets horikita s jab about his phone pass  then stays out of the debate   well  if i just leave it to you and hirata  you ll sort out our problems  right   relax  it s my policy to abstain from voting   the other students aren t all as ambitious as you    he votes for no one while the class splits 16 13  after class he texts karuizawa    no matter what  object to horikita s plan  then ask kushida for her opinion    and meets her at the main entrance   when it comes to improvising  you re quite fast on your feet   besides  i m under no compunction to answer your questions   i m not personally interested in reaching class a  tells karuizawa   one of our classmates will betray us during this sports festival   yes  i ve prepared   now then  i wonder what class a has in mind    katsuragi will be solid  and sakayanagi would be good for the white team and for class d  life jacket parable  in a crisis the able bodied are favored  so  just because sakayanagi wasn t physically active didn t mean she was harmless   karuizawa was better at reading people than i d imagined  probably because of her past  measures 60 6 kilograms of grip strength on the first try   second in the class behind sudou s 82 4  with koenji set aside   having aimed carefully at the average  stops the meter just over 60 once he has worked out that 60 is roughly the average he was aiming for   i see  so  60 was high  then  wins the first round and the second and final round of rock paper scissors despite praying to lose  and is picked for the scavenger hunt team against his wishes  admits the roster problem    many participants were chosen against their will    and horikita answers that the class s athletic gap is to blame","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: The blackboard vote, the betrayal warning, the roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D homeroom: Hirata chalks two systems for the sports festival while Ayanokōji narrates the class’s first real strategy meeting of the volume.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Relax. It’s my policy to abstain from voting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “The other students aren’t all as ambitious as you,” — he votes for no one while the class splits 16–13.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “When it comes to improvising, you’re quite fast on your feet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “We began making comprehensive preparations for the sports festival, which was only one month away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lets Horikita’s jab about his phone pass, then stays out of the debate: “Well, if I just leave it to you and Hirata, you’ll sort out our problems, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After class he texts Karuizawa — “No matter what, object to Horikita’s plan. Then ask Kushida for her opinion.” — and meets her at the main entrance.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, I’m under no compunction to answer your questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not personally interested in reaching Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Unverified<\/span> Tells Karuizawa: “One of our classmates will betray us during this sports festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’ve prepared.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Now then, I wonder what Class A has in mind?” — Katsuragi will be solid, and Sakayanagi would be good for the White Team and for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Life-jacket parable: in a crisis the able-bodied are favored, so “just because Sakayanagi wasn’t physically active didn’t mean she was harmless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Karuizawa was better at reading people than I’d imagined, probably because of her past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Measures 60.6 kilograms of grip strength on the first try — second in the class behind Sudou’s 82.4, with Kōenji set aside — having aimed carefully at the average.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Stops the meter just over 60 once he has worked out that 60 is roughly the average he was aiming for.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I see. So, 60 was high, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Wins the first round and the second and final round of rock-paper-scissors despite praying to lose, and is picked for the scavenger-hunt team against his wishes.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Admits the roster problem — “Many participants were chosen against their will,” — and Horikita answers that the class’s athletic gap is to blame.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the gate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The Ryuuen read, the partner lesson, the two problems<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3  3  watches the homeroom from the back chabashira moves to the back of the classroom during hirata s two hour homeroom and does not speak   she intends to watch the class run itself  lets hirata run the session unopposed   she speaks no word during the whole strategy meeting  the chapter prints nothing further about her  her last stated posture is watching from the back  p 39","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Watches the homeroom from the back<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira moves to the back of the classroom during Hirata’s two-hour homeroom and does not speak — she intends to watch the class run itself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Lets Hirata run the session unopposed — she speaks no word during the whole strategy meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter prints nothing further about her; her last stated posture is watching from the back (p.39).<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p35-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the gate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the report she cannot prove<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei kouenji-rokusuke sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  3  runs the homeroom  the vote and the roster hirata takes the two hour homeroom in hand while chabashira watches from the back  chalks two systems on the board  and walks the class through them   this is a rough outline  but i think that everything boils down to these two approaches   the strength of the raising hands system is  naturally  that everyone gets to voice their wishes  calls the majority vote when the two camps can t agree   if we can t agree  then we ve got to have a majority vote   calm down  both of you  karuizawa accepts the vote mechanism at once    if yousuke kun says so  then i agree   how about we decide which plan we prefer by a show of hands   sixteen votes  then  defuses sudou s confrontation with koenji   kouenji kun must have his reasons   i think that it would be best to take our time with the rest  opens the grip strength testing    how about we measure the grip strength of our dominant hand    and records the results for the tug of war orders  sets the four way tug of war order by grip strength  sudou  ayanokoji  miyake and himself  explains the four way tug of war after looking it up    it s a tug of war competition in which four people are chosen from each of the four classes  for a total of sixteen people   how about we go with rock paper scissors  names the scavenger hunt five    ayanokouji kun  yukimura kun  sotomura kun  mori san  and maezono san    then fills every roster   this information is top secret  so everyone  please only make note of your events and your partners","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Runs the homeroom, the vote and the roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata takes the two-hour homeroom in hand while Chabashira watches from the back, chalks two systems on the board, and walks the class through them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “This is a rough outline, but I think that everything boils down to these two approaches.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “The strength of the raising-hands system is, naturally, that everyone gets to voice their wishes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Calm down, both of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls the majority vote when the two camps can’t agree: “If we can’t agree, then we’ve got to have a majority vote.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Karuizawa accepts the vote mechanism at once — “If Yousuke-kun says so, then I agree.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about we decide which plan we prefer by a show of hands?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sixteen votes, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Defuses Sudou’s confrontation with Kōenji: “Kouenji-kun must have his reasons.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think that it would be best to take our time with the rest.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens the grip-strength testing — “How about we measure the grip strength of our dominant hand?” — and records the results for the tug-of-war orders.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Sets the four-way tug-of-war order by grip strength: Sudou, Ayanokōji, Miyake and himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Explains the four-way tug-of-war after looking it up — “It’s a tug-of-war competition in which four people are chosen from each of the four classes, for a total of sixteen people.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about we go with rock-paper-scissors?”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the scavenger-hunt five — “Ayanokouji-kun, Yukimura-kun, Sotomura-kun, Mori-san, and Maezono-san.” — then fills every roster.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This information is top secret, so everyone, please only make note of your events and your partners.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Gentle methods, three-legged partner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke hondou-ryoutaro","q":"hondo ryotaro ch 3  3  grip strength testing hirata hands hondou one of the two grip strength devices to run the measurement line  stands at hirata s right as a device holder  alongside yukimura  before sudou snatches the other one","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hondou-ryoutaro-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: Grip-strength testing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hondou-ryoutaro\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata hands Hondou one of the two grip-strength devices to run the measurement line.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Stands at Hirata’s right as a device holder, alongside Yukimura, before Sudou snatches the other one.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki sudou-ken karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3  her plan wins the vote horikita cuts into hirata s homeroom with a supplementary proposal while sudou is claiming every recommended event   however  that single tactic isn t guaranteed to carry us to victory   put simply  the strongest  fastest students should be grouped together  tells shinohara her feelings don t matter   it s for the sake of the class  tells her   besides  you probably wouldn t win anything anyway   i don t want to hear your excuses anymore  her compromise  top placers who don t need test points share private points with the bottom    the entire class will share in the gains and losses of private points from the festival  grumbled at karuizawa s side of the room   the other class definitely isn t weighed down by morons like you  closes her appeal   i hope you ll all make the right decision  asks ayanokoji to silence karuizawa    ayanokouji kun  can t you tell karuizawa san to shut up    and gets a refusal  accuses him   you ve been talking to her lately  though  turns on him   don t tell me you agree with karuizawa san s plan  growls back   in that case  you could just have voted for my plan  defends her plan   giving the class the best possible chance of winning will ultimately result in netting a lot of private points  her plan takes sixteen of the twenty nine votes cast  karuizawa s takes thirteen    then it s decided  she says  and hands the rest to hirata  volunteers herself   i will also compete in as many events as possible  notes his mood after the roster is filled    you look more somber than usual    and blames the class s athletic gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Her plan wins the vote<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita cuts into Hirata’s homeroom with a supplementary proposal while Sudou is claiming every recommended event.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “However, that single tactic isn’t guaranteed to carry us to victory,”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Put simply, the strongest, fastest students should be grouped together,”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I don’t want to hear your excuses anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Tells Shinohara her feelings don’t matter: “It’s for the sake of the class,”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Tells her: “Besides, you probably wouldn’t win anything anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Her compromise: top placers who don’t need test points share private points with the bottom — “The entire class will share in the gains and losses of private points from the festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Grumbled at Karuizawa’s side of the room: “The other class definitely isn’t weighed down by morons like you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Closes her appeal: “I hope you’ll all make the right decision,”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks Ayanokōji to silence Karuizawa — “Ayanokouji-kun, can’t you tell Karuizawa-san to shut up?” — and gets a refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accuses him: “You’ve been talking to her lately, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Turns on him: “Don’t tell me you agree with Karuizawa-san’s plan?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Growls back: “In that case, you could just have voted for my plan,”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Defends her plan: “Giving the class the best-possible chance of winning will ultimately result in netting a lot of private points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Result<\/span> Her plan takes sixteen of the twenty-nine votes cast; Karuizawa’s takes thirteen — “Then it’s decided,” she says, and hands the rest to Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Volunteers herself: “I will also compete in as many events as possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes his mood after the roster is filled — “You look more somber than usual.” — and blames the class’s athletic gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly and the coin<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The name bet and the partner problem<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sotomura-hideo ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 3  3  grip strength and the scavenger hunt ike takes his turn at the grip strength meter and pleads for bonus points on his score   i got a 42 6  begs hirata to round 42 6 up to 50    can you give me a few tiny bonus points and make it 50  asks whether the luck events are closed   hey  hirata  are we not getting any more chances to enter events  asks hirata   so  how are we going to decide that    when hirata says the scavenger hunt is decided by luck   i m so jealous    after ayanokoji s group is picked for the scavenger hunt","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Grip strength and the scavenger hunt<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike takes his turn at the grip-strength meter and pleads for bonus points on his score.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “I got a 42.6.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Begs Hirata to round 42.6 up to 50 — “Can you give me a few tiny bonus points and make it 50?”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Asks whether the luck events are closed: “Hey, Hirata, are we not getting any more chances to enter events?”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Asks Hirata: “So, how are we going to decide that?” — when Hirata says the scavenger hunt is decided by luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “I’m so jealous!” — after Ayanokōji’s group is picked for the scavenger hunt.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the briefing and the huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The watching classes and the tug demo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 3  3  the other camp  then the entrance meeting karuizawa raises the unathletic students  objection in homeroom and  after class  waits at the main entrance for ayanokoji   hey  excuse me  i object to this  too   hey  what do you think  kushida san   we re still losing out on chances to win the big prize  horikita answers her   you re objecting just because she objected  that s completely illogical  insists on fairness   we have to make these competitions fair  then yields to hirata s vote  her plan takes thirteen votes against horikita s sixteen   the minority side of the class s first festival vote  shows him the text    no matter what  object to horikita s plan  then ask kushida for her opinion    and demands to know what he is playing at   so  i should just do as i m told  like a loyal dog  and never ask why  hears the betrayal prediction    wait  what  are you being serious right now  asks for reassurance   even if someone does betray the class  we ll be okay  right  her reading of people is praised in his thoughts after she leaves   better than he imagined  from her past","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: The other camp, then the entrance meeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Karuizawa raises the unathletic students’ objection in homeroom and, after class, waits at the main entrance for Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hey, excuse me? I object to this, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Hey, what do you think, Kushida-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “We’re still losing out on chances to win the big prize.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita answers her: “You’re objecting just because she objected? That’s completely illogical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Insists on fairness: “We have to make these competitions fair,” then yields to Hirata’s vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Result<\/span> Her plan takes thirteen votes against Horikita’s sixteen — the minority side of the class’s first festival vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Shows him the text — “No matter what, object to Horikita’s plan. Then ask Kushida for her opinion.” — and demands to know what he is playing at.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, I should just do as I’m told, like a loyal dog, and never ask why.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Hears the betrayal prediction — “Wait, what?! Are you being serious right now?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks for reassurance: “even if someone does betray the class, we’ll be okay. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her reading of people is praised in his thoughts after she leaves — better than he imagined, from her past.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the Class C exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Named in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  3  refuses to cooperate sudou confronts koenji over his abstention in the homeroom vote  koenji refuses to join the festival plan   i have no interest in this   i have no reason to let you bully me into anything  hirata ends the standoff    kouenji kun must have his reasons  ignores sudou s taunts at the meter    i ll pass  ignore me    polishing his fingernails instead  refuses the grip strength meter when sudou challenges him  ayanokoji later writes  kouenji aside  i ended up placing second in the class  so koenji ranked above without a printed figure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Refuses to cooperate<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou confronts Kōenji over his abstention in the homeroom vote; Kōenji refuses to join the festival plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I have no interest in this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I have no reason to let you bully me into anything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata ends the standoff — “Kouenji-kun must have his reasons.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Ignores Sudou’s taunts at the meter — “I’ll pass. Ignore me.” — polishing his fingernails instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Refuses the grip-strength meter when Sudou challenges him; Ayanokōji later writes “Kouenji aside, I ended up placing second in the class,” so Kōenji ranked above without a printed figure.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  3  asked for the middle ground karuizawa calls on kushida during the homeroom debate  and kushida voices the class s wish for a solution both sides can accept   if there were some kind of middle ground solution  that would be ideal   a strategy we could all get behind  names both camps fairly   horikita s wish for the class and shinohara s wish for everyone to have a chance   before horikita offers the compromise  volunteers for recommended events once horikita s plan carries the vote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Asked for the middle ground<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Karuizawa calls on Kushida during the homeroom debate, and Kushida voices the class’s wish for a solution both sides can accept.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “If there were some kind of middle-ground solution, that would be ideal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “A strategy we could all get behind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Names both camps fairly — Horikita’s wish for the class and Shinohara’s wish for everyone to have a chance — before Horikita offers the compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Volunteers for recommended events once Horikita’s plan carries the vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Names Sudou the leader; named the second problem<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-maezono-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke maezono","q":"maezono ch 3  3  on the scavenger hunt roster maezono is named by hirata as one of the five picked for the scavenger hunt after the rock paper scissors  picked into the group    ayanokouji kun  yukimura kun  sotomura kun  mori san  and maezono san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-maezono-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: On the scavenger-hunt roster<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#maezono\">Maezono<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Maezono is named by Hirata as one of the five picked for the scavenger hunt after the rock-paper-scissors.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Picked into the group — “Ayanokouji-kun, Yukimura-kun, Sotomura-kun, Mori-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito ch 3  3  grip strength and the tug of war order miyake is named in the four way tug of war order that hirata sets by grip strength  takes the third tug of war slot behind sudou and ayanokoji   sudou kun  ayanokouji kun  miyake kun  and me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: Grip strength and the tug-of-war order<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#miyake-akito\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Miyake is named in the four-way tug-of-war order that Hirata sets by grip strength.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes the third tug-of-war slot behind Sudou and Ayanokōji: “Sudou-kun, Ayanokouji-kun, Miyake-kun, and me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y1v5-p123-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: left-side horse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyamoto-soshi-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"miyamoto-soshi","q":"miyamoto soshi ch 3  3  grip strength and the tug of war order miyamoto s grip strength is recorded at 48 kilograms during the boys  testing  measures 48 kilograms  between hirata s 57 9 and ike s 42 6  not among the four named for the four way tug of war   hirata s order is sudou  ayanokoji  miyake and himself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyamoto-soshi-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: Grip strength and the tug-of-war order<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#miyamoto-soshi\">Miyamoto Soshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Miyamoto’s grip strength is recorded at 48 kilograms during the boys’ testing.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Measures 48 kilograms, between Hirata’s 57.9 and Ike’s 42.6.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Not among the four named for the four-way tug-of-war — Hirata’s order is Sudou, Ayanokōji, Miyake and himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mori-nene-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke mori-nene","q":"mori nene ch 3  3  on the scavenger hunt roster mori is named by hirata as one of the five picked for the scavenger hunt after the rock paper scissors  picked into the group    ayanokouji kun  yukimura kun  sotomura kun  mori san  and maezono san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mori-nene-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: On the scavenger-hunt roster<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#mori-nene\">Mori Nene<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mori is named by Hirata as one of the five picked for the scavenger hunt after the rock-paper-scissors.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Picked into the group — “Ayanokouji-kun, Yukimura-kun, Sotomura-kun, Mori-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mori-nene-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the weak general<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-onodera-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"onodera","q":"onodera ch 3  3  volunteers for the recommended events onodera is named with kushida among the students who volunteer for recommended competitions after horikita s plan carries the vote  offers herself for the recommended participant events once the class resolves to win as a class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-onodera-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: Volunteers for the recommended events<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#onodera\">Onodera<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Onodera is named with Kushida among the students who volunteer for recommended competitions after Horikita’s plan carries the vote.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Offers herself for the recommended-participant events once the class resolves to win as a class.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-onodera-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Three-legged partner for Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"sudou-ken sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  3  follows sudou s hand sakura raises her hand with sudou and yukimura for horikita s ability plan during the homeroom vote  votes with the ability camp   one of the sixteen hands for horikita s plan  follows sudou s declared choice into the same camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Follows Sudou’s hand<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakura raises her hand with Sudou and Yukimura for Horikita’s ability plan during the homeroom vote.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Votes with the ability camp — one of the sixteen hands for Horikita’s plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Follows Sudou’s declared choice into the same camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Last place, then the worst pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken shinohara-satsuki","q":"shinohara satsuki ch 3  3  objects to the ability plan shinohara is the first student to object when sudou claims the recommended events  and she argues her case against horikita for two pages   won t that leave slower people high and dry   i don t want to throw away my shot   i don t want to lose out on private points   not everyone is as smart as you  horikita san  horikita answers that she should study longer and  probably wouldn t win anything anyway  sudou shuts her down    if we lose because of you  will you take responsibility    and the class sides with the ability plan","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Objects to the ability plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shinohara is the first student to object when Sudou claims the recommended events, and she argues her case against Horikita for two pages.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Won’t that leave slower people high and dry?”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “I don’t want to throw away my shot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “I don’t want to lose out on private points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Not everyone is as smart as you, Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita answers that she should study longer and “probably wouldn’t win anything anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou shuts her down — “If we lose because of you, will you take responsibility?” — and the class sides with the ability plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ike-kanji sotomura-hideo","q":"sotomura hideo ch 3  3  the professor s bad luck sotomura    the professor    is called up for the grip strength test alongside sudou  then loses the rock paper scissors for the scavenger hunt  hirata pairs him with sudou for simultaneous measurements   well then  let s have sotomura kun stand next to you and take his measurement simultaneously  sudou kun  posts 42 kilograms of grip strength  the class s lowest printed score  wails when picked for the scavenger hunt    i i have been chosen to participate in the scavenger hunt   why  oh why did i throw rock at that moment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: The Professor’s bad luck<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sotomura — “the Professor” — is called up for the grip-strength test alongside Sudou, then loses the rock-paper-scissors for the scavenger hunt.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Why, oh why did I throw rock at that moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata pairs him with Sudou for simultaneous measurements: “Well then, let’s have Sotomura-kun stand next to you and take his measurement simultaneously, Sudou-kun”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Posts 42 kilograms of grip strength, the class’s lowest printed score.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Wails when picked for the scavenger hunt — “I-I have been chosen to participate in the scavenger hunt?”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 3  3  the ability camp  then the grip strength king sudou argues the ability side of hirata s blackboard and  by p 40  has claimed every recommended competition for himself   if i win  then it s more likely our class wins   i ll do all the events for recommended participants  turns his new leadership on shinohara    if we lose because of you  will you take responsibility  huh  votes horikita   when winners win  we all win  claims every recommended competition and warns the class    i ll participate in every competition  confronts koenji for abstaining   hey  kouenji  ain t you gonna cooperate  posts 82 4 kilograms of grip strength   the highest printed score   and bellows through the test   this is what a real man looks like   it s just  cause i train all the time  taunts koenji for refusing the meter   what  you scared of losing to me or something   maybe  like  around 60    his guess at the average  which ayanokoji uses to stop his own meter at 60 6  despairs at the class s depth   man  i can t rely on a single one of you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: The ability camp, then the grip-strength king<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou argues the ability side of Hirata’s blackboard and, by p.40, has claimed every recommended competition for himself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “If I win, then it’s more likely our class wins.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “I’ll do all the events for recommended participants,”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “It’s just ’cause I train all the time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Turns his new leadership on Shinohara — “If we lose because of you, will you take responsibility? Huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Votes Horikita: “When winners win, we all win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Claims every recommended competition and warns the class — “I’ll participate in every competition.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Confronts Kōenji for abstaining: “Hey, Kouenji. Ain’t you gonna cooperate?”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Posts 82.4 kilograms of grip strength — the highest printed score — and bellows through the test: “This is what a real man looks like.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Taunts Kōenji for refusing the meter: “What? You scared of losing to me or something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe, like, around 60?” — his guess at the average, which Ayanokōji uses to stop his own meter at 60.6.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Despairs at the class’s depth: “Man, I can’t rely on a single one of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The name bet and the leader’s first week<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"hirata-yousuke hondou-ryoutaro ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  3  hands  votes and the roster yukimura is named among the students who follow sudou into horikita s camp  and he later handles the grip strength device and makes the scavenger hunt roster  raises his hand with sudou and sakura for horikita s ability plan  takes his turn at the grip strength meter after sudou s 82 4  is handed a grip strength device by hirata  alongside hondou  picked with ayanokoji  sotomura  mori and maezono for the scavenger hunt   ayanokouji kun  yukimura kun  sotomura kun  mori san  and maezono san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Hands, votes and the roster<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura is named among the students who follow Sudou into Horikita’s camp, and he later handles the grip-strength device and makes the scavenger-hunt roster.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hondou-ryoutaro\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Raises his hand with Sudou and Sakura for Horikita’s ability plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes his turn at the grip-strength meter after Sudou’s 82.4.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> Is handed a grip-strength device by Hirata, alongside Hondou.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Picked with Ayanokōji, Sotomura, Mori and Maezono for the scavenger hunt: “Ayanokouji-kun, Yukimura-kun, Sotomura-kun, Mori-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: seventh and seventh<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 3  3  class d s festival point compromise horikita s compromise  carried by the class vote  top placers who don t need test score boosts spend their private points lifting the bottom placers  test scores  and the whole class shares the festival s gains and losses in private points  the narrator notes the cost   chances of victory drop across the board  and the bottom ten students per grade would still be in trouble","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v5-p39-1\">Ch.3 §3: Class D’s festival point compromise<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Horikita’s compromise, carried by the class vote: top placers who don’t need test-score boosts spend their private points lifting the bottom placers’ test scores, and the whole class shares the festival’s gains and losses in private points.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Effect<\/span> The narrator notes the cost — chances of victory drop across the board, and the bottom ten students per grade would still be in trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v5-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the sports festival’s point economy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  4  the ryuuen read  the partner lesson  the two problems first independent practice on the athletic grounds  class a and b watch from the windows  class c does not  and ayanokoji and horikita talk strategy at the edge of the field  reads the missing reconnaissance as the tell   he s making it obvious by not bothering to do any reconnaissance   normally  when someone has a secret plan in place  they do whatever it takes to ensure that their enemies don t figure it out  lets her pin him down on his pe record    nope  i m not confident    after she calls his scores average   i m sorry to disappoint  but what you see is what you get   would i do something so pointless    when she asks if he is holding back like he did on tests   you ll learn the answer to that soon enough  pairs with hirata for three legged practice after horikita s partnership with onodera collapses  finds the rhythm quickly   hirata s praise makes the awkward drill feel simple  invites himself as her three legged partner   partner with me for the three legged race  outpaces her on purpose  then gives the lesson   this wasn t about fast or slow   the important thing is to work with your partner  names his two problems for the class  horikita  who cannot keep a partner  and kushida  whose rooftop darkness and hatred of horikita must be confronted   therefore  the only way to resolve the issue was to have them confront one another  the praise after sakura s last place finish    you really gave it your all    carries no speaker tag  sakura s reply addresses ayanokouji kun  so it is recorded here rather than assigned outright","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The Ryuuen read, the partner lesson, the two problems<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First independent practice on the athletic grounds: Class A and B watch from the windows, Class C does not, and Ayanokōji and Horikita talk strategy at the edge of the field.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Normally, when someone has a secret plan in place, they do whatever it takes to ensure that their enemies don’t figure it out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reads the missing reconnaissance as the tell: “He’s making it obvious by not bothering to do any reconnaissance,”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Lets her pin him down on his PE record — “Nope, I’m not confident.” — after she calls his scores average.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m sorry to disappoint, but what you see is what you get.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Would I do something so pointless?” — when she asks if he is holding back like he did on tests.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’ll learn the answer to that soon enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pairs with Hirata for three-legged practice after Horikita’s partnership with Onodera collapses.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Finds the rhythm quickly — Hirata’s praise makes the awkward drill feel simple.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Invites himself as her three-legged partner: “Partner with me for the three-legged race.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Outpaces her on purpose, then gives the lesson: “This wasn’t about fast or slow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “The important thing is to work with your partner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Names his two problems for the class: Horikita, who cannot keep a partner, and Kushida, whose rooftop darkness and hatred of Horikita must be confronted.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Therefore, the only way to resolve the issue was to have them confront one another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The praise after Sakura’s last-place finish — “You really gave it your all.” — carries no speaker tag; Sakura’s reply addresses Ayanokouji-kun, so it is recorded here rather than assigned outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: The blackboard vote, the betrayal warning, the roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: The invitation, the theory, the exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4  4  gentle methods  three legged partner hirata records the aptitude scores and asks sudou to take the festival leadership  records sakura s last place finish  the praise line that follows is untagged  and sakura answers ayanokouji kun   would you mind leading our class for this  keeps up the periodic class a meetings with katsuragi on how best to compete  fixes the cavalry girls  carriage by millimetres    let s change the positioning a bit  calls ayanokoji over for a three legged pair after horikita s partnership fails   it s really  really easy with ayanokouji kun as my partner  finishes his own practice and is straight off advising others   the class s default gentle teacher","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: Gentle methods, three-legged partner<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata records the aptitude scores and asks Sudou to take the festival leadership.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It’s really, really easy with Ayanokouji-kun as my partner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Records Sakura’s last-place finish; the praise line that follows is untagged, and Sakura answers Ayanokouji-kun.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Would you mind leading our class for this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Keeps up the periodic Class A meetings with Katsuragi on how best to compete.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Fixes the cavalry girls’ carriage by millimetres — “Let’s change the positioning a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Calls Ayanokōji over for a three-legged pair after Horikita’s partnership fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finishes his own practice and is straight off advising others — the class’s default gentle teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Runs the homeroom, the vote and the roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: On the pitch and at the podium<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka onodera horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4  the name bet and the partner problem horikita talks strategy at the first practice  then is interrupted by sudou calling her by her first name   surely the other students must think they re safe  though    on the classes watching d practice   anyone would want information on the other classes   i ve told you numerous times  please do not call me by my first name   if you continue to call me  suzune  after this warning  i ll have to take more direct action to make you stop   hard work is its own reward  why should i agree to such an idiotic bet  takes his bet and raises the bar   if you produce the best results  i will allow you to use my first name   show me that you can be the best out of everyone in our grade  the penalty clause   however  in the event that you don t get first place  i ll forever forbid you from saying my first name  neither encourages nor rejects his leadership claim   i wouldn t object to you serving as leader in this   don t get overconfident and sloppy  because i ll make you pay for that  watches his coaching with dry approval   leadership might actually suit him  don t you think   i don t want to teach them    refuses to coach the cavalry girls   you always get average scores    her read on his pe performance   i might not be able to reach class a just by improving my own skills    an uncharacteristically timid admission  fights with onodera through two three legged runs and comes in third  blamed for the pace  rejects every partner until ayanokouji offers himself   if i m expected to yield  my partner must put in the effort first  loses the demonstration run and is told to look at her partner instead of the clock","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The name bet and the partner problem<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita talks strategy at the first practice, then is interrupted by Sudou calling her by her first name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#onodera\">Onodera<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Surely the other students must think they’re safe, though.” — on the classes watching D practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Anyone would want information on the other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “I’ve told you numerous times. Please do not call me by my first name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “If you continue to call me ‘Suzune’ after this warning, I’ll have to take more direct action to make you stop.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Hard work is its own reward. Why should I agree to such an idiotic bet?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Takes his bet and raises the bar: “If you produce the best results, I will allow you to use my first name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Show me that you can be the best out of everyone in our grade,”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The penalty clause: “However, in the event that you don’t get first place, I’ll forever forbid you from saying my first name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Neither encourages nor rejects his leadership claim: “I wouldn’t object to you serving as leader in this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Don’t get overconfident and sloppy, because I’ll make you pay for that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Watches his coaching with dry approval: “Leadership might actually suit him, don’t you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I don’t want to teach them.” — refuses to coach the cavalry girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You always get average scores.” — her read on his PE performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I might not be able to reach Class A just by improving my own skills,” — an uncharacteristically timid admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Onodera<\/b> Fights with Onodera through two three-legged runs and comes in third; blamed for the pace.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Rejects every partner until Ayanokouji offers himself: “If I’m expected to yield, my partner must put in the effort first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Loses the demonstration run and is told to look at her partner instead of the clock.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Her plan wins the vote<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: The theory, the ally question, the anchor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 4  4  the watching classes and the tug demo ike spots class b and a students watching the first practice from the school building windows   hey  they re from class b  right  on the receiving end of sudou s tug of war demonstration   he and yamauchi go down in seconds  gets dirt kicked at him when sudou loses patience with the pull","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The watching classes and the tug demo<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike spots Class B and A students watching the first practice from the school-building windows.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Hey, they’re from Class B, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> On the receiving end of Sudou’s tug-of-war demonstration — he and Yamauchi go down in seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gets dirt kicked at him when Sudou loses patience with the pull.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Grip strength and the scavenger hunt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Rumors and suspicion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-inogashira-kokoro-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi inogashira-kokoro","q":"inogashira kokoro ch 4  4  the slowest pair inogashira runs the three legged race with sakura   the worst of the five girl pairs   slow as molasses  their third place last finish is what prompts horikita and onodera to try the race again","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-inogashira-kokoro-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/inogashira-kokoro.html#sc-inogashira-kokoro-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The slowest pair<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/inogashira-kokoro.html\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Inogashira runs the three-legged race with Sakura — the worst of the five girl pairs, “slow as molasses.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Their third-place-last finish is what prompts Horikita and Onodera to try the race again.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  4  the standing class a meetings katsuragi is named as hirata s periodic counterpart on how the two classes should compete  meetings continue through the run up   class d  an inch from disaster  is doing almost too well  background  ryuuen refused to cooperate with class b earlier in the volume  so no class c b channel exists","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The standing Class A meetings<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi is named as Hirata’s periodic counterpart on how the two classes should compete.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Meetings continue through the run-up — Class D, an inch from disaster, is doing almost too well.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Background: Ryuuen refused to cooperate with Class B earlier in the volume, so no Class C–B channel exists.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the Class A face<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  4  sits out the tests koenji is named among the few who sit out the aptitude testing   along with the professor  sudou s grudge  nobody in the class has seen him run seriously  though he beat sudou s swimming time  won t budge unless he wants to   his skill is obvious  his participation isn t","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kōenji is named among the few who sit out the aptitude testing — along with the Professor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou’s grudge: nobody in the class has seen him run seriously, though he beat Sudou’s swimming time.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Won’t budge unless he wants to — his skill is obvious, his participation isn’t.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Refuses to cooperate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the cottage refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4  names sudou the leader  named the second problem kushida cheers sudou through the aptitude tests and is the first to call him the festival leader   you always end up taking first place in our class  no matter the event   really  sudou kun  you re definitely the sports festival leader  her praise is what pushes sudou toward the leadership hirata then offers  ayanokoji s second problem  a backstage supporting character with unusual influence  academically and physically gifted   and assigned to class d as a mystery  he knows she hates horikita from an early rooftop rant  and resolves that the two must confront each other","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: Names Sudou the leader; named the second problem<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida cheers Sudou through the aptitude tests and is the first to call him the festival leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “You always end up taking first place in our class, no matter the event.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Really, Sudou-kun, you’re definitely the sports festival leader,”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Her praise is what pushes Sudou toward the leadership Hirata then offers.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ayanokōji’s second problem: a backstage supporting character with unusual influence, academically and physically gifted — and assigned to Class D as a mystery.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He knows she hates Horikita from an early rooftop rant, and resolves that the two must confront each other.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Asked for the middle ground<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: “It’s me”<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-onodera-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune onodera","q":"onodera ch 4  4  three legged partner for horikita onodera  the swimming club sprinter  is paired with horikita for three legged race practice   and they come in third  two failed runs   hey  horikita san  can t you try to keep pace with me better  horikita answers that onodera is the slow one  the partnership dissolves on the spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-onodera-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4: Three-legged partner for Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#onodera\">Onodera<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Onodera, the swimming-club sprinter, is paired with Horikita for three-legged race practice — and they come in third.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Two failed runs: “Hey, Horikita-san, can’t you try to keep pace with me better?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita answers that Onodera is the slow one; the partnership dissolves on the spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-onodera-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Volunteers for the recommended events<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  4  the reconnaissance that isn t ayanokoji and horikita discuss ryuuen at the edge of the first practice  not one class c student is watching d  she reads the silence as a strategy already in place    reconnaissance isn t necessary for him  the tell is that he isn t hiding it  making the absence of reconnaissance obvious is itself the display  ryuuen s non scouting reads as a message to the other classes  not as disinterest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The reconnaissance that isn’t<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji and Horikita discuss Ryuuen at the edge of the first practice: not one Class C student is watching D.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She reads the silence as a strategy already in place — “Reconnaissance isn’t necessary for him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The tell is that he isn’t hiding it: making the absence of reconnaissance obvious is itself the display.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Ryuuen’s non-scouting reads as a message to the other classes, not as disinterest.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the walkout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"inogashira-kokoro sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4  4  last place  then the worst pair sakura finishes last in the aptitude tests  barely able to stand  and is praised for giving it her all   a ayanokouji kun  works hard to contribute for the class  but her lack of physical endurance is still the problem  pairs with inogashira for the three legged race   the slowest of the five girl pairs   slow as molasses","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: Last place, then the worst pair<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakura finishes last in the aptitude tests, barely able to stand, and is praised for giving it her all.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/inogashira-kokoro.html\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “A-Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Works hard to contribute for the class, but her lack of physical endurance is still the problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/b> Pairs with Inogashira for the three-legged race — the slowest of the five girl pairs, “slow as molasses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Follows Sudou’s hand<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Named in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sotomura-hideo","q":"sotomura hideo ch 4  4  sits out the tests sotomura   the professor   is named with koenji as one of the few who sit out the aptitude testing  opts out of the physical tests while roughly 90 percent of the class takes part","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sotomura — the Professor — is named with Kōenji as one of the few who sit out the aptitude testing.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> opts out of the physical tests while roughly 90 percent of the class takes part.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: The Professor’s bad luck<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the Professor bows out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 4  4  the name bet and the leader s first week sudou arrives mid practice and calls horikita by her first name  starting the chapter s central bet   you have a minute    how the  suzune  address opens   not too long ago  you saved me    why he wants to do things properly   i think i d like to be friends with you  first  accepts the grade wide bar   if i place first in our grade level  i ll call you by your first name  goes  y yeah  when she adds the forever forbidden penalty  unbeatable in the aptitude tests   kushida calls him the sports festival leader  glares at koenji over the untested running question   even so  i dunno what ll happen if he runs  handed the leadership by hirata   would you mind leading our class for this   i ain t really suited to be a leader or anythin   okay  i ll lead our class to victory    living up to her half approval  coaches tug of war by demonstration  beating ike and yamauchi in seconds  and teaches hips over arms   look  i m tellin  you that ain t it    kicks dirt at ike and yamauchi when they botch the pull  thorough with every student who asks  but his rashness keeps undercutting the gentler style a leader needs","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: The name bet and the leader’s first week<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou arrives mid-practice and calls Horikita by her first name, starting the chapter’s central bet.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You have a minute?” — how the “Suzune” address opens.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Not too long ago, you saved me.” — why he wants to do things properly.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I think I’d like to be friends with you, first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts the grade-wide bar: “If I place first in our grade level, I’ll call you by your first name,”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Goes “Y-yeah” when she adds the forever-forbidden penalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Unbeatable in the aptitude tests — Kushida calls him the sports festival leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Glares at Kōenji over the untested running question: “Even so, I dunno what’ll happen if he runs.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Handed the leadership by Hirata: “Would you mind leading our class for this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I ain’t really suited to be a leader or anythin’…”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Okay! I’ll lead our class to victory,” — living up to her half-approval.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Coaches tug-of-war by demonstration, beating Ike and Yamauchi in seconds, and teaches hips over arms.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Look, I’m tellin’ you that ain’t it!” — kicks dirt at Ike and Yamauchi when they botch the pull.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Thorough with every student who asks, but his rashness keeps undercutting the gentler style a leader needs.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: The ability camp, then the grip-strength king<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Noodles, first names, and the anchor he gives up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4  4  on the losing end of the demo yamauchi faces sudou in the tug of war demonstration alongside ike and is pulled down in seconds  gets dirt kicked at him when sudou snaps during the coaching session","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p54-1\">Ch.4 §4: On the losing end of the demo<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi faces Sudou in the tug-of-war demonstration alongside Ike and is pulled down in seconds.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gets dirt kicked at him when Sudou snaps during the coaching session.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p23-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: The Sakura defeat still stings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ike-kanji sudou-ken shibata-sou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  5  the invitation  the theory  the exit two weeks before the festival  ayanokoji recruits horikita and kushida for a saturday reconnaissance   the first move against  the bomb waiting to go off inside class d   hang out with me today   you ll understand better if you come with me   kushida  do you have a minute   by the way  horikita will be coming  too   doing a little reconnaissance isn t a bad thing  wouldn t you agree  the theory  flat out   one other person was significantly involved in the outcome on the cruise ship   but what about kushida herself  what if she intentionally exposed her identity   only kushida knows    which is why she is invited   you and kushida seem to have some kind of connection  elevator parting   you re free to choose whether or not you come tomorrow  but if you want to lead the class  think about it  probes ike and yamauchi for sakayanagi rumors and gets nothing usable  deflects the message suspicion    absolutely not  so relax  leaves the three to their noodle talk    sorry  guys  i ve got plans  owns the setup when kushida calls it   why do you think that   it s like i half believe it  and half don t  asks the question outright   why don t you and horikita like each other  tells hirata the truth of the outing    we re spying  sets the stage for horikita s vip question  then leaves the two girls alone  glosses horikita s brother trouble for the group    some stuff happened  i guess horikita and her brother aren t really on speaking terms","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: The invitation, the theory, the exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two weeks before the festival, Ayanokōji recruits Horikita and Kushida for a Saturday reconnaissance — the first move against “the bomb waiting to go off inside Class D.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hang out with me today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You’ll understand better if you come with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Kushida, do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “By the way, Horikita will be coming, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Doing a little reconnaissance isn’t a bad thing, wouldn’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The theory, flat out: “One other person was significantly involved in the outcome on the cruise ship,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “But what about Kushida herself? What if she intentionally exposed her identity?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Only Kushida knows.” — which is why she is invited.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You and Kushida seem to have some kind of connection.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Elevator parting: “You’re free to choose whether or not you come tomorrow, but if you want to lead the class, think about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Probes Ike and Yamauchi for Sakayanagi rumors and gets nothing usable.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Deflects the message suspicion — “Absolutely not, so relax.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Leaves the three to their noodle talk — “Sorry, guys. I’ve got plans.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Owns the setup when Kushida calls it: “Why do you think that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “It’s like I half believe it, and half don’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Asks the question outright: “Why don’t you and Horikita like each other?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Tells Hirata the truth of the outing — “We’re spying.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Sets the stage for Horikita’s VIP question, then leaves the two girls alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Glosses Horikita’s brother trouble for the group — “Some stuff happened. I guess Horikita and her brother aren’t really on speaking terms.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The Ryuuen read, the partner lesson, the two problems<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: festival day, first events<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi shibata-sou ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 5  5  on the pitch and at the podium hirata is playing in the mixed year soccer practice the trio comes to watch  outplayed by nagumo in the practice game   sharp  but in a different league  walks over with shibata and forms the five person group  calls shibata the fastest in class b  takes the spy confession in stride and warns the group off shibata   personally  i d rather not compete against him  runs the participation table meeting from the podium on data and clear testing   i need more information    refuses to swap the anchor order without a reason  then submits the swapped list","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: On the pitch and at the podium<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata is playing in the mixed-year soccer practice the trio comes to watch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Outplayed by Nagumo in the practice game — sharp, but in a different league.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Walks over with Shibata and forms the five-person group; calls Shibata the fastest in Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes the spy confession in stride and warns the group off Shibata: “Personally, I’d rather not compete against him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Runs the participation-table meeting from the podium on data and clear testing.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I need more information” — refuses to swap the anchor order without a reason, then submits the swapped list.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: Gentle methods, three-legged partner<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: steady hands<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 5  5  the brother  revealed to the group horikita s brother is named as the student council president when she asks for the relay anchor   it s because i think my brother is an anchor    the reason the group had been pressing for  nagumo is framed as the candidate whose abilities are on par with the president s  ayanokoji s gloss for the others   the two  aren t really on speaking terms","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: The brother, revealed to the group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita’s brother is named as the student council president when she asks for the relay anchor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It’s because I think my brother…is an anchor,” — the reason the group had been pressing for.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo is framed as the candidate whose abilities are on par with the president’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokōji’s gloss for the others — the two “aren’t really on speaking terms.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: first again<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou nagumo-miyabi sudou-ken horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5  the theory  the ally question  the anchor horikita is pulled into ayanokoji s saturday plan and spends the walk to the dorms listening to his cruise ship theory   and if i say i don t want to   what are you planning   i don t understand the reason for inviting me   of course  everyone discovered our vip s identity   that s impossible  right    on kushida exposing herself   even if that s possible  it would hurt class d   so  you re saying that kushida would betray her allies to gain a few measly points   kushida san and i have no bond whatsoever  shows up at the lobby in a bad mood she tries to hide   information is invaluable  we don t know what might be the key to our victory   i m impressed that you have the nerve to say that when i m standing right here  will not concede nagumo s skill    he s just really athletic  that s all  cuts to the heart   during the cruise ship exam  did you tell ryuuen kun or katsuragi kun that you were the vip  the demand that matters   can i trust you to be our class s ally from this point on  asks sudou for the 1200 metre relay anchor and defends the pick    i know your abilities from seeing you practice  reveals why   it s because i think my brother is an anchor  gets the anchor handed back to her once the reason is on the table","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: The theory, the ally question, the anchor<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita is pulled into Ayanokōji’s Saturday plan and spends the walk to the dorms listening to his cruise-ship theory.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “And if I say I don’t want to?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “What are you planning?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I don’t understand the reason for inviting me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Of course. Everyone discovered our VIP’s identity.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That’s impossible, right?” — on Kushida exposing herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Even if that’s possible, it would hurt Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “So, you’re saying that Kushida would betray her allies to gain a few measly points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Kushida-san and I have no bond whatsoever,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Shows up at the lobby in a bad mood she tries to hide.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Information is invaluable. We don’t know what might be the key to our victory,”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m impressed that you have the nerve to say that when I’m standing right here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Will not concede Nagumo’s skill — “He’s just really athletic, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Cuts to the heart: “During the cruise ship exam, did you tell Ryuuen-kun or Katsuragi-kun that you were the VIP?”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The demand that matters: “Can I trust you to be our class’s ally from this point on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Asks Sudou for the 1200-metre relay anchor and defends the pick — “I know your abilities from seeing you practice,”<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Reveals why: “It’s because I think my brother…is an anchor,”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gets the anchor handed back to her once the reason is on the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The name bet and the partner problem<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: races, Kōenji, and the fall<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 5  5  rumors and suspicion ike spends saturday in ayanokoji s room and is the one who brings up sakayanagi  on the class a girl   yeah  dude  of course i remember her   she doesn t really put it out there  you know    no usable rumors  notices the messages   you know  dude  you ve been getting lots of messages lately  haven t you  the noodle room trio with sudou and yamauchi through the morning","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Rumors and suspicion<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike spends Saturday in Ayanokōji’s room and is the one who brings up Sakayanagi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> On the Class A girl: “Yeah, dude, of course I remember her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “She doesn’t really put it out there, you know?” — no usable rumors.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notices the messages: “You know, dude, you’ve been getting lots of messages lately. Haven’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The noodle-room trio with Sudou and Yamauchi through the morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The watching classes and the tug demo<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: loud from the sidelines<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 5  5  named in passing karuizawa is named only as an alternative ayanokoji considers for the saturday outing  he weighs her or sakura against kushida and decides kushida is the right person   no scene presence this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Named in passing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Karuizawa is named only as an alternative Ayanokōji considers for the Saturday outing.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He weighs her or Sakura against Kushida and decides Kushida is the right person — no scene presence this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: The other camp, then the entrance meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: rescue, leak, lunch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 5  5  named in the cruise ship theory katsuragi is the other upperclassman horikita names when she asks kushida the vip question   did you tell ryuuen kun or katsuragi kun that you were the vip    the question  with ryuuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi is the other upperclassman Horikita names when she asks Kushida the VIP question.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “did you tell Ryuuen-kun or Katsuragi-kun that you were the VIP?” — the question, with Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The standing Class A meetings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: Class A’s split on the field<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune shibata-sou sudou-ken kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5  5   it s me  kushida is recruited for the saturday outing and accepts with her usual warmth  noting how unusual the invitation is   hmm  what is it  ayanokouji kun   you know  it s really unusual for you to invite me out  ayanokouji kun   we ll meet in the dorm lobby tomorrow morning  then  welcomes horikita to the lobby with an unwavering smile despite the bad mood aimed at her   i feel kind of like a secret agent  spying on clubs to gain information about other classes   it was really kind of you to do this for horikita san s sake  ayanokouji kun  drops the pretense first   ayanokouji kun  you were the one who decided to invite me out today  weren t you   you understand that things aren t good between horikita san and me  don t you  asked why the two dislike each other  she answers   it s me  well informed as ever   knows shibata outclasses hirata and greets nagumo by nickname  answers the ally demand   of course  i want to get to class a  alongside everyone from class d  intervenes in the anchor dispute and backs the swap once sudou is satisfied","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: “It’s me”<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida is recruited for the Saturday outing and accepts with her usual warmth, noting how unusual the invitation is.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Hmm? What is it, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “You know, it’s really unusual for you to invite me out, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I feel kind of like a secret agent, spying on clubs to gain information about other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “We’ll meet in the dorm lobby tomorrow morning, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Welcomes Horikita to the lobby with an unwavering smile despite the bad mood aimed at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “it was really kind of you to do this for Horikita-san’s sake, Ayanokouji-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Drops the pretense first: “Ayanokouji-kun, you were the one who decided to invite me out today, weren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You understand that things aren’t good between Horikita-san and me, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asked why the two dislike each other, she answers: “It’s me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Well-informed as ever — knows Shibata outclasses Hirata and greets Nagumo by nickname.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Answers the ally demand: “Of course. I want to get to Class A, alongside everyone from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Intervenes in the anchor dispute and backs the swap once Sudou is satisfied.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: Names Sudou the leader; named the second problem<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: compromise partner and searcher<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi","q":"nagumo miyabi ch 5  5  the practice pitch nagumo strolls onto the soccer pitch mid practice and is greeted by kushida by nickname   i see you re on a date   we don t really hold back here  so i think this is a good way to measure our players  strengths  calls her  kikyou chan  and winks before rejoining the game  outclasses both hirata and shibata in the practice game  then scores from midfield    in a different league  horikita refuses to concede the skill   he s just really athletic  that s all  introduced as the candidate to be next student council president  abilities on par with horikita s older brother","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html#sc-nagumo-miyabi-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: The practice pitch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nagumo strolls onto the soccer pitch mid-practice and is greeted by Kushida by nickname.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “I see you’re on a date.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “We don’t really hold back here, so I think this is a good way to measure our players’ strengths,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Calls her “Kikyou-chan” and winks before rejoining the game.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Outclasses both Hirata and Shibata in the practice game, then scores from midfield — “in a different league.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita refuses to concede the skill: “He’s just really athletic, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Introduced as the candidate to be next student council president, abilities on par with Horikita’s older brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 5  5  named in the cruise ship theory ryuuen is the first name in ayanokoji s theory about how the vip identity leaked  horikita s own dead end   i assume ryuuen kun was involved somehow  horikita puts the direct question to kushida   did she tell ryuuen or katsuragi she was the vip  the theory holds that ryuuen was one party  a second  inside class d  was significantly involved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen is the first name in Ayanokōji’s theory about how the VIP identity leaked.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita’s own dead end: “I assume Ryuuen-kun was involved somehow,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Horikita puts the direct question to Kushida — did she tell Ryuuen or Katsuragi she was the VIP?<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The theory holds that Ryuuen was one party; a second, inside Class D, was significantly involved.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The reconnaissance that isn’t<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: foul play and the forfeit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki sakayanagi-arisu","q":"sakayanagi arisu ch 5  5  rumored from a distance sakayanagi is raised in ayanokoji s room as a possible source of class a information  ike remembers her as  that beautiful girl  no usable rumors come back  yamauchi s contribution  people say she s the class leader and  really  like  mature  the two boys deliver nothing actionable   ayanokoji s question goes nowhere","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Rumored from a distance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakayanagi is raised in Ayanokōji’s room as a possible source of Class A information.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike remembers her as “that beautiful girl”; no usable rumors come back.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi’s contribution: people say she’s the class leader and “really, like, mature.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two boys deliver nothing actionable — Ayanokōji’s question goes nowhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the introduction<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the thin smile<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5  5  named in passing sakura is named as the girl yamauchi confessed to over the summer   and lost  the defeat still shows in yamauchi s forced smile during the noodle talk  ayanokoji considers bringing her or karuizawa to the grounds instead of kushida  but judges the wrong person for the job","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Named in passing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakura is named as the girl Yamauchi confessed to over the summer — and lost.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The defeat still shows in Yamauchi’s forced smile during the noodle talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji considers bringing her or Karuizawa to the grounds instead of Kushida, but judges the wrong person for the job.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: Last place, then the worst pair<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p92-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: not last<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka shibata-sou","q":"shibata so ch 5  5  the fastest in class b shibata scores on a brilliant arc during the practice the trio watches  then joins their group the next day  better than hirata by his own senior s account    hirata kun says that shibata kun is better than he is  remembers ayanokoji s name and asks if he is on a date with the two girls  hirata s warning to the group   we need to be especially wary of shibata kun  he s the fastest in class b  makes no attempt to hide his speed   whether for ichinose s class b or from personality","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: The fastest in Class B<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shibata scores on a brilliant arc during the practice the trio watches, then joins their group the next day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Better than Hirata by his own senior’s account — “Hirata-kun says that Shibata-kun is better than he is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Remembers Ayanokōji’s name and asks if he is on a date with the two girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata’s warning to the group: “We need to be especially wary of Shibata-kun. He’s the fastest in Class B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Makes no attempt to hide his speed — whether for Ichinose’s Class B or from personality.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: Sudou’s rival on the clock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 5  5  noodles  first names  and the anchor he gives up sudou spends saturday morning in ayanokoji s room with ike and yamauchi  cup noodles in hand  talking about horikita   what flavor did you get   trade with me  please  an untagged classmate asks  do you plan on telling horikita  and sudou answers  huh  the hell is this about   that depends on how the festival goes    on making a move after the bet   there ain t none of the first years better than me at sports   let s talk about my future with suzune  given the relay anchor  then pulled aside when horikita asks for it  not convinced   it s just  y know  the anchor position goes to the fastest team member   i ain t convinced  this ain t like you  horikita  yields once the brother reason is on the table    i don t mind handin  it over to you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: Noodles, first names, and the anchor he gives up<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou spends Saturday morning in Ayanokōji’s room with Ike and Yamauchi, cup noodles in hand, talking about Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “What flavor did you get?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Trade with me, please?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> An untagged classmate asks “Do you plan on telling Horikita?” and Sudou answers “Huh? The hell is this about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That depends on how the festival goes.” — on making a move after the bet.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “there ain’t none of the first years better than me at sports,”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Let’s talk about my future with Suzune,”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Given the relay anchor, then pulled aside when Horikita asks for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Not convinced: “It’s just, y’know, the anchor position goes to the fastest team member.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I ain’t convinced. This ain’t like you, Horikita,”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Yields once the brother reason is on the table — “I don’t mind handin’ it over to you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The name bet and the leader’s first week<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the leader’s festival<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5  5  the sakura defeat still stings yamauchi is in the saturday noodle group  forced smiling through the talk  still nursing the summer confession defeat    y yeah  to ike s teasing  passes on the class leader rumor   from what i ve heard  people say that she s the class leader  presses the girlfriend question   you don t have a girlfriend  do you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p68-1\">Ch.5 §5: The Sakura defeat still stings<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi is in the Saturday noodle group, forced-smiling through the talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Still nursing the summer confession defeat — “Y-yeah.” to Ike’s teasing.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Passes on the class-leader rumor: “From what I’ve heard, people say that she’s the class leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Presses the girlfriend question: “You don’t have a girlfriend, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: On the losing end of the demo<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: lunch detail<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p86-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke sakayanagi-arisu","q":"sports festival ch 6  6  the festival runs festival day  opening ceremony  then the thirteen event schedule begins with the 100 metre dash under a finish line camera  first year boys form ten groups of eight for the 100 metre dash   two from each class   run at about twenty second intervals  hurdle penalties  0 5 seconds for a knocked down hurdle  0 3 for a touch  ten hurdles at ten metre intervals  all down adds five seconds  capture the flag  the group that makes two captures wins  offense may not contact the other side s offense  blatant punches and kicks are prohibited but a degree of roughhousing is overlooked  tug of war and ball toss run as team competitions  the first team to two points wins the tug  same structure as capture the flag  girls  ball toss result printed   with fifty four points total  the red team wins  after the 100 metre dash across all grades  red team 2011 points  white team 1891   red slightly ahead as the festival opens  takes first in the 100 metre dash and the boys  obstacle course   three individual firsts in a row by p 112  absent from his lane  the school marks the absence without searching   a missing red team scorer  also non participating  but with a valid reason in the text s account   two red team handicaps against b and c full rosters","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html#sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p86-1\">Ch.6 §6: the festival runs<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.86–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html\">Sports Festival<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Festival day: opening ceremony, then the thirteen-event schedule begins with the 100-metre dash under a finish-line camera.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> First-year boys form ten groups of eight for the 100-metre dash — two from each class — run at about twenty-second intervals.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Hurdle penalties: 0.5 seconds for a knocked-down hurdle, 0.3 for a touch; ten hurdles at ten-metre intervals; all down adds five seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Capture the flag: the group that makes two captures wins; offense may not contact the other side’s offense; blatant punches and kicks are prohibited but a degree of roughhousing is overlooked.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Tug-of-war and ball toss run as team competitions; the first team to two points wins the tug, same structure as capture the flag.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Girls’ ball toss result printed: “With fifty-four points total, the Red Team wins.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> After the 100-metre dash across all grades: Red Team 2011 points, White Team 1891 — Red slightly ahead as the festival opens.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Takes first in the 100-metre dash and the boys’ obstacle course — three individual firsts in a row by p.112.<span class=\"pg\">p.88, 112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Absent from his lane; the school marks the absence without searching — a missing Red Team scorer.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Also non-participating, but with a valid reason in the text’s account — two Red Team handicaps against B and C full rosters.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Four-way tug-of-war and the luck events<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.7–6.10: afternoon rules and the morning’s end<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji sakura-airi horikita-suzune yukimura-teruhiko katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  6  festival day  first events sports festival day opens  fujimaki s speech  medical cottage and facing team tents  a camera on the 100 metre finish line  class d marches in jerseys   all right  time to really show off for kikyou chan  shouted ike as he walked directly behind me  tells horikita he drew the seventh group for the 100 metre dash  his only aim is not to come in last  watches sudou win group one by a landslide and hirata take first in group seven  he finishes fifth  keeping his pace inconspicuous  spots sudou missing from the seat and runs with hirata toward the cottage as sudou confronts koenji  when sakura asks if he watched her race  he answers  you did well  without admitting he had been chasing sudou  after the girls  dash he asks whether she reached out to koenji  she lets slip  i never hated her or anything  about kushida and clamps down  holds third in the hurdles and trades talk with kanzaki  who reports ichinose s read of him as calm for a high schooler  gives yukimura room after seventh and seventh  then turns to the girls  hurdles  in capture the flag he brings up the rear with ike and yukimura while sudou tears into the defense  after sudou is dropped he keeps his distance  walks back with hirata and katsuragi exchanging apologies after the flag falls  talks sudou out of a new scandal  recalling the fight that almost got him expelled  and accepts class c will call the stomp heat of the moment  pulls in the d a tug of war under hirata and katsuragi  after ryuuen s rope drop he is thrown backward with the rest  takes third in the obstacle heat to avoid sudou s wrath  then watches sudou edge shibata for first  leaves hirata in charge of the group and goes to horikita after her fall  he judges that another such  accident  would be too much to believe  treats the stacked mishaps as deliberate and takes hirata s uneasy agreement as confirmation someone is working the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\">Ch.6 §6: festival day, first events<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.86–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sports festival day opens: Fujimaki’s speech, medical cottage and facing team tents, a camera on the 100-metre finish line; Class D marches in jerseys.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “All right, time to really show off for Kikyou-chan!” shouted Ike as he walked directly behind me.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tells Horikita he drew the seventh group for the 100-metre dash; his only aim is not to come in last.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Sudou win group one by a landslide and Hirata take first in group seven; he finishes fifth, keeping his pace inconspicuous.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Spots Sudou missing from the seat and runs with Hirata toward the cottage as Sudou confronts Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> When Sakura asks if he watched her race, he answers “You did well,” without admitting he had been chasing Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> After the girls’ dash he asks whether she reached out to Kōenji; she lets slip “I never hated her or anything” about Kushida and clamps down.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Holds third in the hurdles and trades talk with Kanzaki, who reports Ichinose’s read of him as calm for a high schooler.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Gives Yukimura room after seventh-and-seventh, then turns to the girls’ hurdles.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In capture the flag he brings up the rear with Ike and Yukimura while Sudou tears into the defense; after Sudou is dropped he keeps his distance.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Walks back with Hirata and Katsuragi exchanging apologies after the flag falls.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Talks Sudou out of a new scandal, recalling the fight that almost got him expelled, and accepts Class C will call the stomp heat-of-the-moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pulls in the D/A tug-of-war under Hirata and Katsuragi; after Ryuuen’s rope-drop he is thrown backward with the rest.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes third in the obstacle heat to avoid Sudou’s wrath, then watches Sudou edge Shibata for first.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Leaves Hirata in charge of the group and goes to Horikita after her fall; he judges that another such “accident” would be too much to believe.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Treats the stacked mishaps as deliberate and takes Hirata’s uneasy agreement as confirmation someone is working the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: The invitation, the theory, the exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.7–6.10: observation, cavalry, and the plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-fujimaki-y1v5-p86-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"fujimaki","q":"fujimaki ch 6  6  the opening speech fujimaki  third year class a  gives a speech during the opening ceremony as the whole student body stands in jerseys  speaks for the red team command he took at the assembly  spectators on the outskirts watch without strict restriction  the speech s content is not quoted  only the fact of it is on the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-fujimaki-y1v5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the opening speech<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.86<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#fujimaki\">Fujimaki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fujimaki, third-year Class A, gives a speech during the opening ceremony as the whole student body stands in jerseys.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Speaks for the Red Team command he took at the assembly; spectators on the outskirts watch without strict restriction.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The speech’s content is not quoted; only the fact of it is on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-fujimaki-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: Red Team command<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p86-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 6  6  loud from the sidelines ike walks behind ayanokoji into the festival already vowing to show off for kushida   all right  time to really show off for kikyou chan  shouted ike as he walked directly behind me   sudou s got first place covered   oh  baldy s i mean  katsuragi s in the first lane  said ike  pointing at katsuragi s head   dude  we ve got more important things to look at  gets put in a headlock as sudou s stress relief and taps out   i give  i give  shouted ike  in capture the flag he hangs at the rear with ayanokoji and yukimura  muttering he does not want sudou to kill him for skipping   that one half japanese guy  yamada or whatever  he s going on a rampage   it s just  like  those guys are really strong  you know   better keep my distance  ike muttered  in the tug of war he doubts the line up and panics when the second round turns   look  they ain t even lining up by height  like we are  said ike  finishes sixth in the obstacle heat and dreads sudou s reaction before sudou s own race   man  i ran my heart out  and i still only got sixth place   what place did you get  ayanokouji  ike demanded   will you get sudou s death penalty   we re practically equal  blubbered ike  all bark and no bite by ayanokoji s account  his festival voice is crude cheer and panic in equal measure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p86-1\">Ch.6 §6: loud from the sidelines<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.86–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike walks behind Ayanokōji into the festival already vowing to show off for Kushida.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “All right, time to really show off for Kikyou-chan!” shouted Ike as he walked directly behind me.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Sudou’s got first place covered!”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Oh, Baldy’s—I mean, Katsuragi’s—in the first lane,” said Ike, pointing at Katsuragi’s head.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dude, we’ve got more important things to look at.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gets put in a headlock as Sudou’s stress relief and taps out.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I give, I give!” shouted Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In capture the flag he hangs at the rear with Ayanokōji and Yukimura, muttering he does not want Sudou to kill him for skipping.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That one half-Japanese guy, Yamada or whatever, he’s going on a rampage!”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s just, like, those guys are really strong, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Better keep my distance,” Ike muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In the tug-of-war he doubts the line-up and panics when the second round turns.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Look, they ain’t even lining up by height, like we are,” said Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finishes sixth in the obstacle heat and dreads Sudou’s reaction before Sudou’s own race.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Man, I ran my heart out, and I still only got sixth place!”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What place did you get, Ayanokouji?” Ike demanded.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you get Sudou’s death penalty?”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re practically equal!” blubbered Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> All bark and no bite by Ayanokōji’s account; his festival voice is crude cheer and panic in equal measure.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Rumors and suspicion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: carried, then lunch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p87-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke horikita-manabu sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6  races  koenji  and the fall horikita opens the chapter asking ayanokoji which 100 metre group he drew  then runs her own races through the day   what group are you in for the 100 meter dash  again  horikita asked   i ll be cheering you on for the class s sake  takes first in her 100 metre heat as expected  later wins a tight finish against ibuki  had pressed him to participate  after his no show she admits the outreach was meaningless and lets slip she never hated kushida   i never hated her or anything  horikita realized that she d slipped up  and immediately clamped her mouth shut   you didn t hear that  she added  watches her brother take first in the third year dash and answers ayanokoji s comment as simple fact   that s because my brother is perfect  horikita answered  finishes third in the girls  hurdles behind class c s yajima and kinoshita after hirata s warning  in the girls  obstacle course she fights up to second  then tangles with kinoshita on the final stretch and drops to seventh  shares the day s stage with sakura s races but does not join her conversation with ayanokoji   if i rest  i ll be okay   leave me alone  said horikita  tries to look tough after the fall while he checks her injury  the pride that produced results now has to sit out  takes pride in producing results  so an injury she cannot train through hits harder than the pain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p87-1\">Ch.6 §6: races, Kōenji, and the fall<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.87–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita opens the chapter asking Ayanokōji which 100-metre group he drew, then runs her own races through the day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What group are you in for the 100-meter dash, again?” Horikita asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’ll be cheering you on for the class’s sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I never hated her or anything.” Horikita realized that she’d slipped up, and immediately clamped her mouth shut.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes first in her 100-metre heat as expected; later wins a tight finish against Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Had pressed him to participate; after his no-show she admits the outreach was meaningless and lets slip she never hated Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You didn’t hear that,” she added.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Watches her brother take first in the third-year dash and answers Ayanokōji’s comment as simple fact.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s because my brother is perfect.” Horikita answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finishes third in the girls’ hurdles behind Class C’s Yajima and Kinoshita after Hirata’s warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In the girls’ obstacle course she fights up to second, then tangles with Kinoshita on the final stretch and drops to seventh.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Shares the day’s stage with Sakura’s races but does not join her conversation with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I rest, I’ll be okay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Leave me alone.” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Tries to look tough after the fall while he checks her injury; the pride that produced results now has to sit out.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes pride in producing results, so an injury she cannot train through hits harder than the pain.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: The theory, the ally question, the anchor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: injury, cavalry, and the wake-up call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p87-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 6  6  the leader s festival sudou lines up for the first year boys  100 metre dash in group one and carries class d s hopes on his speed  wins the 100 metre dash by a landslide  the professor  in the same heat  comes in last  storms the cottage to confront koenji for sitting out  his punch is caught in koenji s palm  and hirata walks him back to camp   don t give me that bull crap   next time  i m seriously going to punch that jerk  he huffed   stress relief  said sudou    headlocks ike as horikita s heat is about to start  threatens to beat him for skipping the event  then sulks that he will punch him next time  as capture the flag offense he charges the flag line alone  yamada punches him in the stomach and ryuuen stomps his back as the flag falls   just how many of you are gonna come after me   you re useless   that was foul play   the next time i run into him  i m gonna lay him out flat  vows to lay ryuuen flat  ayanokoji talks him down by citing the near expulsion fight  accepts hirata s calming hand after the flag falls  though his anger outweighs the pain  pushes the tug of war despite his injured back  after ryuuen s forfeit he charges again and katsuragi holds him back   that s exactly why we can t lose this  sudou said   class b put their biggest dudes up way up in front   with those guys lined up like that  there s no way they ll win  said sudou   i won t accept anything besides victory  takes first in the obstacle course three times in a row  beating shibata in a close finish  then pins ike in a nelson hold for sixth place   still  though  that shibata guy was really fast  said sudou  balls his fists cheering horikita on in the girls  obstacle course  his leadership style is open threats   kick the asses of the people under him   and he admits no one really wants such a leader","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p87-1\">Ch.6 §6: the leader’s festival<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.87–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou lines up for the first-year boys’ 100-metre dash in group one and carries Class D’s hopes on his speed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Don’t give me that bull crap!”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Next time, I’m seriously going to punch that jerk,” he huffed.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Stress relief,” said Sudou. — headlocks Ike as Horikita’s heat is about to start.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Wins the 100-metre dash by a landslide; the Professor, in the same heat, comes in last.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Storms the cottage to confront Kōenji for sitting out; his punch is caught in Kōenji’s palm, and Hirata walks him back to camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Threatens to beat him for skipping the event, then sulks that he will punch him next time.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> As capture-the-flag offense he charges the flag line alone; Yamada punches him in the stomach and Ryuuen stomps his back as the flag falls.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just how many of you are gonna come after me?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re useless!”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was foul play!”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next time I run into him, I’m gonna lay him out flat!”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Vows to lay Ryuuen flat; Ayanokōji talks him down by citing the near-expulsion fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Accepts Hirata’s calming hand after the flag falls, though his anger outweighs the pain.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pushes the tug-of-war despite his injured back; after Ryuuen’s forfeit he charges again and Katsuragi holds him back.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s exactly why we can’t lose this,” Sudou said.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class B put their biggest dudes up way up in front.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With those guys lined up like that, there’s no way they’ll win,” said Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t accept anything besides victory!”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes first in the obstacle course three times in a row, beating Shibata in a close finish; then pins Ike in a nelson hold for sixth place.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Still, though, that Shibata guy was really fast.” said Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Balls his fists cheering Horikita on in the girls’ obstacle course.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His leadership style is open threats — kick the asses of the people under him — and he admits no one really wants such a leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Noodles, first names, and the anchor he gives up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: first place, bait, and the punch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p88-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  6  steady hands hirata runs the seventh group of the 100 metre dash and takes first  then spends the day as class d s calmer counterweight to sudou  takes first in his heat  when ayanokoji apologizes for fifth he refuses to blame him    that s not true  everyone was fast  it was a good race  goes with ayanokoji to stop sudou s confrontation with koenji at the cottage   kouenji kun s attitude is a problem  but if he says he s not feeling well  then he has the right to rest  steps between sudou and koenji  then switches to the leader s duty argument to pull sudou away   the next competition is about to begin  sudou kun  after the flag falls he apologizes for not protecting it and proposes the next game   it s because we couldn t protect the flag  accepts the shared blame with katsuragi on the way back to tents  later katsuragi quietly apologizes to him for class a s split  co commands the tug of war with katsuragi  insists no contact rules favour pure strength  and holds the height order line   in tug of war  there s no physical contact   when you re pulling the rope  an elevated position is advantageous  names shibata s pure speed as a real threat to sudou in the obstacle heat   i don t know  honestly   this is the most intense match so far today  said hirata  warns horikita that class c s track club pair yajima and kinoshita are in her hurdles group  after horikita s fall agrees the  accident  pattern is ominous and accepts the charge of watching the group while ayanokoji goes to her   that s my role  after all  takes his caretaker role without a hint of disgust even when asked to carry it alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p88-1\">Ch.6 §6: steady hands<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.88–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata runs the seventh group of the 100-metre dash and takes first, then spends the day as Class D’s calmer counterweight to Sudou.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Kouenji-kun’s attitude is a problem, but if he says he’s not feeling well, then he has the right to rest.”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “The next competition is about to begin, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It’s because we couldn’t protect the flag.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes first in his heat; when Ayanokōji apologizes for fifth he refuses to blame him — “That’s not true. Everyone was fast. It was a good race,”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes with Ayanokōji to stop Sudou’s confrontation with Kōenji at the cottage.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Steps between Sudou and Kōenji, then switches to the leader’s duty argument to pull Sudou away.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After the flag falls he apologizes for not protecting it and proposes the next game.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Accepts the shared blame with Katsuragi on the way back to tents; later Katsuragi quietly apologizes to him for Class A’s split.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Co-commands the tug-of-war with Katsuragi; insists no-contact rules favour pure strength, and holds the height-order line.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “in tug-of-war, there’s no physical contact.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When you’re pulling the rope, an elevated position is advantageous,”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Names Shibata’s pure speed as a real threat to Sudou in the obstacle heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know, honestly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is the most intense match so far today,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Warns Horikita that Class C’s track club pair Yajima and Kinoshita are in her hurdles group.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> After Horikita’s fall agrees the “accident” pattern is ominous and accepts the charge of watching the group while Ayanokōji goes to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s my role, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes his caretaker role without a hint of disgust even when asked to carry it alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: On the pitch and at the podium<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: jockey, victim, cover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p88-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji ch 6  6  the chats at the line kanzaki wins the third group of the 100 metre dash ahead of katsuragi  then meets ayanokoji again in the hurdles  takes first place  katsuragi is third   class b s runner outclasses class a s wall in pure speed   we meet again  said kanzaki   ichinose says you re pretty fast  he replied  carries ichinose s homework on ayanokoji   his ranking and his thought process   into the pre race talk   it didn t seem to me that you were taking the race seriously  kanzaki replied   you know  you re really calm for a high schooler  kanzaki added  he follows with  it s scary    a two word reply kept as note  not a quote row  weighs him as a strategist who would not waste effort holding back  and finishes ahead of him in the heat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p88-1\">Ch.6 §6: the chats at the line<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.88–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kanzaki wins the third group of the 100-metre dash ahead of Katsuragi, then meets Ayanokōji again in the hurdles.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “We meet again,” said Kanzaki.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Ichinose says you’re pretty fast,” he replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “It didn’t seem to me that you were taking the race seriously,” Kanzaki replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes first place; Katsuragi is third — Class B’s runner outclasses Class A’s wall in pure speed.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Carries Ichinose’s homework on Ayanokōji — his ranking and his thought process — into the pre-race talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, you’re really calm for a high schooler,” Kanzaki added.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He follows with “It’s scary.” — a two-word reply kept as note, not a quote row.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Weighs him as a strategist who would not waste effort holding back, and finishes ahead of him in the heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p124-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: cavalry horse under a Class B general<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p88-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 6  6  class a s split on the field katsuragi takes third in his 100 metre group behind kanzaki  then co directs the d a teams through capture the flag and the tug of war  is named by ike as  baldy  at the line  his scalp catches the sun  kanzaki wins the heat and katsuragi third  holds the defensive side of capture the flag  after sudou s flag falls he accepts shared blame with hirata   i apologize that we weren t of much use  he said  is challenged mid tug of war by hashimoto s half of class a and answers that losing to bickering would be sakayanagi s fault   but if we lose because of meaningless bickering  it won t be our lack of cooperation or skill to blame  reads the timed rebellion as her work  her thin smile from camp can only mean she instigated it   you really are blind  huh  katsuragi kun  hashimoto sneered  steadies the third tug round after the second loss  then stops sudou s charge at ryuuen s rope drop   we lost because our opponents used the right formation to beat us  names the forfeit as a plan to waste d a energy and provoke foul play  and notes it was unsportsmanlike but not a rules violation  holds sudou back  pats his shoulder  and later apologizes to hirata for failing to lead class a   i wasn t able to lead my class  he told hirata  control under fire is masterful   class a s crisis is visible  but he does not panic in front of the coalition","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p88-1\">Ch.6 §6: Class A’s split on the field<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.88–110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi takes third in his 100-metre group behind Kanzaki, then co-directs the D/A teams through capture the flag and the tug-of-war.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hashimoto-masayoshi\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I apologize that we weren’t of much use,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “But if we lose because of meaningless bickering, it won’t be our lack of cooperation or skill to blame.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You really are blind, huh, Katsuragi-kun?” Hashimoto sneered.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Is named by Ike as “Baldy” at the line; his scalp catches the sun; Kanzaki wins the heat and Katsuragi third.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Holds the defensive side of capture the flag; after Sudou’s flag falls he accepts shared blame with Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Is challenged mid tug-of-war by Hashimoto’s half of Class A and answers that losing to bickering would be Sakayanagi’s fault.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reads the timed rebellion as her work; her thin smile from camp can only mean she instigated it.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steadies the third tug round after the second loss, then stops Sudou’s charge at Ryuuen’s rope-drop.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We lost because our opponents used the right formation to beat us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Names the forfeit as a plan to waste D/A energy and provoke foul play, and notes it was unsportsmanlike but not a rules violation.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Holds Sudou back, pats his shoulder, and later apologizes to Hirata for failing to lead Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wasn’t able to lead my class,” he told Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Control under fire is masterful — Class A’s crisis is visible, but he does not panic in front of the coalition.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p123-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the abandoned rescue and the pincer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 6  6  the cottage refusal koenji fails to appear in his assigned lane for the third group of the 100 metre dash  the school marks an absence without searching  found inside the medical cottage fussing with his hair while class d and the red team lose a competitor   you re quite foul  aren t you   i came here to enjoy some me time  catches sudou s punch in one palm and waves him off without looking at him   you cannot hope to beat me  kouenji didn t even look at sudou as he spoke   both you and that girl seem to consider me unreliable  names that cold girl   the one inflaming sudou s passion   as horikita  who keeps pushing him to participate  the printed sentence runs across the p 90 91 break and is not quoted whole   in any case  leave now  said kouenji  waving us away   my proud carriage serves to disguise how poor my health is   if i recover  i will of course participate  replied kouenji  is lectured on violence and leader absence by hirata  then escorted out of the way as sudou is walked back  illness is openly a pose  he cooperated only through the opening ceremonies and bows out when it counts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\">Ch.6 §6: the cottage refusal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.88–91<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kōenji fails to appear in his assigned lane for the third group of the 100-metre dash; the school marks an absence without searching.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “You’re quite foul, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “I came here to enjoy some me time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “You cannot hope to beat me.” Kouenji didn’t even look at Sudou as he spoke.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Found inside the medical cottage fussing with his hair while Class D and the Red Team lose a competitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Catches Sudou’s punch in one palm and waves him off without looking at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both you and that girl seem to consider me unreliable,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Names that cold girl — the one inflaming Sudou’s passion — as Horikita, who keeps pushing him to participate; the printed sentence runs across the p.90–91 break and is not quoted whole.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In any case, leave now.” said Kouenji, waving us away.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My proud carriage serves to disguise how poor my health is,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I recover, I will of course participate.” replied Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Is lectured on violence and leader-absence by Hirata, then escorted out of the way as Sudou is walked back.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Illness is openly a pose; he cooperated only through the opening ceremonies and bows out when it counts.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: still absent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p92-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6  6  not last sakura arrives breathless beside ayanokoji after the girls  100 metre dash  still hurting from the effort  sakura arrives panting  ahh ahh  i it hurts    the broken cry is too short for a quote row   w were you watching me  ayanokouji kun  she asked  he lies by omission and says  you did well  because he had been chasing sudou and saw nothing   this is the first time i didn t come in dead last  she beamed  her race ran while he was chasing sudou  she never knows the gap   you might hurt yourself  i said  she replies  o okay    a five character answer kept as note rather than a quote row  always the slowest in practice  she finally beats someone on her own effort  not an opponent s mistake  runs the girls  hurdles in the same heat as horikita  zero expectations  trembling at the start  gratitude for the smallest kindness  her festival is measured in not finishing last","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p92-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p92-1\">Ch.6 §6: not last<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.92–99<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakura arrives breathless beside Ayanokōji after the girls’ 100-metre dash, still hurting from the effort.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “W-were you watching me, Ayanokouji-kun?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “This is the first time I didn’t come in dead last.” She beamed.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> “You might hurt yourself,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakura arrives panting “Ahh…ahh…! I-It hurts…” — the broken cry is too short for a quote row.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He lies by omission and says “You did well,” because he had been chasing Sudou and saw nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Her race ran while he was chasing Sudou; she never knows the gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She replies “O-okay!” — a five-character answer kept as note rather than a quote row.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Always the slowest in practice, she finally beats someone on her own effort, not an opponent’s mistake.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Runs the girls’ hurdles in the same heat as Horikita; zero expectations, trembling at the start.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gratitude for the smallest kindness; her festival is measured in not finishing last.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Named in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  6  the rivalry heat ibuki draws the same 100 metre group as horikita   her most bitter rival   and burns to beat her  starts better than horikita  stays neck and neck  then loses by a narrow margin at the tape  hyperawareness of horikita costs her the win  had she not watched her  the result might have differed   ibuki was faster than i expected  said horikita  kicks the ground in frustration after the loss  determined never to lose to horikita  no matter the event   fire in her eyes from the line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\">Ch.6 §6: the rivalry heat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.94–95<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki draws the same 100-metre group as Horikita — her most bitter rival — and burns to beat her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Ibuki was faster than I expected,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Starts better than Horikita, stays neck and neck, then loses by a narrow margin at the tape.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Hyperawareness of Horikita costs her the win; had she not watched her, the result might have differed.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kicks the ground in frustration after the loss.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Determined never to lose to Horikita, no matter the event — fire in her eyes from the line.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the order on Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6  first again horikita manabu runs in the second group of the third year 100 metre dash as his sister watches  naturally takes first place  she answers ayanokoji s comment as simple fact  her brother is perfect and always number one   that s because my brother is perfect  ayanokoji adds that the president does not care about his little sister s feelings in the slightest   his read  not a page quote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\">Ch.6 §6: first again<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.95–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita Manabu runs in the second group of the third-year 100-metre dash as his sister watches.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s because my brother is perfect.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Naturally takes first place.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She answers Ayanokōji’s comment as simple fact: her brother is perfect and always number one.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji adds that the president does not care about his little sister’s feelings in the slightest — his read, not a page quote.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: The brother, revealed to the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p95-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken shibata-sou","q":"shibata so ch 6  6  sudou s rival on the clock shibata is named again as faster than hirata as the 100 metre results settle  hirata   shibata kun s even faster than me  after all    seen during club practice  wins the hurdle race without much difficulty and becomes sudou s main individual rival  named with kanzaki as leading class b s side in capture the flag  after the first tug round he tells ryuuen the white team must work together  ryuuen ignores him and re forms class c  is brushed off when he warns that the d a side is too strong to face split  pushes sudou to the tape in the obstacle course  pure speed may be his  but sudou takes first for the third time  sudou after the race  the shibata guy was really fast  and he only just beat him  like ichinose  his leadership makes others rally around him   a standing threat to sudou s all grade first place dream","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p95-1\">Ch.6 §6: Sudou’s rival on the clock<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.95–112<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shibata is named again as faster than Hirata as the 100-metre results settle.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Wins the hurdle race without much difficulty and becomes Sudou’s main individual rival.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Named with Kanzaki as leading Class B’s side in capture the flag.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata: “Shibata-kun’s even faster than me, after all,” — seen during club practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After the first tug round he tells Ryuuen the White Team must work together; Ryuuen ignores him and re-forms Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Is brushed off when he warns that the D/A side is too strong to face split.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pushes Sudou to the tape in the obstacle course; pure speed may be his, but Sudou takes first for the third time.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou after the race: the Shibata guy was really fast, and he only just beat him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Like Ichinose, his leadership makes others rally around him — a standing threat to Sudou’s all-grade first-place dream.<span class=\"pg\">p.97–112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: The fastest in Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p124-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: cavalry horse under a Class B general<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p97-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"shibata-sou kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 6  6  passing mentions ichinose is named as shibata s leadership peer as he pulls ahead of sudou in the hurdles   like ichinose  his leadership qualities made others rally around him  kanzaki carries her read of ayanokoji into the pre race talk   ichinose says you re pretty fast  ichinose does not appear on these pages  both rows are other characters  reports of her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p97-1\">Ch.6 §6: passing mentions<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.97–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose is named as Shibata’s leadership peer as he pulls ahead of Sudou in the hurdles.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> “like Ichinose, his leadership qualities made others rally around him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Kanzaki carries her read of Ayanokōji into the pre-race talk: “Ichinose says you’re pretty fast,”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose does not appear on these pages; both rows are other characters’ reports of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: confronting the walkout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p119-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: fair play under the smile<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p97-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken sotomura-hideo","q":"sotomura hideo ch 6  6  the professor bows out the referee calls for sotomura before the hurdle race  he tries to take an absence for an upset stomach   would it be permissible for me to take an absence  sudou glares him into running   knocking every hurdle is better than disqualification   finish the race at any cost  shouted sudou  the professor answers  egad  o okay  i will    too short for a quote row  clears no hurdles  knocks them all over  finishes last  sudou still credits shibata s first  chickens out of what he barely cleared in practice   the professor s body betrays the name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html#sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p97-1\">Ch.6 §6: the Professor bows out<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.97–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The referee calls for Sotomura before the hurdle race; he tries to take an absence for an upset stomach.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Would it be permissible for me to take an absence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Finish the race at any cost!” shouted Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou glares him into running — knocking every hurdle is better than disqualification.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Professor answers “Egad! O-okay, I will!” — too short for a quote row.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Clears no hurdles, knocks them all over, finishes last; Sudou still credits Shibata’s first.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Chickens out of what he barely cleared in practice — the Professor’s body betrays the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sotomura-hideo-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 6  6  seventh and seventh yukimura grumbles back to camp after a second straight seventh place  downtrodden before the hurdles and flag   seventh and seventh  he grumbled  gets space rather than comfort  then a redirect to the written tests he still plans to ace   i won t fail  but my scores will plummet  said yukimura  wants class a more than anyone  so the burden of a bad sports day sits heavier on him than on most  brings up the rear of the capture the flag offense with ike and ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\">Ch.6 §6: seventh and seventh<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.98–101<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura grumbles back to camp after a second straight seventh place, downtrodden before the hurdles and flag.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Seventh and seventh,” he grumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “I won’t fail, but my scores will plummet.” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets space rather than comfort, then a redirect to the written tests he still plans to ace.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wants Class A more than anyone, so the burden of a bad sports day sits heavier on him than on most.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Brings up the rear of the capture-the-flag offense with Ike and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Hands, votes and the roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: cutting the leader<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p99-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune kinoshita-minori","q":"kinoshita minori ch 6  6  class c s track pair hirata names kinoshita and yajima as class c s fastest   both track and field   in horikita s hurdles group   class c s fastest students are yajima san and kinoshita san from the track and field club  helps push horikita to third in the girls  hurdles  in the obstacle course she bolts to the balance beam  stays second through the net  then tangles with horikita on the final stretch  falls with horikita  kinoshita ends last with a leg injury that stops her running  fast enough to lead an obstacle heat and to drag a rival down in the contact that follows","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p99-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html#sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p99-1\">Ch.6 §6: Class C’s track pair<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.99–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata names Kinoshita and Yajima as Class C’s fastest — both track and field — in Horikita’s hurdles group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Class C’s fastest students are Yajima-san and Kinoshita-san from the track and field club.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Helps push Horikita to third in the girls’ hurdles.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In the obstacle course she bolts to the balance beam, stays second through the net, then tangles with Horikita on the final stretch.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Falls with Horikita; Kinoshita ends last with a leg injury that stops her running.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fast enough to lead an obstacle heat and to drag a rival down in the contact that follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the name that caused the fall<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yajima-mariko-y1v5-p99-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune yajima-mariko","q":"yajima mariko ch 6  6  class c s track pair hirata names yajima and kinoshita as class c s fastest   both from the track and field club   in horikita s hurdles group   class c s fastest students are yajima san and kinoshita san from the track and field club  beats horikita for third in the girls  hurdles   the pair gets ahead of her  in the girls  obstacle course she leads early  kinoshita dashes to the balance beam first and yajima sits second  one of the two who keep horikita off the podium in both races  the obstacle fall drops the whole group  specialized speed that horikita  all round  cannot match in a pure race","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yajima-mariko-y1v5-p99-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: Class C’s track pair<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.99–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yajima-mariko\">Yajima Mariko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata names Yajima and Kinoshita as Class C’s fastest — both from the track and field club — in Horikita’s hurdles group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Class C’s fastest students are Yajima-san and Kinoshita-san from the track and field club.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Beats Horikita for third in the girls’ hurdles — the pair gets ahead of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In the girls’ obstacle course she leads early; Kinoshita dashes to the balance beam first and Yajima sits second.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> One of the two who keep Horikita off the podium in both races; the obstacle fall drops the whole group.<span class=\"pg\">p.99, 113–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Specialized speed that Horikita, all-round, cannot match in a pure race.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yajima-mariko-y1v5-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p100-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken komiya-kyogo","q":"komiya kyogo ch 6  6  passing mention named with sakazaki as one of the class c students from the earlier fight with sudou  assembled for capture the flag  recalled among those involved in the fight that almost got sudou expelled  sakazaki is named on the same page but has no roster row  only komiya is ledgered here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html#sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p100-1\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.100<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Sakazaki as one of the Class C students from the earlier fight with Sudou, assembled for capture the flag.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Recalled among those involved in the fight that almost got Sudou expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakazaki is named on the same page but has no roster row; only Komiya is ledgered here.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 6  6  foul play and the forfeit ryuuen leads class c into the boys  capture the flag against the d a coalition  laughing from the rear like a general  stomps sudou s back as he guards the flag   a low blow the referee culture will call heat of the moment   oh  i didn t notice you  replied ryuuen  he picked up the flag without any hesitation  drops him  takes the flag  and draws a vow of revenge that katsuragi and ayanokoji have to talk down  re forms class c shortest in front into a bow shape after the first tug round loss and threatens them into leverage   if you lose here  i ll kill you  warned ryuuen  lets go of the rope in the third round so the d a side tumbles  calls it a break because they could not win   i decided to take a break  since i thought we couldn t win  said ryuuen   you managed to pick up a meaningless win  is read by katsuragi as wasting their energy and trying to provoke a foul  he turns his back when provocation yields nothing  violence and psychological games are interchangeable tools  even a lost round is a chance to tilt the opponents","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\">Ch.6 §6: foul play and the forfeit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.100–110<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen leads Class C into the boys’ capture the flag against the D/A coalition, laughing from the rear like a general.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Oh, I didn’t notice you,” replied Ryuuen. He picked up the flag without any hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “If you lose here, I’ll kill you,” warned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I decided to take a break, since I thought we couldn’t win,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stomps Sudou’s back as he guards the flag — a low blow the referee culture will call heat-of-the-moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Drops him, takes the flag, and draws a vow of revenge that Katsuragi and Ayanokōji have to talk down.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Re-forms Class C shortest-in-front into a bow shape after the first tug round loss and threatens them into leverage.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lets go of the rope in the third round so the D/A side tumbles; calls it a break because they could not win.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You managed to pick up a meaningless win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Is read by Katsuragi as wasting their energy and trying to provoke a foul; he turns his back when provocation yields nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Violence and psychological games are interchangeable tools; even a lost round is a chance to tilt the opponents.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the cavalry crown and the bait<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamada-albert-y1v5-p100-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken yamada-albert","q":"yamada albert ch 6  6  the flag breaker yamada   large  brawny  half japanese and half black   lines up for class c in capture the flag  goes through sudou on the red flag  his physical mass far surpasses sudou s   who the hell punched me in the stomach  the direct puncher in the chaos while sudou turtles under the flag  ryuuen finishes the job with a stomp  is named by ike mid fight as the half japanese guy going on a rampage  pure mass as a weapon   the class d offensive wall has no one who can match him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamada-albert-y1v5-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the flag-breaker<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.100–104<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yamada-albert\">Yamada Albert<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamada — large, brawny, half-Japanese and half-black — lines up for Class C in capture the flag.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Who the hell punched me in the stomach?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes through Sudou on the Red flag; his physical mass far surpasses Sudou’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The direct puncher in the chaos while Sudou turtles under the flag; Ryuuen finishes the job with a stomp.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Is named by Ike mid-fight as the half-Japanese guy going on a rampage.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pure mass as a weapon — the Class D offensive wall has no one who can match him.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamada-albert-y1v5-p127-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the wall in front of Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y1v5-p106-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu katsuragi-kouhei hashimoto-masayoshi","q":"hashimoto masayoshi ch 6  6  the rebellion on the rope hashimoto steps out of katsuragi s formation as the tug of war lines up and openly doubts class a s slump is katsuragi s fault to fix   what do you mean by that  hashimoto  asked katsuragi   it s your fault that class a is in a slump now  ayanokoji reads his timing as hers   a thin smile from camp and a perfectly aimed challenge  will not obey until katsuragi answers  then grips the rope and pretends cooperation so the referee stays away   you really are blind  huh  katsuragi kun  hashimoto sneered   like you said  it would be ever so annoying if we made you think we weren t cooperating  gentle expression  harsh cynical eyes  the doubt is public  the timing too strange to be his alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hashimoto-masayoshi-y1v5-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the rebellion on the rope<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.106–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hashimoto-masayoshi\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hashimoto steps out of Katsuragi’s formation as the tug-of-war lines up and openly doubts Class A’s slump is Katsuragi’s fault to fix.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> “What do you mean by that, Hashimoto?” asked Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> “It’s your fault that Class A is in a slump now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> “You really are blind, huh, Katsuragi-kun?” Hashimoto sneered.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Ayanokōji reads his timing as hers — a thin smile from camp and a perfectly aimed challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Will not obey until Katsuragi answers; then grips the rope and pretends cooperation so the referee stays away.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Like you said, it would be ever so annoying if we made you think we weren’t cooperating.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gentle expression, harsh cynical eyes; the doubt is public, the timing too strange to be his alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p106-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei hashimoto-masayoshi sakayanagi-arisu","q":"sakayanagi arisu ch 6  6  the thin smile sakayanagi watches from the class a camp while hashimoto s half openly challenges katsuragi s tug of war orders  ayanokoji reads her thin smile as proof she instigated the rebellion   a bid to crush katsuragi  her opposition inside class a  her faction s timing is too strange to be coincidence  katsuragi names her fault if the coalition loses to the bickering  hashimoto s public doubt of katsuragi s strategy is read as her handiwork  she does not need to appear on the rope  unsettling in a different way than ryuuen   no brawl  only a smile and the perfectly timed question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html#sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p106-1\">Ch.6 §6: the thin smile<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.106–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakayanagi watches from the Class A camp while Hashimoto’s half openly challenges Katsuragi’s tug-of-war orders.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hashimoto-masayoshi\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Ayanokōji reads her thin smile as proof she instigated the rebellion — a bid to crush Katsuragi, her opposition inside Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Her faction’s timing is too strange to be coincidence; Katsuragi names her fault if the coalition loses to the bickering.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Hashimoto’s public doubt of Katsuragi’s strategy is read as her handiwork; she does not need to appear on the rope.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Unsettling in a different way than Ryuuen — no brawl, only a smile and the perfectly timed question.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakayanagi-arisu-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Rumored from a distance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p107-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu hashimoto-masayoshi totsuka-yahiko","q":"totsuka yahiko ch 6  6  shouting for katsuragi yahiko  from katsuragi s faction  answers hashimoto s half by thrusting the rope at a rebel   hurry up and do it   enough with the shameful behavior  yahiko  from katsuragi s faction  shouted at sakayanagi s faction  rallies for katsuragi s order when half of class a refuses to move  directs the shout at sakayanagi s faction across the rope  faces hashimoto s group as the visible counterweight inside class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p107-1\">Ch.6 §6: shouting for Katsuragi<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yahiko, from Katsuragi’s faction, answers Hashimoto’s half by thrusting the rope at a rebel.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#hashimoto-masayoshi\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Hurry up and do it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Enough with the shameful behavior!” Yahiko, from Katsuragi’s faction, shouted at Sakayanagi’s faction.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Rallies for Katsuragi’s order when half of Class A refuses to move.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Directs the shout at Sakayanagi’s faction across the rope.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Faces Hashimoto’s group as the visible counterweight inside Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-nomura-yuuji-y1v5-p111-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken nomura-yuuji","q":"nomura yuji ch 6  6  passing mention named in the obstacle course heat draw as one of the class c runners lined up against sudou  with suzuki  counted especially unathletic   part of why sudou s win looks guaranteed  ike names the pair  no action of nomura s own is shown on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-nomura-yuuji-y1v5-p111-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#nomura-yuuji\">Nomura Yūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the obstacle-course heat draw as one of the Class C runners lined up against Sudou.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> With Suzuki, counted especially unathletic — part of why Sudou’s win looks guaranteed.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike names the pair; no action of Nomura’s own is shown on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-suzuki-hidetoshi-y1v5-p111-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken suzuki-hidetoshi","q":"suzuki hidetoshi ch 6  6  passing mention named in the obstacle course heat draw as one of the class c runners lined up against sudou  with nomura  counted especially unathletic   part of why sudou s win looks guaranteed  ike names the pair  no action of suzuki s own is shown on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-suzuki-hidetoshi-y1v5-p111-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.111<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#suzuki-hidetoshi\">Suzuki Hidetoshi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the obstacle-course heat draw as one of the Class C runners lined up against Sudou.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> With Nomura, counted especially unathletic — part of why Sudou’s win looks guaranteed.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike names the pair; no action of Suzuki’s own is shown on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"sports festival ch 6  6 7 6 10  afternoon rules and the morning s end second half runs three legged through cavalry to the lunch break that ends the morning half  three legged  two people per team  only four teams run at once  races follow one another like a live television program  cavalry  three minute period  points from enemy units defeated and allied units remaining  four horsemen per unit  each horseman fifty points  each class s  general  one hundred  a stolen headband scores even if the opponent stands  knocking down a jockey in cavalry counts as a self ko  not a headband steal   the fifty points vanish  absentees in an event are disqualified and earn no points  the show goes on  morning half ends at the lunch break  the contests will run in reverse order in the second half  three legged first and boys  cavalry spearhead before the punch removes him from the board  girls  cavalry win for b c  boys  cavalry win for class c alone  then first in the 200 metre dash  third injured student of the day  her rankings fall across every event after the obstacle fall","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html#sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6.7–6.10: afternoon rules and the morning’s end<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–143<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/sports-festival.html\">Sports Festival<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second half runs three-legged through cavalry to the lunch break that ends the morning half.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Three-legged: two people per team, only four teams run at once; races follow one another like a live television program.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Cavalry: three-minute period; points from enemy units defeated and allied units remaining; four horsemen per unit; each horseman fifty points, each class’s “general” one hundred; a stolen headband scores even if the opponent stands.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Knocking down a jockey in cavalry counts as a self-KO, not a headband steal — the fifty points vanish.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Absentees in an event are disqualified and earn no points; the show goes on.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Morning half ends at the lunch break; the contests will run in reverse order in the second half.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Three-legged first and boys’ cavalry spearhead before the punch removes him from the board.<span class=\"pg\">p.115, 123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Girls’ cavalry win for B/C, boys’ cavalry win for Class C alone, then first in the 200-metre dash.<span class=\"pg\">p.123, 128, 135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Third injured student of the day; her rankings fall across every event after the obstacle fall.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sports-festival-y1v5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the festival runs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  6 7 6 10  observation  cavalry  and the plan second half opens mid conversation with injured horikita after the obstacle fall  ayanokoji then runs three legged  watches the cavalry battles  confronts the leak with karuizawa  and sends horikita after sudou  learns kinoshita called horikita s name to force the collision  notes horikita has thirty points to his twenty seven   i ll do everything i can  watches sudou carry ike to three legged first  then pairs with hirata for their own first place  sees horikita and kushida fade to last in the girls  three legged as the leg injury tells  later names the stack of hard matchups as deliberate  stays through the ten minute break observing class a s two faction split and asks hirata what kind of student sakayanagi is   amazing that they ve gotten this far with such internal discord  reads her silence and single focus on katsuragi as willingness to lose points for his downfall  serves as a right side horse under hirata s jockey in the boys  cavalry  holds position while sudou crashes the line and hirata twice grabs ryuuen s headband  watches the one on one bait take sudou  then the hair gel trick that makes the stolen headband unprovable  explains the leak  the fixed matchups and the horikita crush to karuizawa  answers  no intention of winning  with  do nothing   she s being targeted   win  i have no intention of winning  keeps distance while sudou punches hirata and walks off  tells karuizawa the mess has nothing to do with him  takes third in the 200 metre dash  then delivers the  burden  and  weapon  confrontation that is meant to wake horikita and send her for sudou   you re nothing but a burden   how long do you plan to be useless  horikita   i m calling you useless because you are useless  calls her useless on purpose so she will reclaim sudou as her asset for class a s climb  at lunch he lies to hirata and karuizawa that the traitor acts on horikita s orders  the morning ends with horikita and sudou both missing   i ve taken stock of the traitor s moral fiber   yeah  everything is going according to horikita s plan  runs a deliberate double game  full analysis for his inner circle  controlled misinformation for the class  and one surgical pressure campaign on horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6.7–6.10: observation, cavalry, and the plan<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second half opens mid-conversation with injured Horikita after the obstacle fall; Ayanokōji then runs three-legged, watches the cavalry battles, confronts the leak with Karuizawa, and sends Horikita after Sudou.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’ll do everything I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Amazing that they’ve gotten this far with such internal discord,”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “She’s being targeted,”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Learns Kinoshita called Horikita’s name to force the collision; notes Horikita has thirty points to his twenty-seven.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Watches Sudou carry Ike to three-legged first, then pairs with Hirata for their own first place.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sees Horikita and Kushida fade to last in the girls’ three-legged as the leg injury tells; later names the stack of hard matchups as deliberate.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays through the ten-minute break observing Class A’s two-faction split and asks Hirata what kind of student Sakayanagi is.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119, §6.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reads her silence and single focus on Katsuragi as willingness to lose points for his downfall.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Serves as a right-side horse under Hirata’s jockey in the boys’ cavalry; holds position while Sudou crashes the line and Hirata twice grabs Ryuuen’s headband.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–129, §6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Watches the one-on-one bait take Sudou, then the hair-gel trick that makes the stolen headband unprovable.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Explains the leak, the fixed matchups and the Horikita crush to Karuizawa; answers “no intention of winning” with “do nothing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Win? I have no intention of winning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps distance while Sudou punches Hirata and walks off; tells Karuizawa the mess has nothing to do with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes third in the 200-metre dash, then delivers the “burden” and “weapon” confrontation that is meant to wake Horikita and send her for Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–139, §6.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re nothing but a burden.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How long do you plan to be useless, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m calling you useless because you are useless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her useless on purpose so she will reclaim Sudou as her asset for Class A’s climb.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> At lunch he lies to Hirata and Karuizawa that the traitor acts on Horikita’s orders; the morning ends with Horikita and Sudou both missing.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–142, §6.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve taken stock of the traitor’s moral fiber,”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Everything is going according to Horikita’s plan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs a deliberate double game: full analysis for his inner circle, controlled misinformation for the class, and one surgical pressure campaign on Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: festival day, first events<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7: the beatdown already landed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru chabashira-sae hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 6  6  jockey  victim  cover hirata ties legs with ayanokoji for the boys  three legged and worries about horikita s injury between races   how s horikita san doing   it s pretty serious  partners ayanokoji to three legged first  the girls cheer only for him  watches the horikita kushida pair fade  later takes the cavalry jockey seat for the boys  describes sakayanagi to ayanokoji   polite  mature  but class a calls her aggressive and ruthless   so  you re also curious about her  ayanokouji kun   she s very polite  she s good with people  and she s mature  jockeys the strongest d unit  merges with class a on his plan  twice snags the edge of ryuuen s headband  then loses his own   i have an idea  if it s okay with you guys   sorry  my hand was slippery   ugh  sorry  sudou kun  fall back for now   sorry  sudou kun  his headband was so strangely wet  i couldn t seem to pull it off  first to feel the wet headband  later tells ryuuen the leak is known and promises something interesting before the day ends  blocks sudou s charge  is punched to the ground  and covers for him in front of chabashira   i understand what you re saying  sudou kun  but you need to calm down   you know what ll happen if you get violent with ryuuen kun   no  that s not it  sensei  i just fell down  that s all   well  you d be wrong to think he hit me  look  i fell  so there shouldn t be a problem  convinces her to log a preventative report rather than a violence case  confronts ryuuen with the stolen participation table and the weak opponent pattern   it looks like the only reason you ve come in first is because you went up against much weaker people  you re quite lucky  ryuuen kun   you got class d s participation table  and you obtained detailed information about all our students  athletic abilities  too   i just have one thing to say to you  pulls ike and yamauchi into the lunch circle with karuizawa and ayanokoji  presses the traitor question and accepts the horikita orders story   okay  i won t hound you   and this is all on horikita s orders  right  ayanokouji kun   yeah  we re relying on sudou kun  absorbs the punch without exposing sudou  keeps class a cooperation intact  and is the only peer ryuuen s taunts cannot rattle into a mistake","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6: jockey, victim, cover<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata ties legs with Ayanokōji for the boys’ three-legged and worries about Horikita’s injury between races.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “How’s Horikita-san doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “It’s pretty serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “So, you’re also curious about her, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Partners Ayanokōji to three-legged first; the girls cheer only for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Watches the Horikita–Kushida pair fade; later takes the cavalry jockey seat for the boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Describes Sakayanagi to Ayanokōji — polite, mature, but Class A calls her aggressive and ruthless.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119, §6.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s very polite, she’s good with people, and she’s mature.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jockeys the strongest D unit; merges with Class A on his plan, twice snags the edge of Ryuuen’s headband, then loses his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–128, §6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have an idea, if it’s okay with you guys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. My hand was slippery!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ugh! Sorry, Sudou-kun! Fall back for now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, Sudou-kun. His headband was so strangely wet, I couldn’t seem to pull it off,”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> First to feel the wet headband; later tells Ryuuen the leak is known and promises something interesting before the day ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Blocks Sudou’s charge, is punched to the ground, and covers for him in front of Chabashira.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what you’re saying, Sudou-kun, but you need to calm down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know what’ll happen if you get violent with Ryuuen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s not it, sensei. I just fell down, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you’d be wrong to think he hit me. Look, I fell, so there shouldn’t be a problem,”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Convinces her to log a preventative report rather than a violence case.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Confronts Ryuuen with the stolen participation table and the weak-opponent pattern.<span class=\"pg\">p.135, §6.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It looks like the only reason you’ve come in first is because you went up against much weaker people. You’re quite lucky, Ryuuen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You got Class D’s participation table, and you obtained detailed information about all our students’ athletic abilities, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just have one thing to say to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pulls Ike and Yamauchi into the lunch circle with Karuizawa and Ayanokōji; presses the traitor question and accepts the Horikita-orders story.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–142, §6.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I won’t hound you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And this is all on Horikita’s orders, right, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. We’re relying on Sudou-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Absorbs the punch without exposing Sudou, keeps Class A cooperation intact, and is the only peer Ryuuen’s taunts cannot rattle into a mistake.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: steady hands<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8: pays for substitutes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"kinoshita-minori kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio ryuuen-kakeru horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6  injury  cavalry  and the wake up call horikita sits with her injured leg after the obstacle fall and tells ayanokoji the collision was no accident   that girl s a sneak   while she was running behind me  she called my name over and over  names the girl behind her as the one who called her name  later  p 137  allows kinoshita may have been told to trip her   i ll participate  even if i have to crawl  pairs with kushida in the girls  three legged  second early  then last as the stiff leg and an obstructing line do the rest  the odd pair looks safe to class d but finishes last  sudou s  go  suzune  does not reach them  leaves for the nurse s office for a poultice during the ten minute break  jockeys class d in the girls  cavalry with ishizaki  komiya and kondou as horses  class c s four horsemen take her alone and snatch her headband  ibuki  also a jockey  issues the order and heads straight for her  is the sole target of the b c attack   ryuuen s plan to break her  not merely to score   that doesn t change the fact that i lost   i d expect no less of you  stares at her brother from a distance she cannot close while the upperclassmen s cavalry runs  keeps watching the president through the second  and third year events with no way to approach  is told she is useless and a burden  then pressed to choose her own ranking or sudou s return  the  weapon  speech is the pivot   that s an awful thing to say   clearly  we have a traitor who leaked our participation table to ryuuen kun   i guess he told kinoshita san to trip me   on what grounds do you call me useless   how dare you  i m a highly capable student and athlete  pride and injury together  she will not withdraw  will not accept the crash as luck once pressed  and is finally pushed toward acting for the class rather than only for her rank  skips lunch and leaves   perhaps for sudou   after ayanokoji s words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6: injury, cavalry, and the wake-up call<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–138<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita sits with her injured leg after the obstacle fall and tells Ayanokōji the collision was no accident.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That girl’s a sneak.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “While she was running behind me, she called my name over and over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’ll participate, even if I have to crawl,”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> Names the girl behind her as the one who called her name; later (p.137) allows Kinoshita may have been told to trip her.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pairs with Kushida in the girls’ three-legged; second early, then last as the stiff leg and an obstructing line do the rest.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The odd pair looks safe to Class D but finishes last; Sudou’s “Go, Suzune!” does not reach them.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Leaves for the nurse’s office for a poultice during the ten-minute break.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jockeys Class D in the girls’ cavalry with Ishizaki, Komiya and Kondou as horses; Class C’s four horsemen take her alone and snatch her headband.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123, §6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Ibuki, also a jockey, issues the order and heads straight for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Is the sole target of the B/C attack — Ryuuen’s plan to break her, not merely to score.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That doesn’t change the fact that I lost.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d expect no less of you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stares at her brother from a distance she cannot close while the upperclassmen’s cavalry runs.<span class=\"pg\">p.135, §6.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Keeps watching the president through the second- and third-year events with no way to approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Is told she is useless and a burden, then pressed to choose her own ranking or Sudou’s return; the “weapon” speech is the pivot.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s an awful thing to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Clearly, we have a traitor who leaked our participation table to Ryuuen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess he told Kinoshita-san to trip me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “On what grounds do you call me useless?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How dare you? I’m a highly capable student and athlete.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pride and injury together: she will not withdraw, will not accept the crash as luck once pressed, and is finally pushed toward acting for the class rather than only for her rank.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Skips lunch and leaves — perhaps for Sudou — after Ayanokōji’s words.<span class=\"pg\">p.140, §6.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: races, Kōenji, and the fall<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7: alone after the beatdown<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 6  6  carried  then lunch ike is sudou s three legged partner and spends the race being practically dragged to first  ike cried in agony during the forced carry to first  nabbed first place by sudou s forced carry  watches the girls  three legged from the side  body as ballast for sudou s strength  later cowers with the others when sudou s temper peaks  shouts at the girls  cavalry as class c zeroes in on horikita   h hey  what the hell   they re just going after horikita  aren t they  dude   dude  this is an awesome game  loses rock paper scissors for lunch duty with yamauchi and shows no interest in finding sudou   gah  god  i m so tired  why do i gotta suffer through this  dude  he and yamauchi have known sudou since day one and will not chase him  most girls who saw the punch have dropped any goodwill  paired for the lunch run  joins hirata s ten person eating group without caring about sudou","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6: carried, then lunch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–141<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike is Sudou’s three-legged partner and spends the race being practically dragged to first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “H-hey, what the hell?”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “They’re just going after Horikita, aren’t they, dude?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Dude, this is an awesome game!”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike cried in agony during the forced carry to first.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Nabbed first place by Sudou’s forced carry; watches the girls’ three-legged from the side.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Body as ballast for Sudou’s strength; later cowers with the others when Sudou’s temper peaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shouts at the girls’ cavalry as Class C zeroes in on Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.120, §6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Loses rock-paper-scissors for lunch duty with Yamauchi and shows no interest in finding Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.140, §6.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Gah! God, I’m so tired! Why do I gotta suffer through this, dude?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He and Yamauchi have known Sudou since day one and will not chase him; most girls who saw the punch have dropped any goodwill.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Paired for the lunch run; joins Hirata’s ten-person eating group without caring about Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: loud from the sidelines<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8: scavenger-hunt substitute<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kinoshita-minori","q":"kinoshita minori ch 6  6  the name that caused the fall horikita names the girl behind her in the obstacle fall   the one who called her name until she turned  called her name over and over so that looking back produced the collision  horikita calls it a sneak s move   while she was running behind me  she called my name over and over  horikita allows kinoshita may have been told to trip her  while doubting a blatant injury plot under scrutiny  the trip is horikita s speculation to ayanokoji  not a confession on kinoshita s page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html#sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6: the name that caused the fall<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–137<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita names the girl behind her in the obstacle fall — the one who called her name until she turned.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “While she was running behind me, she called my name over and over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Called her name over and over so that looking back produced the collision; Horikita calls it a sneak’s move.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Horikita allows Kinoshita may have been told to trip her, while doubting a blatant injury plot under scrutiny.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The trip is Horikita’s speculation to Ayanokōji, not a confession on Kinoshita’s page.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p99-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: Class C’s track pair<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: the accusation from the bed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru yamada-albert yukimura-teruhiko sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 6  6  first place  bait  and the punch sudou runs the boys  three legged with ike  practically carrying him  and takes first  carries ike across the line  hirata and ayanokoji follow with their own first of the day  ike cried in agony as sudou bolted with him  the pair still nabbed first  sudou calls out  go  suzune  during the girls  three legged   the still forbidden first name  safely out of horikita s earshot  cheeks her first name  then volunteers to get class c back for her after the cavalry loss   hey  don t worry  bout it  it was hopeless   leave it to me  i ll get  em back for you  anchors the boys  cavalry at the centre of hirata s unit  smashes through class b  then takes ryuuen s one on one bait and rejects katsuragi s pincer   aim for that shitty ryuuen s head   oh  i remember your name  sudou  bites the one on one offer  threatens katsuragi s unit if he interferes  then loses when the sticky headband kills hirata s grip   fine  don t forget what you just said  ryuuen   stick your nose in this  and i ll bust up your unit  cannot break through yamada  whose strength matches his own  confronts ryuuen over the hair gel  evidence already gone   that s foul play  you slathered your headband with something  storms class c after the provocation stack  shoves hirata aside  and punches him down in front of the class   i m seriously going to beat the crap out of that jerk   shut it  he s the one who should be sorry   i m the leader here  so  listen up  hirata  let s confront ryuuen together   so what if i did  what then   whatever  do what you want  go ahead and lose for all i care  you scum  this sports festival thing can go to hell  walks off toward the dormitory  absent for the rest of the morning half   koenji gone  sudou gone  is cut by yukimura for showboating before the punch lands on hirata instead  peak athlete and worst crisis in one body  three individual wins  then a single swing that removes the class s ace from the board","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p115-1\">Ch.6 §6: first place, bait, and the punch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–135<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou runs the boys’ three-legged with Ike, practically carrying him, and takes first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yamada-albert\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Hey, don’t worry ’bout it. It was hopeless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Leave it to me. I’ll get ’em back for you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Aim for that shitty Ryuuen’s head!”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Carries Ike across the line; Hirata and Ayanokōji follow with their own first of the day.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike cried in agony as Sudou bolted with him; the pair still nabbed first.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou calls out “Go, Suzune!” during the girls’ three-legged — the still-forbidden first name, safely out of Horikita’s earshot.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Cheeks her first name, then volunteers to get Class C back for her after the cavalry loss.<span class=\"pg\">p.116, 123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Anchors the boys’ cavalry at the centre of Hirata’s unit; smashes through Class B, then takes Ryuuen’s one-on-one bait and rejects Katsuragi’s pincer.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–128, §6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I remember your name. Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Bites the one-on-one offer, threatens Katsuragi’s unit if he interferes, then loses when the sticky headband kills Hirata’s grip.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. Don’t forget what you just said, Ryuuen!”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stick your nose in this, and I’ll bust up your unit!”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Cannot break through Yamada, whose strength matches his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Confronts Ryuuen over the hair gel; evidence already gone.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s foul play! You slathered your headband with something!”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Storms Class C after the provocation stack, shoves Hirata aside, and punches him down in front of the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m seriously going to beat the crap out of that jerk!”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shut it! He’s the one who should be sorry!”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m the leader here! So, listen up, Hirata. Let’s confront Ryuuen together,”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what if I did? What then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever, do what you want. Go ahead and lose for all I care, you scum. This sports festival thing can go to hell,”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks off toward the dormitory; absent for the rest of the morning half — Kōenji gone, Sudou gone.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Is cut by Yukimura for showboating before the punch lands on Hirata instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Peak athlete and worst crisis in one body: three individual wins, then a single swing that removes the class’s ace from the board.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the leader’s festival<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.1: the lobby lecture<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p116-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6  6  compromise partner and searcher kushida pairs with horikita in the girls  three legged   always willing to compromise against horikita s grudge  takes the lead when horikita s leg stiffens  the pair drops to last after a brief second and an obstructing lane change  the bizarre pair looks safe to class d and fails on the field  neither bridges the gap  abstains from lunch  tells other girls she is going to look for sudou  and leaves  one of the two girls who go searching while ike and yamauchi refuse to  her search is reported  not shown  before the chapter closes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p116-1\">Ch.6 §6: compromise partner and searcher<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.116–140<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida pairs with Horikita in the girls’ three-legged — always willing to compromise against Horikita’s grudge.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Takes the lead when Horikita’s leg stiffens; the pair drops to last after a brief second and an obstructing lane change.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Abstains from lunch, tells other girls she is going to look for Sudou, and leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.140, §6.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The bizarre pair looks safe to Class D and fails on the field; neither bridges the gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> One of the two girls who go searching while Ike and Yamauchi refuse to.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her search is reported, not shown, before the chapter closes.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: “It’s me”<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p145-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7: fetches Horikita, admits she told the teacher<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yajima-mariko-y1v5-p116-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune yajima-mariko","q":"yajima mariko ch 6  6  passing mention named in the class c team that takes second in the first year girls  three legged race  part of the pair that finishes ahead of horikita and kushida in that heat  no separate action beyond the team result on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yajima-mariko-y1v5-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yajima-mariko\">Yajima Mariko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the Class C team that takes second in the first-year girls’ three-legged race.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Part of the pair that finishes ahead of Horikita and Kushida in that heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No separate action beyond the team result on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yajima-mariko-y1v5-p99-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: Class C’s track pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p119-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 6  6  fair play under the smile ichinose and class b are watched enjoying the festival   cheerful and fair while c and a scheme  as class b s cavalry general she blocks karuizawa s rescue of horikita and holds the collision course until the melee  direct fight   unity versus manoeuvrability   that drags on while class c finishes horikita  does not join the four on one  class b still supports its ally team  unlike class a s sit out  genuinely enjoying the games while playing them straight   the text s contrast with ryuuen s psychological war","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p119-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p119-1\">Ch.6 §6: fair play under the smile<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.119–123<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose and Class B are watched enjoying the festival — cheerful and fair while C and A scheme.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">As Class B’s cavalry general she blocks Karuizawa’s rescue of Horikita and holds the collision course until the melee.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123, §6.8<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Direct fight — unity versus manoeuvrability — that drags on while Class C finishes Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Does not join the four-on-one; Class B still supports its ally team, unlike Class A’s sit-out.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Genuinely enjoying the games while playing them straight — the text’s contrast with Ryuuen’s psychological war.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: the Class B three-legged pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ibuki mio ch 6  6  the order on horikita ibuki rides as a class b c jockey in the girls  cavalry and singles out horikita  issues an order and heads straight for horikita   first of the four horsemen to commit  personal rivalry continues off the track  she is out for blood against the same girl she lost to in the dash  her charge fits ryuuen s plan even if the text does not say she was ordered by name for this moment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p120-1\">Ch.6 §6: the order on Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki rides as a Class B/C jockey in the girls’ cavalry and singles out Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Issues an order and heads straight for Horikita — first of the four horsemen to commit.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Personal rivalry continues off the track: she is out for blood against the same girl she lost to in the dash.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Her charge fits Ryuuen’s plan even if the text does not say she was ordered by name for this moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v5-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the rivalry heat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi","q":"ishizaki daichi ch 6  6  passing mention named as one of the three class d horsemen supporting horikita s jockey in the girls  cavalry  horse under her  the unit is called not bad at all before class c s focus fire  no separate action is shown for him on these pages beyond the formation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the three Class D horsemen supporting Horikita’s jockey in the girls’ cavalry.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horse under her; the unit is called not bad at all before Class C’s focus fire.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No separate action is shown for him on these pages beyond the formation.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 6  6  rescue  leak  lunch karuizawa jockeys a class d cavalry unit and first moves to horikita s rescue when class c attacks her alone  rushes with shinohara  blocked by ichinose s general unit  ends in an eight to one scrape and snatches one headband at the end  direct collision   unity versus manoeuvrability   while class a sits out  rescues her too late  after the loss says horikita s opponents were simply too much  calls ayanokoji  kiyotaka  and opens the leak conversation  connects the fixed matchups to the traitor   isn t this bad news  kiyotaka   why  well  i call yousuke kun by his first name  so i thought i d try using yours   targeted  so  it s not accidental that she keeps facing all these incredible students   so  information about our class got leaked  someone sent out our participation table   what  i don t like her  she s all high and mighty and full of herself   well maybe i kinda understand what she s dealing with  gets the full ryuuen targeting theory  is told nothing can be done and that the plan is to do nothing  joins the lunch circle  presses for the traitor s name  and accepts that sudou s return now rides on horikita   so  who s the traitor  you know  don t you  yousuke kun   wait  the traitor might be someone nearby  right  it might even be someone among us right now  uses the first name opening as intimacy  then switches to class survival mode   the bullying history lets her read horikita s targeting without liking her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p120-1\">Ch.6 §6: rescue, leak, lunch<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Karuizawa jockeys a Class D cavalry unit and first moves to Horikita’s rescue when Class C attacks her alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Isn’t this bad news, Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Why? Well, I call Yousuke-kun by his first name, so I thought I’d try using yours,”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Targeted? So, it’s not accidental that she keeps facing all these incredible students?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Rushes with Shinohara; blocked by Ichinose’s general unit; ends in an eight-to-one scrape and snatches one headband at the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123, §6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Direct collision — unity versus manoeuvrability — while Class A sits out.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Rescues her too late; after the loss says Horikita’s opponents were simply too much.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Ayanokōji “Kiyotaka” and opens the leak conversation; connects the fixed matchups to the traitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–132, after cavalry<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, information about our class got leaked? Someone sent out our participation table?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? I don’t like her. She’s all high and mighty and full of herself,”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well…maybe I kinda understand what she’s dealing with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets the full Ryuuen-targeting theory; is told nothing can be done and that the plan is to do nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Joins the lunch circle, presses for the traitor’s name, and accepts that Sudou’s return now rides on Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–142, §6.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, who’s the traitor? You know, don’t you, Yousuke-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. The traitor might be someone nearby, right? It might even be someone among us right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Uses the first-name opening as intimacy, then switches to class-survival mode — the bullying history lets her read Horikita’s targeting without liking her.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Named in passing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune komiya-kyogo","q":"komiya kyogo ch 6  6  passing mention named as one of the three class d horsemen supporting horikita s jockey in the girls  cavalry  horse under her  the unit holds until four enemy horsemen commit to the jockey  no separate action is shown for him on these pages beyond the formation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html#sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p120-1\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the three Class D horsemen supporting Horikita’s jockey in the girls’ cavalry.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horse under her; the unit holds until four enemy horsemen commit to the jockey.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No separate action is shown for him on these pages beyond the formation.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v5-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kondou-reo-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kondou-reo","q":"kondo reo ch 6  6  passing mention named as one of the three class d horsemen supporting horikita s jockey in the girls  cavalry  horse under her  the unit is named as not bad before the sole target attack  no separate action is shown for him on these pages beyond the formation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kondou-reo-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kondou-reo\">Kondō Reo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the three Class D horsemen supporting Horikita’s jockey in the girls’ cavalry.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horse under her; the unit is named as not bad before the sole-target attack.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No separate action is shown for him on these pages beyond the formation.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mori-nene-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune mori-nene","q":"mori nene ch 6  6  the weak general mori jockeys a class d girls  cavalry unit built around unathletic students  her unit s strategy is to make the weak horseman the general so the three others can protect them   the weak link stays out of the fight  one of the three named jockeys with horikita and kushida  her unit is expected to go down first  the roster logic that turns weakness into a scoring shell   visible class d tactic under fire","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mori-nene-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the weak general<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#mori-nene\">Mori Nene<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mori jockeys a Class D girls’ cavalry unit built around unathletic students.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Her unit’s strategy is to make the weak horseman the general so the three others can protect them — the weak link stays out of the fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> One of the three named jockeys with Horikita and Kushida; her unit is expected to go down first.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The roster logic that turns weakness into a scoring shell — visible Class D tactic under fire.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-mori-nene-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: On the scavenger-hunt roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 6  6  the cavalry crown and the bait ryuuen s class c horsemen ignore class a and take horikita alone in the girls  cavalry   the crush plan made visible  orders the four on one  class c wipes the remaining a d units after her headband falls  sole target  ayanokoji reads it as humiliation for its own sake  not points  rides as class c s general on yamada s power  absorbs sudou s hits  wins the one on one bait  and keeps the sticky headband secret   oh  i remember your name  sudou   oh  i guess this is all meaningless  unless we settle things one onone   if you can only beat me when it s two against one  i suppose that s that   tough words  but with nothing to back them up   if you re so very strong  then face me one on one  studies him  offers the kneel  then wins when hirata s grip fails on the treated cloth   i don t know what you re talking about   if there s anything on my headband  it s probably just hair gel  don t be a sore loser  approaches the tent to ask after sudou while knowing exactly what happened  takes first in the 200 metre dash   hirata  what happened to sudou  he taking a dump   heh  i really don t think lying suits you  is told the leak is known  answers that the class gap fills d with despair and looks forward to hirata s  something interesting   guess luck is on my side   ooh  i d be scared if that weren t such an obvious bluff  psychological harm over raw score  target the leader  bait the hot head  poison the cloth  then smile through the accusation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\">Ch.6 §6: the cavalry crown and the bait<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120–136<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen’s Class C horsemen ignore Class A and take Horikita alone in the girls’ cavalry — the crush plan made visible.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Oh, I remember your name. Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Oh? I guess this is all meaningless, unless we settle things one-onone,”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “If you can only beat me when it’s two against one, I suppose that’s that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Orders the four-on-one; Class C wipes the remaining A/D units after her headband falls.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sole target; Ayanokōji reads it as humiliation for its own sake, not points.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123, 130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Rides as Class C’s general on Yamada’s power; absorbs Sudou’s hits, wins the one-on-one bait, and keeps the sticky headband secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–129, boys’ cavalry<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tough words, but with nothing to back them up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re so very strong, then face me one-on-one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Studies him, offers the kneel, then wins when Hirata’s grip fails on the treated cloth.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s anything on my headband, it’s probably just hair gel. Don’t be a sore loser,”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Approaches the tent to ask after Sudou while knowing exactly what happened; takes first in the 200-metre dash.<span class=\"pg\">p.135, §6.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata, what happened to Sudou? He taking a dump?”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. I really don’t think lying suits you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Is told the leak is known; answers that the class gap fills D with despair and looks forward to Hirata’s “something interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Guess luck is on my side.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ooh. I’d be scared if that weren’t such an obvious bluff.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Psychological harm over raw score: target the leader, bait the hot head, poison the cloth, then smile through the accusation.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: foul play and the forfeit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: arrives at the infirmary<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p121-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei shinohara-satsuki","q":"shinohara satsuki ch 6  6  passing mention shinohara hurries over to support karuizawa s rescue ride in the girls  cavalry  second rider in the support dash that ichinose s unit intercepts  no further action shown for her on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html#sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p121-1\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.121<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shinohara hurries over to support Karuizawa’s rescue ride in the girls’ cavalry.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Second rider in the support dash that Ichinose’s unit intercepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No further action shown for her on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Objects to the ability plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p123-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 6  6  the abandoned rescue and the pincer class a s cavalry units sit out the attack on horikita and only re engage after her headband falls  after horikita s loss  class a and class c wipe the rest of the a d side  katsuragi s group takes down shibata and kanzaki s unit later in the boys  match  class a shows no sign of helping her   ayanokoji suspects bait and swoop  offers the two on one pincer while sudou is being baited  sudou threatens his unit if he interferes   what are you talking about  we can t let this chance go  we should use a pincer attack to defeat him  loses the argument  watches the one on one unfold with a bitter expression  receives hirata s merge plan and the order to rush ryuuen  later exchanges the look that seals the last surround  willing to trade d s pain for a s points until the coalition s own units are at stake   the split with sakayanagi still reading from the camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html#sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p123-1\">Ch.6 §6: the abandoned rescue and the pincer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.123–126<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class A’s cavalry units sit out the attack on Horikita and only re-engage after her headband falls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “What are you talking about? We can’t let this chance go. We should use a pincer attack to defeat him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Horikita’s loss, Class A and Class C wipe the rest of the A/D side; Katsuragi’s group takes down Shibata and Kanzaki’s unit later in the boys’ match.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Class A shows no sign of helping her — Ayanokōji suspects bait-and-swoop.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Offers the two-on-one pincer while Sudou is being baited; Sudou threatens his unit if he interferes.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Loses the argument; watches the one-on-one unfold with a bitter expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Receives Hirata’s merge plan and the order to rush Ryuuen; later exchanges the look that seals the last surround.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Willing to trade D’s pain for A’s points until the coalition’s own units are at stake — the split with Sakayanagi still reading from the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: Class A’s split on the field<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-miyake-akito-y1v5-p123-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken miyake-akito","q":"miyake akito ch 6  6  left side horse miyake takes the left of ayanokoji s unit in the boys  cavalry   sudou centre  ayanokoji right  miyake left  hirata jockey  supports the jockey from the side  with ayanokoji has maybe half sudou s power against ryuuen s wall  rides in the class s strongest unit  cannot match sudou s crashes but holds the formation  yamada s power is called equal to sudou s while miyake and ayanokoji together are only about half of sudou each","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-miyake-akito-y1v5-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: left-side horse<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.123–127<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#miyake-akito\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Miyake takes the left of Ayanokōji’s unit in the boys’ cavalry — Sudou centre, Ayanokōji right, Miyake left, Hirata jockey.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Supports the jockey from the side; with Ayanokōji has maybe half Sudou’s power against Ryuuen’s wall.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Rides in the class’s strongest unit; cannot match Sudou’s crashes but holds the formation.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yamada’s power is called equal to Sudou’s while Miyake and Ayanokōji together are only about half of Sudou each.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-miyake-akito-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Grip strength and the tug-of-war order<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p124-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"shibata-sou ryuuen-kakeru kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji ch 6  6  cavalry horse under a class b general kanzaki rides in the class b general s cavalry unit against the merged d a mass in the boys  match  that unit is taken down by katsuragi and other class a students after three of their own fall  rides with shibata under the same class b general   one of the two units the coalition must clear before ryuuen  left as sole enemy after this unit and shibata s fall  the d a surround begins","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p124-1\">Ch.6 §6: cavalry horse under a Class B general<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.124–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kanzaki rides in the Class B general’s cavalry unit against the merged D/A mass in the boys’ match.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">That unit is taken down by Katsuragi and other Class A students after three of their own fall.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Rides with Shibata under the same Class B general — one of the two units the coalition must clear before Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Left as sole enemy after this unit and Shibata’s fall; the D/A surround begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the chats at the line<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p124-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru shibata-sou","q":"shibata so ch 6  6  cavalry horse under a class b general shibata rides in the class b general s cavalry unit against the merged d a mass in the boys  match  that unit is taken down by katsuragi and other class a students after three of their own fall  rides with kanzaki under the same class b general  his fall leaves ryuuen alone for the final surround","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p124-1\">Ch.6 §6: cavalry horse under a Class B general<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.124–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shibata rides in the Class B general’s cavalry unit against the merged D/A mass in the boys’ match.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">That unit is taken down by Katsuragi and other Class A students after three of their own fall.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Rides with Kanzaki under the same Class B general.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His fall leaves Ryuuen alone for the final surround.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: Sudou’s rival on the clock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: Ichinose’s three-legged partner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamada-albert-y1v5-p127-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken ryuuen-kakeru yamada-albert","q":"yamada albert ch 6  6  the wall in front of ryuuen yamada albert is the half japanese horse protecting ryuuen at the centre of class c s cavalry unit  his strength is incredible  just like the rumors had said   equal to sudou s  sudou cannot break him  yamada and the other riders hold while ryuuen conserves energy  the body that makes the one on one bait safe for the general  mass as structure  the unit s centre does not fall even when sudou slams it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamada-albert-y1v5-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the wall in front of Ryuuen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.127<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yamada-albert\">Yamada Albert<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamada Albert is the half-Japanese horse protecting Ryuuen at the centre of Class C’s cavalry unit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> His strength is incredible, just like the rumors had said — equal to Sudou’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou cannot break him; Yamada and the other riders hold while Ryuuen conserves energy.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The body that makes the one-on-one bait safe for the general.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Mass as structure: the unit’s centre does not fall even when Sudou slams it.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamada-albert-y1v5-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the flag-breaker<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p128-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru totsuka-yahiko","q":"totsuka yahiko ch 6  6  passing mention named among the class d jockeys who lose their headbands in the last stand against ryuuen  part of the two against one that still cannot strip the treated headband  no separate dialogue on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p128-1\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.128<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named among the Class D jockeys who lose their headbands in the last stand against Ryuuen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Part of the two-against-one that still cannot strip the treated headband.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No separate dialogue on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v5-p107-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: shouting for Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 6  6  cutting the leader yukimura interjects while sudou demands the class follow him after the cavalry loss   is that really the case   it seems like you just want to show off how amazing you are   your emotions are completely out of control  and they re making all your decisions for you  cuts sudou s  trying my hardest for the class  claim  sudou tells him to shut up  then punches hirata instead  the academic who resents sudou s sports day power finally says the quiet part aloud   and nearly becomes the fist s target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html#sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1\">Ch.6 §6: cutting the leader<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.132<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura interjects while Sudou demands the class follow him after the cavalry loss.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Is that really the case?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “It seems like you just want to show off how amazing you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Your emotions are completely out of control, and they’re making all your decisions for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Cuts Sudou’s “trying my hardest for the class” claim; Sudou tells him to shut up, then punches Hirata instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The academic who resents Sudou’s sports-day power finally says the quiet part aloud — and nearly becomes the fist’s target.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: seventh and seventh<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6  6  the report she cannot prove chabashira approaches hirata on the ground after sudou s punch and reads the rage immediately   what s going on   did you hit him  sudou does not deny it    so what if i did  what then    so she has the answer she needed  accepts hirata s fall story only enough to log a preventative report  the pair are told to keep apart  and superiors will hear later   if the victim says that nothing happened  then there s no problem  she adds that she can tell something is going on  tells them to keep their distance from each other  and will give her superiors a report later as a preventative measure  detached  matter of fact  she knows the cover is thin and files it as prevention rather than discipline","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\">Ch.6 §6: the report she cannot prove<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.133<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira approaches Hirata on the ground after Sudou’s punch and reads the rage immediately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “What’s going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Did you hit him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “If the victim says that nothing happened, then there’s no problem.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou does not deny it — “So what if I did? What then?” — so she has the answer she needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Accepts Hirata’s fall story only enough to log a preventative report: the pair are told to keep apart, and superiors will hear later.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She adds that she can tell something is going on, tells them to keep their distance from each other, and will give her superiors a report later as a preventative measure.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Detached, matter-of-fact: she knows the cover is thin and files it as prevention rather than discipline.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Watches the homeroom from the back<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: relays Kinoshita’s accusation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 6  6  still absent with sudou gone  the page notes koenji was already absent   class d s two strongest both off the board  no new koenji action in the second half  the morning ends on his continued absence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1\">Ch.6 §6: still absent<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.134<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With Sudou gone, the page notes Kōenji was already absent — Class D’s two strongest both off the board.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No new Kōenji action in the second half; the morning ends on his continued absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the cottage refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6  6  passing mention horikita keeps staring at her brother during the upperclassmen s cavalry   someone she cannot approach  the distance is both social and physical while she is injured and the class is collapsing  the president does not act on or answer the look on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\">Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.135<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita keeps staring at her brother during the upperclassmen’s cavalry — someone she cannot approach.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The distance is both social and physical while she is injured and the class is collapsing.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The president does not act on or answer the look on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: first again<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.2: speaks to Suzune at the entrance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p140-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6  6  lunch detail yamauchi loses rock paper scissors and is sent to fetch the group s lunches   man  i m starving  i m gonna inhale this  shows no interest in sudou s whereabouts   same as ike  the three have known each other since day one  paired for lunch duty  both accept hirata s invitation to eat with the larger group","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p140-1\">Ch.6 §6: lunch detail<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.140–141<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi loses rock-paper-scissors and is sent to fetch the group’s lunches.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Man, I’m starving. I’m gonna inhale this!”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shows no interest in Sudou’s whereabouts — same as Ike; the three have known each other since day one.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Paired for lunch duty; both accept Hirata’s invitation to eat with the larger group.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: The Sakura defeat still stings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8: loses the sub draw<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  7  the beatdown already landed horikita walks to the nurse s office still stinging from ayanokouji s earlier speech  horikita admits he was absolutely right and she had no reply","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\">Ch.7 §7: the beatdown already landed<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita walks to the nurse’s office still stinging from Ayanokouji’s earlier speech.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita admits he was absolutely right and she had no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.7–6.10: observation, cavalry, and the plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.2: declines the search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p144-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nurse-unnamed kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7  alone after the beatdown horikita leaves ayanokouji s verbal beatdown for the school nurse alone  her leg still stiff from the obstacle fall   since he usually followed his so called policy of noninterference  i never would ve imagined he would speak to me like that   ayanokouji kun had been absolutely right  and i d had nothing to say in reply   no  that s not it   i already said this  but participating in more competitions will be difficult   i was planning to  but i think i ve changed my mind   that s a wise decision  a substitute for all three recommended events costs 300 000 points  her dream of running alongside her brother ends with the withdrawal  kushida runs up in a panic and says kinoshita is badly hurt and wants to talk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p144-1\">Ch.7 §7: alone after the beatdown<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.144–145<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita leaves Ayanokouji’s verbal beatdown for the school nurse alone, her leg still stiff from the obstacle fall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “No, that’s not it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">nurse-unnamed<\/b> “I already said this, but participating in more competitions will be difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I was planning to, but I think I’ve changed my mind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Since he usually followed his so-called policy of noninterference, I never would’ve imagined he would speak to me like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun had been absolutely right, and I’d had nothing to say in reply.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a wise decision.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> A substitute for all three recommended events costs 300,000 points; her dream of running alongside her brother ends with the withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida runs up in a panic and says Kinoshita is badly hurt and wants to talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: injury, cavalry, and the wake-up call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: the accusation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p145-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kinoshita-minori kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 7  7  fetches horikita  admits she told the teacher kushida runs up to horikita in a panic and leads her back to the nurse s office for kinoshita s accusation   i m so glad i found you  horikita san  i need to talk to you about something   would you mind coming with me  things are going to get difficult   it sounds as though kinoshita san actually suffered a serious injury   sorry  horikita san  kinoshita san asked me to talk to a teacher   i m good friends with kinoshita san  when i went to check on her during our break  she told me   she seems frightened  and might be emotionally unstable  claims friendship with kinoshita as the reason she heard the accusation first","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p145-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p145-1\">Ch.7 §7: fetches Horikita, admits she told the teacher<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.145–148<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida runs up to Horikita in a panic and leads her back to the nurse’s office for Kinoshita’s accusation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’m so glad I found you, Horikita-san! I need to talk to you about something,”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Would you mind coming with me? Things are going to get difficult,”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “It sounds as though Kinoshita-san actually suffered a serious injury.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, Horikita-san. Kinoshita-san asked me to talk to a teacher,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m good friends with Kinoshita-san. When I went to check on her during our break, she told me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She seems frightened, and might be emotionally unstable,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> Claims friendship with Kinoshita as the reason she heard the accusation first.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: compromise partner and searcher<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: defends Horikita, offers her points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7  7 1  relays kinoshita s accusation in the infirmary chabashira tells horikita that kinoshita claims she was knocked down deliberately   i had kushida fetch you  looks like she was quick about it   well  kinoshita says that you deliberately knocked her down  horikita   kinoshita claims that  during the race  you repeatedly looked back at her   even if that s true  though  she claims you kicked her   i believe you re innocent  but as long as we have no proof one way or the other  we must consider the matter  names the devil s proof and warns a foul play finding would invalidate scores and bar the recommended events   you haven t forgotten what happened to sudou after his fight  have you   under the circumstances  it would probably be easy for the school to believe that the incident was intentional rather than accidental   kinoshita won t accept that   her testimony  and the footage  make this fairly damning   kushida consulted me on the matter   okay  i ll let you try","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: relays Kinoshita’s accusation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.146–148<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the infirmary Chabashira tells Horikita that Kinoshita claims she was knocked down deliberately.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I had Kushida fetch you. Looks like she was quick about it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Well, Kinoshita says that you deliberately knocked her down, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Kinoshita claims that, during the race, you repeatedly looked back at her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if that’s true, though, she claims you kicked her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re innocent, but as long as we have no proof one way or the other, we must consider the matter,”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the Devil’s Proof and warns a foul-play finding would invalidate scores and bar the recommended events.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You haven’t forgotten what happened to Sudou after his fight, have you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Under the circumstances, it would probably be easy for the school to believe that the incident was intentional rather than accidental.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kinoshita won’t accept that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Her testimony, and the footage, make this fairly damning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida consulted me on the matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I’ll let you try,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p133-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the report she cannot prove<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: presses the look-back, objects to Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p146-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 1  the accusation back in the infirmary  chabashira opens the curtain on a sobbing kinoshita and says kinoshita claims horikita knocked her down deliberately   i had kushida fetch you  looks like she was quick about it   well  kinoshita says that you deliberately knocked her down  horikita   that s not true at all  it was completely by accident   kinoshita claims that  during the race  you repeatedly looked back at her   that s because she called my name   even if that s true  though  she claims you kicked her   even if she s badly injured  she s still lying  i didn t do anything   i believe you re innocent  but as long as we have no proof one way or the other  we must consider the matter   that s idiotic  proving foul play would invalidate her scores and bar the recommended events  chabashira names the devil s proof   it s a case of the devil s proof  isn t it   how did you hear about this  chabashira sensei  who else knows   sorry  horikita san  kinoshita san asked me to talk to a teacher  ryuuen arrives strutting  both hands in his pockets  and says things have gotten really serious","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p146-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: the accusation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.146–148<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back in the infirmary, Chabashira opens the curtain on a sobbing Kinoshita and says Kinoshita claims Horikita knocked her down deliberately.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I had Kushida fetch you. Looks like she was quick about it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Well, Kinoshita says that you deliberately knocked her down, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s not true at all. It was completely by accident.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kinoshita claims that, during the race, you repeatedly looked back at her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s because she called my name,”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if that’s true, though, she claims you kicked her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if she’s badly injured, she’s still lying. I didn’t do anything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re innocent, but as long as we have no proof one way or the other, we must consider the matter,”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s idiotic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Proving foul play would invalidate her scores and bar the recommended events; Chabashira names the Devil’s Proof.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s a case of the Devil’s Proof, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How did you hear about this, Chabashira-sensei? Who else knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, Horikita-san. Kinoshita-san asked me to talk to a teacher,”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryuuen arrives strutting, both hands in his pockets, and says things have gotten really serious.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7: alone after the beatdown<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: Kinoshita’s story and the denial<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p146-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kinoshita-minori","q":"kinoshita minori ch 7  7 1  the accusation from the bed behind the infirmary curtain kinoshita accuses horikita of knocking her down on purpose in the obstacle course  absent from all competitions after the obstacle course  teacher inspected injuries look severe   sorry  i tried my best  but my leg just won t listen   when i fell  you said that i definitely wouldn t win   i never called her name   i can t forgive horikita san for this  now i have to take a break from track and field practice  stands with ryuuen  he inspects her leg and speaks for the pair","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html#sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p146-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: the accusation from the bed<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.146–152<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Behind the infirmary curtain Kinoshita accuses Horikita of knocking her down on purpose in the obstacle course.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> “Sorry. I tried my best, but…my leg just won’t listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> “When I fell, you said…that I definitely wouldn’t win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> “I never called her name,”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Absent from all competitions after the obstacle course; teacher-inspected injuries look severe.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t forgive Horikita-san for this. Now I have to take a break from track and field practice,”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Stands with Ryuuen; he inspects her leg and speaks for the pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the name that caused the fall<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: refuses the apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 1  arrives at the infirmary ryuuen struts into the hallway and then the infirmary to inspect kinoshita s leg   looks like things have gotten really serious   i rushed over after kinoshita asked for me  to think someone did this on purpose   hey  kinoshita  you all right  looks like you ve had a rough time   whoa  this looks bad  i m impressed you ve held up  considering all you re dealing with","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: arrives at the infirmary<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.148–149<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen struts into the hallway and then the infirmary to inspect Kinoshita’s leg.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Looks like things have gotten really serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I rushed over after Kinoshita asked for me. To think someone did this on purpose…”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Hey, Kinoshita. You all right? Looks like you’ve had a rough time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whoa, this looks bad. I’m impressed you’ve held up, considering all you’re dealing with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the cavalry crown and the bait<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: builds the case, demands a million points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p149-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kinoshita-minori horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 1  kinoshita s story and the denial ryuuen inspects kinoshita s bandaged leg  then the three of them confront horikita in the hallway   hey  kinoshita  you all right  looks like you ve had a rough time   whoa  this looks bad  i m impressed you ve held up  considering all you re dealing with   sorry  i tried my best  but my leg just won t listen   don t blame yourself  kinoshita  i know you wanted to participate in the three legged race   we ran into each other by accident  kinoshita san  why are you saying that i made you fall   you really did this on purpose  didn t you   stop joking around  you think i d do something like this   when i fell  you said that i definitely wouldn t win   i said no such thing  why are you lying   because she kept calling my name when she was behind me   i never called her name   i can t forgive horikita san for this  now i have to take a break from track and field practice   don t you feel any shame at all   it s clear you did this  isn t it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p149-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: Kinoshita’s story and the denial<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.149–152<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen inspects Kinoshita’s bandaged leg, then the three of them confront Horikita in the hallway.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Hey, Kinoshita. You all right? Looks like you’ve had a rough time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Whoa, this looks bad. I’m impressed you’ve held up, considering all you’re dealing with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> “Sorry. I tried my best, but…my leg just won’t listen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t blame yourself, Kinoshita. I know you wanted to participate in the three-legged race,”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We ran into each other by accident, Kinoshita-san. Why are you saying that I made you fall?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really did this on purpose, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop joking around. You think I’d do something like this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When I fell, you said…that I definitely wouldn’t win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said no such thing. Why are you lying?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because she kept calling my name when she was behind me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never called her name,”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t forgive Horikita-san for this. Now I have to take a break from track and field practice,”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you feel any shame at all?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s clear you did this, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: the accusation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p153-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: the million-point deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7  7 1  presses the look back  objects to ryuuen chabashira presses horikita on why she looked back during the race  then tries to stop ryuuen s kneeling demand   horikita  you only looked behind you when you raced with kinoshita  why did you do that   is that true  kinoshita   ryuuen  this is going too far   you still have about twenty minutes  you haven t eaten yet  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: presses the look-back, objects to Ryuuen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.151–156<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira presses Horikita on why she looked back during the race, then tries to stop Ryuuen’s kneeling demand.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Horikita, you only looked behind you when you raced with Kinoshita. Why did you do that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Is that true, Kinoshita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Ryuuen. This is going too far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still have about twenty minutes. You haven’t eaten yet, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: relays Kinoshita’s accusation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: accepts Ayanokouji as substitute<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 1  builds the case  demands a million points ryuuen turns the collision into intent  then offers to withdraw the complaint for a million points   don t blame yourself  kinoshita  i know you wanted to participate in the three legged race   you really did this on purpose  didn t you   you can never really know someone  can you  convenient  isn t it   it s clear you did this  isn t it   i don t have the time to drag this out   we can strike a quick deal  though   you should compensate kinoshita and class c for any losses   if you hand over a million points  i ll have kinoshita withdraw her complaint   then go ahead and prove that  suzune  lay it all out in black and white for us   we can prove that we aren t lying  let s hurry up and have the student council president render his judgment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: builds the case, demands a million points<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.151–153<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen turns the collision into intent, then offers to withdraw the complaint for a million points.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Don’t blame yourself, Kinoshita. I know you wanted to participate in the three-legged race,”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You really did this on purpose, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You can never really know someone, can you? Convenient, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s clear you did this, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t have the time to drag this out,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can strike a quick deal, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should compensate Kinoshita and Class C for any losses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you hand over a million points, I’ll have Kinoshita withdraw her complaint.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then go ahead and prove that, Suzune. Lay it all out in black and white for us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can prove that we aren’t lying. Let’s hurry up and have the student council president render his judgment,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: arrives at the infirmary<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: the kneeling condition and the deadline<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p152-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 7  7 1  defends horikita  offers her points kushida speaks up quietly for horikita  then offers her own points when ryuuen demands payment   i think this is all just bad luck  i can t imagine that horikita san would deliberately hurt her opponent   don t you think your desire not to lose just got to you   would you let me talk things over a little more with horikita san  please   what exactly do you want  then   could i use my points  ryuuen kun   i don t believe horikita san would do something like this on purpose  ordered to bring suzune to ryuuen after the festival   are you okay  horikita san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p152-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: defends Horikita, offers her points<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.152–156<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida speaks up quietly for Horikita, then offers her own points when Ryuuen demands payment.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I think this is all just bad luck. I can’t imagine that Horikita-san would deliberately hurt her opponent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Don’t you think your desire not to lose just got to you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Would you let me talk things over a little more with Horikita-san, please?”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What exactly do you want, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could I use my points, Ryuuen-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t believe Horikita-san would do something like this on purpose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ordered to bring Suzune to Ryuuen after the festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay? Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p145-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7: fetches Horikita, admits she told the teacher<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: volunteers for the three-legged race<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p153-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 1  the million point deal ryuuen offers to drop the complaint for a million points  then adds a kneeling condition after horikita first refuses   would you let me talk things over a little more with horikita san  please   i don t have the time to drag this out   we can strike a quick deal  though   you should compensate kinoshita and class c for any losses   this isn t a joke  i don t have to listen to this   what exactly do you want  then   if you hand over a million points  i ll have kinoshita withdraw her complaint   don t be ridiculous   i haven t done anything wrong  i don t need to pay one single point   then go ahead and prove that  suzune  lay it all out in black and white for us   we can prove that we aren t lying  let s hurry up and have the student council president render his judgment   could i use my points  ryuuen kun   i don t believe horikita san would do something like this on purpose   oh  that s quaint  sorry using your points is a no go   very well  kinoshita  we re going to report this to the teachers  then to the student council   if i pay you  you ll make it so this issue never happened  right   you re admitting to foul play   no  because i m not a liar   your strategy beat mine  that s why  kinoshita answers  no  i can t    too short for a says row   how about you get down on your knees and beg   ryuuen  this is going too far   teachers should stay out of this  it s a problem between students   kushida  bring suzune to me after the festival  deadline  kneel and pay a million points after the festival  or let the school deliberate  kushida is to bring suzune   are you okay  horikita san   i m okay  more importantly  how long has it been  sensei  how much time is left for our lunch break   you still have about twenty minutes  you haven t eaten yet  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p153-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: the million-point deal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.153–156<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen offers to drop the complaint for a million points, then adds a kneeling condition after Horikita first refuses.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Would you let me talk things over a little more with Horikita-san, please?”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I don’t have the time to drag this out,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “We can strike a quick deal, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should compensate Kinoshita and Class C for any losses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t a joke. I don’t have to listen to this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What exactly do you want, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you hand over a million points, I’ll have Kinoshita withdraw her complaint.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be ridiculous,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I haven’t done anything wrong. I don’t need to pay one single point.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then go ahead and prove that, Suzune. Lay it all out in black and white for us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can prove that we aren’t lying. Let’s hurry up and have the student council president render his judgment,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could I use my points, Ryuuen-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t believe Horikita-san would do something like this on purpose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, that’s quaint. Sorry—using your points is a no-go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Very well. Kinoshita, we’re going to report this to the teachers, then to the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I pay you, you’ll make it so this issue never happened, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re admitting to foul play?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, because I’m not a liar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your strategy beat mine. That’s why,”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kinoshita answers “No, I can’t,” — too short for a says row.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about you get down on your knees and beg?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen. This is going too far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Teachers should stay out of this. It’s a problem between students,”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida, bring Suzune to me after the festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Deadline: kneel and pay a million points after the festival, or let the school deliberate; Kushida is to bring Suzune.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay? Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m okay. More importantly, how long has it been? Sensei, how much time is left for our lunch break?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still have about twenty minutes. You haven’t eaten yet, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p149-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: Kinoshita’s story and the denial<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p157-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.2: the brother and the search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 1  the kneeling condition and the deadline ryuuen refuses kushida s points  orders the report upward  then adds a kneeling demand after horikita agrees to pay   oh  that s quaint  sorry using your points is a no go   very well  kinoshita  we re going to report this to the teachers  then to the student council   you re admitting to foul play   did you hear that  kinoshita  she doesn t think she s in the wrong  can you forgive her   how about you get down on your knees and beg   teachers should stay out of this  it s a problem between students   kushida  bring suzune to me after the festival  provokes horikita by naming her brother  the student council president  as the judge  deadline after the festival  kneel and pay a million points  or let the school deliberate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: the kneeling condition and the deadline<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.154–156<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen refuses Kushida’s points, orders the report upward, then adds a kneeling demand after Horikita agrees to pay.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Oh, that’s quaint. Sorry—using your points is a no-go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Very well. Kinoshita, we’re going to report this to the teachers, then to the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “You’re admitting to foul play?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you hear that, Kinoshita? She doesn’t think she’s in the wrong. Can you forgive her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about you get down on your knees and beg?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Teachers should stay out of this. It’s a problem between students,”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida, bring Suzune to me after the festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Provokes Horikita by naming her brother, the student council president, as the judge.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Deadline after the festival: kneel and pay a million points, or let the school deliberate.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: builds the case, demands a million points<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8: checks on Sudou’s absence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p155-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kinoshita-minori","q":"kinoshita minori ch 7  7 1  refuses the apology asked whether she can forgive horikita after the strategy admission  kinoshita says no  kinoshita answers  no  i can t    too short for a says row  follows ryuuen out when he orders the report to teachers then the student council","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html#sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p155-1\">Ch.7 §7.1: refuses the apology<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.155<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Asked whether she can forgive Horikita after the strategy admission, Kinoshita says no.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kinoshita answers “No, I can’t,” — too short for a says row.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Follows Ryuuen out when he orders the report to teachers then the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kinoshita-minori-y1v5-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: the accusation from the bed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7  7 2  speaks to suzune at the entrance walking in with tachibana  manabu stops and asks his sister whether she understands class d s situation  student council president  tachibana  secretary  is with him   do you understand class d s situation right now  one line to his sister  then she says she will not bother him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\">Ch.7 §7.2: speaks to Suzune at the entrance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.157<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking in with Tachibana, Manabu stops and asks his sister whether she understands Class D’s situation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “Do you understand Class D’s situation right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Student council president; Tachibana, secretary, is with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> One line to his sister, then she says she will not bother him.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p135-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.3: named as the one she runs for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p157-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 2  the brother and the search on the way out horikita spots her brother  the student council president  with secretary tachibana  he speaks to her for the first time today   this was all due to my carelessness  i d only thought of myself   big brother  he asks whether she understands class d s situation   do you understand class d s situation right now   i m starting to   don t worry  i won t bother you  big brother  after the search fails she meets ayanokouji on the field and accepts sudou as an asset despite herself   you sound like you re out of breath   i m looking for sudou kun  he hasn t shown up  has he   yes  he s a valuable asset  i accept it  even though i don t like it   no  i don t  but there re only so many places he can go  if he wants privacy  he probably returned to his dorm room   is your leg all right   no  but i can run  are you coming   i ll pass  i d only end up getting in your way  lunch nearly over  sudou still missing  class d s defeat in the festival looking certain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p157-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p157-1\">Ch.7 §7.2: the brother and the search<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.157–158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the way out Horikita spots her brother, the student council president, with Secretary Tachibana; he speaks to her for the first time today.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “This was all due to my carelessness. I’d only thought of myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “Do you understand Class D’s situation right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m starting to,”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “Big brother…”; he asks whether she understands Class D’s situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I won’t bother you, big brother.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> After the search fails she meets Ayanokouji on the field and accepts Sudou as an asset despite herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You sound like you’re out of breath,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m looking for Sudou-kun. He hasn’t shown up, has he?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. He’s a valuable asset. I accept it, even though I don’t like it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t. But there’re only so many places he can go. If he wants privacy, he probably returned to his dorm room,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is your leg all right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, but I can run. Are you coming?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll pass. I’d only end up getting in your way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Lunch nearly over, Sudou still missing, Class D’s defeat in the festival looking certain.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p153-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: the million-point deal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.1: the dorm lobby with Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v5-p157-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"tachibana-akane","q":"tachibana akane ch 7  7 2  passing mention with the president tachibana walks in beside the student council president  she notices horikita  he does not glance her way   passing mention   p 157  named only as secretary tachibana with the president at the school entrance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v5-p157-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html#sc-tachibana-akane-y1v5-p157-1\">Ch.7 §7.2: passing mention with the president<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.157<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tachibana walks in beside the student council president; she notices Horikita, he does not glance her way. [passing mention] (p.157) Named only as Secretary Tachibana with the president at the school entrance.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  7 2  declines the search on the field after horikita s failed search  ayanokouji notes her breath and refuses to come along   you sound like you re out of breath   is your leg all right   i ll pass  i d only end up getting in your way  she treats sudou as an asset she accepts  he lets her go alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\">Ch.7 §7.2: declines the search<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the field after Horikita’s failed search, Ayanokouji notes her breath and refuses to come along.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You sound like you’re out of breath,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Is your leg all right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’ll pass. I’d only end up getting in your way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She treats Sudou as an asset she accepts; he lets her go alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7: the beatdown already landed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8: the scavenger hunt draws<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8  8  the scavenger hunt draws second half opens with ayanokouji stuck in the scavenger hunt after losing rock paper scissors  while sudou and horikita are both missing   you re participating in the scavenger hunt  right  ayanokouji kun   i d rather not  if possible   hirata  you don t need my opinion to make a sound decision  right   we need 100 000 points to put in a substitute  i ll figure something out with the points  i think we d do well substituting ike kun or yamauchi kun   that s because  if they do happen to take first place  they ll be able to put points toward their tests  right   so  that muscle headed moron won t be participating in the scavenger hunt  huh   no idea  that has nothing to do with me   ayanokouji  lend me your left foot  your left foot   my left foot   your shoe  dude  your shoe  that s my item   if i give it to you  i can t run anymore  though  ike takes first on a lucky draw  ayanokouji s own lots are  ten friends  then  a person you love  he redraws to a table clock and finishes last   i d like to request a change","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\">Ch.8 §8: the scavenger hunt draws<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.160–162<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second half opens with Ayanokouji stuck in the scavenger hunt after losing rock-paper-scissors, while Sudou and Horikita are both missing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “You’re participating in the scavenger hunt, right, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’d rather not, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hirata, you don’t need my opinion to make a sound decision, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need 100,000 points to put in a substitute. I’ll figure something out with the points. I think we’d do well substituting Ike-kun or Yamauchi-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s because, if they do happen to take first place, they’ll be able to put points toward their tests. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, that muscle-headed moron won’t be participating in the scavenger hunt, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No idea. That has nothing to do with me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji! Lend me your left foot! Your left foot!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My left foot?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your shoe, dude! Your shoe! That’s my item!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I give it to you, I can’t run anymore, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ike takes first on a lucky draw; Ayanokouji’s own lots are “Ten friends” then “A person you love”; he redraws to a table clock and finishes last.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to request a change.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.2: declines the search<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: the points crisis and Kushida<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p160-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 8  8  pays for substitutes hirata takes ayanokouji s opinion on a substitute and funds ike for the scavenger hunt   i think we need a substitute  in the individual competitions  our class ranks right at the bottom  to win in overall points  we need to win the next events   we need 100 000 points to put in a substitute  i ll figure something out with the points  i think we d do well substituting ike kun or yamauchi kun   yeah  we can use that to our advantage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p160-1\">Ch.8 §8: pays for substitutes<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.160–161<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata takes Ayanokouji’s opinion on a substitute and funds Ike for the scavenger hunt.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I think we need a substitute. In the individual competitions, our class ranks right at the bottom. To win in overall points, we need to win the next events,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “We need 100,000 points to put in a substitute. I’ll figure something out with the points. I think we’d do well substituting Ike-kun or Yamauchi-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yeah. We can use that to our advantage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: jockey, victim, cover<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p168-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: the 500,000-point burden<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p160-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji","q":"ike kanji ch 8  8  scavenger hunt substitute ike wins the rock paper scissors against yamauchi and takes sudou s scavenger hunt place   all right  i ll do my best  for sudou s sake   ayanokouji  lend me your left foot  your left foot   your shoe  dude  your shoe  that s my item   not bad  not bad at all  takes first place on a lucky draw despite not being the fastest runner   dude  why are you spacing out  hurry up  ayanokouji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p160-1\">Ch.8 §8: scavenger-hunt substitute<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.160–162<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike wins the rock-paper-scissors against Yamauchi and takes Sudou’s scavenger-hunt place.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “All right. I’ll do my best, for Sudou’s sake!”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Ayanokouji! Lend me your left foot! Your left foot!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Your shoe, dude! Your shoe! That’s my item!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not bad, not bad at all,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Takes first place on a lucky draw despite not being the fastest runner.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Dude, why are you spacing out? Hurry up, Ayanokouji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: carried, then lunch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p160-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 8  8  loses the sub draw yamauchi plays rock paper scissors with ike for the scavenger hunt substitute and loses   passing mention   p 160  named only as the other candidate hirata and ayanokouji consider for sudou s replacement  ike wins the draw","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p160-1\">Ch.8 §8: loses the sub draw<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.160<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi plays rock-paper-scissors with Ike for the scavenger-hunt substitute and loses. [passing mention] (p.160) Named only as the other candidate Hirata and Ayanokouji consider for Sudou’s replacement; Ike wins the draw.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v5-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: lunch detail<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 8  8  checks on sudou s absence ryuuen needles ayanokouji about sudou and horikita both being missing before the scavenger hunt   so  that muscle headed moron won t be participating in the scavenger hunt  huh  i thought he d take part for sure  suzune s not here  either  they couldn t be doing each other backstage  right   what a shitty answer  named by kushida as the man she gambled with on the vip scheme  she calls him a liar who entraps people  horikita tells sudou ryuuen has thoroughly beaten her and holds her points by blackmail","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1\">Ch.8 §8: checks on Sudou’s absence<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.161<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen needles Ayanokouji about Sudou and Horikita both being missing before the scavenger hunt.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “So, that muscle-headed moron won’t be participating in the scavenger hunt, huh? I thought he’d take part for sure. Suzune’s not here, either. They couldn’t be doing each other backstage, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “What a shitty answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named by Kushida as the man she gambled with on the VIP scheme; she calls him a liar who entraps people.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita tells Sudou Ryuuen has thoroughly beaten her and holds her points by blackmail.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: the kneeling condition and the deadline<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p163-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 8  8 1  the dorm lobby with sudou horikita finds sudou alone on a sofa in the dormitory lobby and refuses to leave until he comes back  sudou greets her with  horikita    too short for a says row   why are you here  don t tell me you came to persuade me to go back   do i look like the type to come all the way here to persuade you   if you stay out of the competitions  class d has no hope of winning   probably not  guess we re in a lot of trouble right now  huh   you may be a bit of a problem child  but you certainly gave it your all today   your weakness is completely obvious   if you don t like it  feel free to hit me   huh  what  you  there ain t no way i could do somethin  like that   maybe i just wanted to see how it felt for people to pay attention to me and give me some respect   you abandoned the class  though  just like me  right  so  you don t got any right to lecture me   no  i suppose not   i was born to worthless people  that s why i m worthless  too   it s incorrect to conclude that someone with worthless parents will inevitably turn out worthless themselves   fine  then just brand me worthless  already  go ahead  i don t even care anymore   go back  horikita   no  not unless i bring you with me   i ll wait here  forever  compares herself to sudou  ayanokouji destroyed her  ryuuen defeated her  her brother abandoned her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p163-1\">Ch.8 §8.1: the dorm lobby with Sudou<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.163–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita finds Sudou alone on a sofa in the dormitory lobby and refuses to leave until he comes back.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Why are you here? Don’t tell me you came to persuade me to go back?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Do I look like the type to come all the way here to persuade you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “If you stay out of the competitions, Class D has no hope of winning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou greets her with “Horikita.” — too short for a says row.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Probably not. Guess we’re in a lot of trouble right now, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You may be a bit of a problem child, but you certainly gave it your all today,”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your weakness is completely obvious,”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t like it, feel free to hit me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? What? You… There ain’t no way I could do somethin’ like that!”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe I just wanted to see how it felt for people to pay attention to me and give me some respect.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You abandoned the class, though, just like me. Right? So, you don’t got any right to lecture me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I suppose not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was born to worthless people. That’s why I’m worthless, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s incorrect to conclude that someone with worthless parents will inevitably turn out worthless themselves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. Then just brand me worthless, already. Go ahead. I don’t even care anymore,”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Go back, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. Not unless I bring you with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll wait here. Forever.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Compares herself to Sudou: Ayanokouji destroyed her, Ryuuen defeated her, her brother abandoned her.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p157-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.2: the brother and the search<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p176-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.3: the ally<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p163-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 8  8 1  the lobby lecture sudou sits alone on a dorm lobby sofa after walking out  he expects a scolding and gets horikita s honesty instead  sudou greets her with  horikita    too short for a says row   why are you here  don t tell me you came to persuade me to go back   probably not  guess we re in a lot of trouble right now  huh   and after i carried everyone on my back  that hirata  resents hirata for stopping the rampage  horikita says he should be grateful   you re seriously tryin  to preach to me  give me a break  horikita  i m really pissed  sudou snaps  shut up    too short for a says row   i took the leader job because i thought the sports festival would be easy as pie  i haven t lost to anyone from the other classes   maybe i just wanted to see how it felt for people to pay attention to me and give me some respect   i was born to worthless people  that s why i m worthless  too  blames worthless parents for turning out worthless  horikita rejects the hypothesis   fine  then just brand me worthless  already  go ahead  i don t even care anymore   go back  horikita   do what you want","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p163-1\">Ch.8 §8.1: the lobby lecture<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.163–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou sits alone on a dorm lobby sofa after walking out; he expects a scolding and gets Horikita’s honesty instead.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Why are you here? Don’t tell me you came to persuade me to go back?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Probably not. Guess we’re in a lot of trouble right now, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “And after I carried everyone on my back. That Hirata,”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou greets her with “Horikita.” — too short for a says row.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Resents Hirata for stopping the rampage; Horikita says he should be grateful.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re seriously tryin’ to preach to me? Give me a break, Horikita. I’m really pissed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou snaps “Shut up!” — too short for a says row.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I took the leader job because I thought the sports festival would be easy as pie. I haven’t lost to anyone from the other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe I just wanted to see how it felt for people to pay attention to me and give me some respect.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was born to worthless people. That’s why I’m worthless, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blames worthless parents for turning out worthless; Horikita rejects the hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. Then just brand me worthless, already. Go ahead. I don’t even care anymore,”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Go back, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do what you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: first place, bait, and the punch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p176-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.3: comes back for her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8  8 2  the points crisis and kushida after a lost four way tug of war  hirata has paid three substitutes  kushida volunteers for the three legged race and ayanokouji takes sudou s place   hirata  are you going to pay for the next competition  too   yeah  i am  we need it  hirata has paid twice for sudou and once for horikita  another substitute would push his total to 500 000 points   well  sudou aside  horikita should be able to repay you   hey  hirata  could i go in as sudou s substitute  i ll pay the points  i can t guarantee i ll be much help  but i ll try   so  you re going to be sudou s substitute  ayanokouji   rather unusual  since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines  ties him into the three legged pair  then he names her as the traitor who photographed the participation table   it s you  you re the traitor who leaked class d s participation table to class c   come on  ayanokouji kun  what s the matter with you  even as a joke  that s a cruel thing to say   i saw you  you took a picture with your phone of the participation table we drew on the blackboard   i suppose there s nothing i can do  now that i ve been found out  yes  i leaked the participation table   i wanted to expel her  expel horikita suzune  that s what   i m going to get horikita san expelled  no matter what you say  i won t change my mind   oh  but i reconsidered one thing  i added you to the list of people i want expelled  ayanokouji kun  open blackmail leverage  the uniform he touched on the cruise ship  she admits she gambled on ryuuen  three legged race run in silent hostility after the confession","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: the points crisis and Kushida<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.168–175<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After a lost four-way tug-of-war, Hirata has paid three substitutes; Kushida volunteers for the three-legged race and Ayanokouji takes Sudou’s place.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Hirata, are you going to pay for the next competition, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yeah, I am. We need it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, Sudou aside, Horikita should be able to repay you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Hirata has paid twice for Sudou and once for Horikita; another substitute would push his total to 500,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata. Could I go in as Sudou’s substitute? I’ll pay the points. I can’t guarantee I’ll be much help, but I’ll try,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’re going to be Sudou’s substitute, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Rather unusual, since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Ties him into the three-legged pair, then he names her as the traitor who photographed the participation table.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s you. You’re the traitor who leaked Class D’s participation table to Class C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, Ayanokouji-kun. What’s the matter with you? Even as a joke, that’s a cruel thing to say,”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I saw you. You took a picture with your phone of the participation table we drew on the blackboard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose there’s nothing I can do, now that I’ve been found out. Yes. I leaked the participation table,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to expel her. Expel Horikita Suzune. That’s what,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to get Horikita-san expelled, no matter what you say. I won’t change my mind,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, but I reconsidered one thing. I added you to the list of people I want expelled, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Open blackmail leverage: the uniform he touched on the cruise ship; she admits she gambled on Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Three-legged race run in silent hostility after the confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8: the scavenger hunt draws<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p168-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 8  8 2  the 500 000 point burden after the lost tug of war hirata has paid three times and faces a fourth  he still agrees because the class needs the points   yeah  i am  we need it   you might be right  but 100 000 points is a lot  and it s hard to save that many  also  i m the one who gave the go ahead to use substitutes  so i can t exactly go asking for points  sudou punched him earlier  hirata does not dwell on it and keeps paying   i suppose there s the class s victory to think about  but if we place well here  our winnings will give us an advantage on future tests   since you re pretty good at sports  kushida san  your offer is welcome   well  yeah  sure  i don t mind  of course  but are you okay with that  grants ayanokouji sudou s substitute place after kushida s offer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p168-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: the 500,000-point burden<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.168–169<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the lost tug-of-war Hirata has paid three times and faces a fourth; he still agrees because the class needs the points.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yeah, I am. We need it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “You might be right, but 100,000 points is a lot, and it’s hard to save that many. Also, I’m the one who gave the go-ahead to use substitutes, so I can’t exactly go asking for points,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I suppose there’s the class’s victory to think about, but if we place well here, our winnings will give us an advantage on future tests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou punched him earlier; Hirata does not dwell on it and keeps paying.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since you’re pretty good at sports, Kushida-san, your offer is welcome.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well… Yeah, sure. I don’t mind, of course, but…are you okay with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Grants Ayanokouji Sudou’s substitute place after Kushida’s offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v5-p160-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8: pays for substitutes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 8  8 2  accepts ayanokouji as substitute chabashira raises an eyebrow at ayanokouji volunteering for sudou s three legged place   so  you re going to be sudou s substitute  ayanokouji   rather unusual  since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines  notes his usual sideline habit while approving the entry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p169-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: accepts Ayanokouji as substitute<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.169<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira raises an eyebrow at Ayanokouji volunteering for Sudou’s three-legged place.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “So, you’re going to be Sudou’s substitute, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Rather unusual, since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes his usual sideline habit while approving the entry.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v5-p151-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: presses the look-back, objects to Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p169-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"shibata-sou ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 8  8 2  the class b three legged pair ichinose greets kushida and ayanokouji as fellow three legged competitors with shibata as her partner   yoo hoo  ayanokouji kun  oh  kikyou chan  too  looks like we re competing in the same group  huh   well  shibata kun might be tough  but i m really not all that special  you know  i haven t gotten first place in anything yet   i placed second one time  but i got fourth or fifth for all the rest of my events  to tell you the truth  someone else was supposed to participate in this three legged race  but i guess she sprained her ankle before lunch  quite a few people got injured this year  ties the cord with shibata for their race  class b pair cheerily readies against ayanokouji and kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p169-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: the Class B three-legged pair<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.169–170<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose greets Kushida and Ayanokouji as fellow three-legged competitors with Shibata as her partner.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Yoo-hoo! Ayanokouji-kun! Oh, Kikyou-chan, too. Looks like we’re competing in the same group, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Well, Shibata-kun might be tough, but I’m really not all that special, you know? I haven’t gotten first place in anything yet,”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I placed second one time, but I got fourth or fifth for all the rest of my events. To tell you the truth, someone else was supposed to participate in this three-legged race, but I guess she sprained her ankle before lunch. Quite…”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I placed second one time, but I got fourth or fifth for all the rest of my events. To tell you the truth, someone else was supposed to participate in this three-legged race, but I guess she sprained her ankle before lunch. Quite a few people got injured this year,”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Ties the cord with Shibata for their race.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Class B pair cheerily readies against Ayanokouji and Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v5-p119-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: fair play under the smile<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p169-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 8  8 2  volunteers for the three legged race kushida offers to pay for horikita s three legged place so hirata is not left holding the bill alone   um  hirata kun  would you mind if i helped  too  i d like to participate in the three legged race  of course  i ll pay the points for it  is that okay   i can t let you bear this burden alone  besides  i want to try my best for the class  and for horikita san and sudou kun s sake   thank you  i ll go tell chabashira sensei that i ll participate in horikita san s place  then   you re taking sudou kun s place  then  ayanokouji kun  i m looking forward to racing with you   in the three legged race  coordination s more important than simple speed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p169-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: volunteers for the three-legged race<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.169<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida offers to pay for Horikita’s three-legged place so Hirata is not left holding the bill alone.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Um, Hirata-kun, would you mind if I helped, too? I’d like to participate in the three-legged race. Of course, I’ll pay the points for it. Is that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I can’t let you bear this burden alone. Besides, I want to try my best for the class, and for Horikita-san and Sudou-kun’s sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Thank you. I’ll go tell Chabashira-sensei that I’ll participate in Horikita-san’s place, then,”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re taking Sudou-kun’s place, then, Ayanokouji-kun? I’m looking forward to racing with you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the three-legged race, coordination’s more important than simple speed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: defends Horikita, offers her points<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p172-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8.2: named as the traitor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p169-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami shibata-sou","q":"shibata so ch 8  8 2  ichinose s three legged partner shibata walks up with ichinose as her three legged race partner   passing mention   p 169  named only as ichinose s partner beside her when the class b pair approaches  shibata answers  okay    too short for a says row  agrees that she can tie their legs now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html#sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p169-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: Ichinose’s three-legged partner<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.169–170<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Shibata walks up with Ichinose as her three-legged-race partner. [passing mention] (p.169) Named only as Ichinose’s partner beside her when the Class B pair approaches.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Shibata answers “Okay.” — too short for a says row.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Agrees that she can tie their legs now.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shibata-sou-y1v5-p124-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: cavalry horse under a Class B general<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p172-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 8  8 2  named as the traitor while tying their legs together  ayanokouji names kushida as the leaker of the participation table  she admits it and states her goal   come on  ayanokouji kun  what s the matter with you  even as a joke  that s a cruel thing to say   i did that to record the information  so i would remember   hey  ayanokouji kun  assuming that i am responsible for leaking class d s information  if my taking a picture led you to determine that  it must mean you knew the participation table was leaked  right   i understand what you re getting at  but i m not the culprit  okay  i don t want to suspect any of my classmates  either   hee hee  you really aren t an ordinary person  are you  ayanokouji kun   i suppose there s nothing i can do  now that i ve been found out  yes  i leaked the participation table   i wanted to expel her  expel horikita suzune  that s what   i m going to get horikita san expelled  no matter what you say  i won t change my mind   that s right  i don t care if i never make it to class a  if it means horikita san gets expelled  oh  but don t misunderstand me once she s gone  i ll unite everyone  and we ll work toward reaching class a together  i promise   oh  but i reconsidered one thing  i added you to the list of people i want expelled  ayanokouji kun   i m not an idiot  i obviously wouldn t do anything that left any evidence behind  ryuuen kun is a liar who entraps people without batting an eyelash  well  i gambled on whether or not he would betray me  admits she used ryuuen on the cruise ship vip scheme and gambled on his silence  goal unchanged  expel horikita first  then unite the class for class a  smile returns  the three legged race runs in silent hostility","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p172-1\">Ch.8 §8.2: named as the traitor<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.172–175<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">While tying their legs together, Ayanokouji names Kushida as the leaker of the participation table; she admits it and states her goal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Come on, Ayanokouji-kun. What’s the matter with you? Even as a joke, that’s a cruel thing to say,”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I did that to record the information, so I would remember.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Hey, Ayanokouji-kun. Assuming that I am responsible for leaking Class D’s information… If my taking a picture led you to determine that, it must mean you knew the participation table was leaked, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what you’re getting at, but I’m not the culprit, okay? I don’t want to suspect any of my classmates, either,”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hee hee. You really aren’t an ordinary person, are you, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose there’s nothing I can do, now that I’ve been found out. Yes. I leaked the participation table,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to expel her. Expel Horikita Suzune. That’s what,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to get Horikita-san expelled, no matter what you say. I won’t change my mind,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. I don’t care if I never make it to Class A, if it means Horikita-san gets expelled. Oh, but don’t misunderstand me—once she’s gone, I’ll unite everyone, and we’ll work toward reaching Class A together. I promise,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, but I reconsidered one thing. I added you to the list of people I want expelled, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not an idiot. I obviously wouldn’t do anything that left any evidence behind. Ryuuen-kun is a liar who entraps people without batting an eyelash. Well, I gambled on whether or not he would betray me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Admits she used Ryuuen on the cruise-ship VIP scheme and gambled on his silence.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Goal unchanged: expel Horikita first, then unite the class for Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Smile returns; the three-legged race runs in silent hostility.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v5-p169-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8.2: volunteers for the three-legged race<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p176-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 8  8 3  the ally after an hour at the elevator  sudou returns  horikita admits she is worthless and asks for his strength until graduation   did did you seriously wait around here   you came back  sudou kun   nope  i just came down here to see if you were still hanging around  is all   i concluded that you and i really are similar after all   we ain t got anythin  in common  you and i are way too different   no  we re very similar  the more i think about it  the more i see that it s true   he s my older brother   that s why i ve been running straight ahead  not caring what anyone else thinks of me   i m not incredible  ryuuen kun s thoroughly beaten me  and i haven t gotten one single result i m satisfied with  either   if there s a difference between you and i  that might be it  i will never  ever give up  i ll strive to become someone worthy of my brother s admiration   that sounds like a painful path to take   if you ever stray from your path in future  i ll bring you back to it  so  until we graduate  please lend me your strength  i promise that i ll lend you all mine  too   i ll ask you again  sudou kun  lend me your strength   i ll work with you  horikita  i i feel like someone s finally noticed me outside basketball  first ally  not ayanokouji  not her brother   something she had lacked  small first step  she smiles for the first time in the chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p176-1\">Ch.8 §8.3: the ally<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.176–179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After an hour at the elevator, Sudou returns; Horikita admits she is worthless and asks for his strength until graduation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Did…did you seriously wait around here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You came back, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Nope. I just came down here to see if you were still hanging around, is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I concluded that you and I really are similar after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We ain’t got anythin’ in common. You and I are way too different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. We’re very similar. The more I think about it, the more I see that it’s true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s my older brother.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why I’ve been running straight ahead, not caring what anyone else thinks of me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not incredible. Ryuuen-kun’s thoroughly beaten me, and I haven’t gotten one single result I’m satisfied with, either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s a difference between you and I, that might be it. I will never, ever give up. I’ll strive to become someone worthy of my brother’s admiration,”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That sounds like a painful path to take.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you ever stray from your path in future, I’ll bring you back to it. So, until we graduate, please lend me your strength. I promise that I’ll lend you all mine, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll ask you again, Sudou-kun. Lend me your strength.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll work with you, Horikita. I…I feel like someone’s finally noticed me outside basketball.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> First ally: not Ayanokouji, not her brother — something she had lacked.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Small first step; she smiles for the first time in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8.1: the dorm lobby with Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p176-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 8  8 3  comes back for her an hour later sudou returns only to see if she is still at the elevator  then agrees to work with her until graduation   did did you seriously wait around here   it s already over  isn t it  the sports festival  i mean   nope  i just came down here to see if you were still hanging around  is all   we ain t got anythin  in common  you and i are way too different   yeah  that prim and proper guy  names the president as prim and proper before learning he is her brother   oh  so  wait  you said something about fighting with him  right   you re not givin  up   that sounds like a painful path to take   ah  what the hell am i feelin  right now  i don t get it  but it s like  i feel like i ve finally had my eyes opened   i ll work with you  horikita  i i feel like someone s finally noticed me outside basketball  accepts her as an ally  first time anyone outside basketball has noticed him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p176-1\">Ch.8 §8.3: comes back for her<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.176–179<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">An hour later Sudou returns only to see if she is still at the elevator, then agrees to work with her until graduation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Did…did you seriously wait around here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “It’s already over, isn’t it? The sports festival, I mean.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Nope. I just came down here to see if you were still hanging around, is all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We ain’t got anythin’ in common. You and I are way too different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, that prim-and-proper guy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Names the president as prim-and-proper before learning he is her brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? So… Wait. You said something about fighting with him, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re not givin’ up?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That sounds like a painful path to take.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. What the hell am I feelin’ right now?! I don’t get it, but it’s like… I feel like I’ve finally had my eyes opened.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll work with you, Horikita. I…I feel like someone’s finally noticed me outside basketball.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts her as an ally; first time anyone outside basketball has noticed him.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v5-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8.1: the lobby lecture<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 8  8 3  named as the one she runs for horikita tells sudou the prim and proper president is her older brother and why she chases his regard   he s my older brother  far from good because she lacks talent  she chases class a for his respect   that s why i ve been running straight ahead  not caring what anyone else thinks of me  sudou learns the connection only here  after calling the president prim and proper","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p178-1\">Ch.8 §8.3: named as the one she runs for<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.178<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita tells Sudou the prim-and-proper president is her older brother and why she chases his regard.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “That’s why I’ve been running straight ahead, not caring what anyone else thinks of me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “He’s my older brother.”; far from good because she lacks talent; she chases Class A for his respect.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou learns the connection only here, after calling the president prim-and-proper.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v5-p157-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.2: speaks to Suzune at the entrance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
